1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:03,807
(D-11 until the Shujitsu match)

2
00:00:04,307 --> 00:00:05,306
(Gasps)

3
00:00:05,307 --> 00:00:06,470
What is all this?

4
00:00:07,807 --> 00:00:09,343
- Has it always been like this?
- No way!

5
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:13,540
- Hey!
- Unbelievable.

6
00:00:15,273 --> 00:00:19,273
(The training camp
even has its own gym...)

7
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,973
(and a treatment room for immediate care.)

8
00:00:25,907 --> 00:00:29,573
(All the players have moved in.)

9
00:00:30,173 --> 00:00:31,372
Can everyone see clearly?

10
00:00:31,373 --> 00:00:32,351
- Yes.
- Yes.

11
00:00:32,376 --> 00:00:33,033
Good.

12
00:00:33,507 --> 00:00:35,072
Let's get started.

13
00:00:35,073 --> 00:00:39,073
First, I want to talk
about our goal for this season.

14
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,273
Our goal is...

15
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:44,906
to win every single match.

16
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:46,606
I want everyone to keep that in mind.

17
00:00:46,607 --> 00:00:49,239
Starting today,
your only focus is training.

18
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:50,884
Let's give it everything we've got.

19
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:54,473
If we can show real improvement,

20
00:00:54,807 --> 00:00:56,645
won't corporate sponsors start thinking,

21
00:00:56,669 --> 00:01:01,073
"Maybe we should turn
the Wonder Dogs into a pro team?"

22
00:01:01,773 --> 00:01:04,673
That's why winning every match
matters most.

23
00:01:05,207 --> 00:01:06,473
I knew this was coming.

24
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,202
I think I'm starting to get
a little ambitious myself.

25
00:01:09,373 --> 00:01:12,573
Coach set the bar even higher
than in Season One.

26
00:01:13,207 --> 00:01:17,140
For now, think of it
as mostly the same as last year.

27
00:01:17,773 --> 00:01:21,107
Our system volleyball will look
similar to last season.

28
00:01:21,473 --> 00:01:22,972
Remember the game plan we put together?

29
00:01:22,973 --> 00:01:24,885
Just tip it like that.

30
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:27,440
(The coordinated plays drilled
relentlessly in Season 1)

31
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:30,772
(A game played strictly by the book)

32
00:01:30,773 --> 00:01:33,006
You need to know these signals
inside and out.

33
00:01:33,007 --> 00:01:34,772
Knowing all of this is the bare minimum.

34
00:01:34,773 --> 00:01:36,840
(Signals for blocking, defense,
and setting)

35
00:01:37,107 --> 00:01:39,040
(Everything goes according to plan.)

36
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:42,207
(Yeon Koung's "system volleyball")

37
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:46,106
Last season, we focused
on laying down the overall system.

38
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:49,773
This time, we're dialing
into the finer details.

39
00:01:50,173 --> 00:01:51,839
Let's start with setters.

40
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:54,972
Positioning is crucial today,
especially for blocks,

41
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:56,950
so let's walk through it first
before we run drills. Got it?

42
00:01:56,975 --> 00:01:57,909
- Yes.
- Yes.

43
00:01:58,307 --> 00:01:59,872
(Morning)

44
00:01:59,873 --> 00:02:02,873
(Position-specific training)

45
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:15,006
We've split the coaching staff
by position,

46
00:02:15,007 --> 00:02:17,404
so each coach can work closely
with the players...

47
00:02:17,429 --> 00:02:19,973
and drill down
into position-specific details.

48
00:02:20,507 --> 00:02:23,007
(Afternoon: Team training)

49
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,972
(Double the training volume
of last season)

50
00:02:26,973 --> 00:02:30,407
We've mapped out targeted drills
for every position,

51
00:02:30,432 --> 00:02:32,632
so we'll be able to prepare...

52
00:02:32,873 --> 00:02:35,140
far more systematically.

53
00:02:35,973 --> 00:02:38,673
Bring in the setting basket.

54
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,773
Bring out the basket, please.

55
00:02:41,473 --> 00:02:42,663
Pull this strap a little tighter.

56
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:47,607
(The training gear gets an upgrade too...)

57
00:02:47,807 --> 00:02:50,573
(to handle the heavier workload.)

58
00:02:56,907 --> 00:02:59,640
Compared to Season One, you can tell...

59
00:02:59,873 --> 00:03:03,140
I've really turned up the heat
before our first match, right?

60
00:03:03,407 --> 00:03:04,785
You can feel the difference, can't you?

61
00:03:05,273 --> 00:03:08,206
(And that's not all.)

62
00:03:08,207 --> 00:03:10,641
(Every match is broken down thoroughly...)

63
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:12,940
(through data-driven analysis.)

64
00:03:13,707 --> 00:03:17,330
I've been in close contact
with foreign coaches,

65
00:03:17,355 --> 00:03:19,006
exchanging materials and insights.

66
00:03:19,007 --> 00:03:21,606
We've been looking at key stats.

67
00:03:21,607 --> 00:03:22,772
The approach itself...

68
00:03:22,773 --> 00:03:24,239
Things like running quick sets...

69
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,339
When someone else has to take
the second ball, like this...

70
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,106
We call that setting
along the same vector.

71
00:03:28,107 --> 00:03:29,806
A double substitution is...

72
00:03:29,807 --> 00:03:32,606
You swap the setter and opposite to rotate
front-row and back-row hitting power.

73
00:03:32,607 --> 00:03:33,639
Understood?

74
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,716
And we talked about this too.
When you close in...

75
00:03:36,273 --> 00:03:37,207
- Got it?
- When we close in?

76
00:03:37,573 --> 00:03:39,806
If you move like this, push it forward.

77
00:03:39,807 --> 00:03:41,439
If you move like this, send it behind you.

78
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:43,506
Keep it tight.

79
00:03:43,507 --> 00:03:44,539
(Staring)

80
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,626
Like you actually get what I'm explaining.

81
00:03:48,173 --> 00:03:50,707
We're pulling an all-nighter today.
We stay until everyone gets it.

82
00:03:51,173 --> 00:03:52,839
Keep your hands out front.

83
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,173
Keep your hands out front.

84
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,673
That's it.
Keep your hands in front of you.

85
00:03:57,073 --> 00:03:59,372
(The coach won't let up
until it's flawless.)

86
00:03:59,373 --> 00:04:02,739
Too late!

87
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,873
Watch your footwork!

88
00:04:04,573 --> 00:04:05,739
Too late!

89
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:11,239
Cover!

90
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,740
Where's the cover?

91
00:04:13,373 --> 00:04:15,839
If you cut it like that,
it's basically just a tip.

92
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,239
Look at it this way first.

93
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,739
This angle gives you better leverage,
so keep your body squared like this.

94
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,093
Then swing through and drive it down.

95
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:23,340
(Her intensity is off the charts.)

96
00:04:24,407 --> 00:04:26,840
(Completely overwhelmed)

97
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,772
(Speechless)

98
00:04:29,773 --> 00:04:31,805
We're dialing in the timing,
so keep at it.

99
00:04:32,404 --> 00:04:34,603
(Didn't you say
there wouldn't be a Season 2?)

100
00:04:34,604 --> 00:04:37,970
I did say I wouldn't do a Season Two,

101
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:41,469
but I was already sketching
out ideas in my head.

102
00:04:41,470 --> 00:04:45,018
You never stop learning.

103
00:04:45,270 --> 00:04:49,637
Honestly, I feel much more confident now
than I did in Season One.

104
00:04:50,637 --> 00:04:51,703
Let's stay focused and get to work.

105
00:04:51,704 --> 00:04:53,404
(D-10 until the Shujitsu match)

106
00:04:53,737 --> 00:04:56,470
We're using both sides of the court.

107
00:04:57,137 --> 00:04:59,603
Hyo Hee, can you clock this
with the stopwatch?

108
00:04:59,604 --> 00:05:00,503
I've got the timer.

109
00:05:00,504 --> 00:05:01,903
- She wants us to clock it.
- On it.

110
00:05:01,904 --> 00:05:03,003
I'll start timing from here.

111
00:05:11,404 --> 00:05:12,970
Good. Nice set!

112
00:05:14,570 --> 00:05:15,569
Hey!

113
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:16,469
- That's the one!
- Nice!

114
00:05:16,470 --> 00:05:17,836
That's a solid time.

115
00:05:17,837 --> 00:05:18,703
Right there.

116
00:05:18,704 --> 00:05:20,604
(Why are they clocking plays
with a stopwatch?)

117
00:05:20,870 --> 00:05:27,037
In Season One, we relied heavily
on Pyo Seung Ju as our go-to hitter.

118
00:05:28,204 --> 00:05:30,904
(Seung Ju isn't playing?)

119
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:34,370
Then we'll definitely beat them.

120
00:05:34,937 --> 00:05:37,703
So this time around,
we're hyper-focused on precision.

121
00:05:37,704 --> 00:05:41,103
Without a dominant go-to hitter
this season,

122
00:05:41,104 --> 00:05:43,536
our strategy is to run
a high-tempo offense...

123
00:05:43,537 --> 00:05:48,384
and strike before the opposing block
has time to set up.

124
00:05:48,409 --> 00:05:50,070
(Fast-tempo volleyball means
speeding up the attack.)

125
00:05:51,637 --> 00:05:53,103
Go immediately.

126
00:05:53,104 --> 00:05:55,169
(A quick set from the setter)

127
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:56,137
Right on target.

128
00:05:56,504 --> 00:05:59,503
Ultimately, our goal is
to execute the attack...

129
00:05:59,504 --> 00:06:04,631
in under one second
from setter contact to hit.

130
00:06:08,004 --> 00:06:09,303
- Go!
- Nice.

131
00:06:09,304 --> 00:06:11,770
Good pace.

132
00:06:12,737 --> 00:06:14,337
Great job, Chae Rim.

133
00:06:15,537 --> 00:06:16,337
Hey.

134
00:06:17,904 --> 00:06:19,670
- Nice.
- Great hit!

135
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:24,037
Nice!

136
00:06:24,946 --> 00:06:26,845
Good ball, Song Hee. Clean hit!

137
00:06:26,870 --> 00:06:27,770
(Nailed it!)

138
00:06:29,270 --> 00:06:30,637
It's 0.79. Great time.

139
00:06:32,437 --> 00:06:33,704
Nice. 0.84.

140
00:06:35,870 --> 00:06:37,704
- Flat one second.
- One second works.

141
00:06:38,804 --> 00:06:40,837
They're picking it up faster
than I expected.

142
00:06:42,704 --> 00:06:45,570
(Looking sharp)

143
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:53,304
Too slow.

144
00:06:54,304 --> 00:06:56,404
You're late on the approach, Young In.

145
00:06:56,670 --> 00:06:58,470
- Young In, too late.
- Understood!

146
00:07:00,037 --> 00:07:01,004
Lock in the timing.

147
00:07:07,155 --> 00:07:08,081
(Hesitates)

148
00:07:08,106 --> 00:07:09,204
What are you doing?

149
00:07:10,337 --> 00:07:11,337
Go for the spike.

150
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:13,937
Young In!

151
00:07:14,437 --> 00:07:16,745
The whole reason we start our approach
from back here...

152
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,236
is to explode in when the pass
is off the net, right?

153
00:07:19,237 --> 00:07:20,736
- Get in there faster.
- Yes, Coach!

154
00:07:20,737 --> 00:07:22,804
Your timing is consistently late.

155
00:07:27,870 --> 00:07:29,804
Mine! Cover!

156
00:07:30,237 --> 00:07:31,069
Cover!

157
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,504
- No, reset.
- Come on.

158
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:34,529
(The attack stalls...)

159
00:07:34,553 --> 00:07:37,037
(because she broke her approach
from outside the mark.)

160
00:07:37,770 --> 00:07:38,737
Young In.

161
00:07:39,437 --> 00:07:40,969
- The set came up short earlier, remember?
- Right.

162
00:07:40,994 --> 00:07:43,730
How far back did you drift?
You ended up right by Coach Sang Hwa.

163
00:07:44,054 --> 00:07:46,100
How are you going to hit
from the outside out there?

164
00:07:46,124 --> 00:07:46,687
Got it!

165
00:07:46,688 --> 00:07:48,520
Drop straight back, not diagonally.

166
00:07:48,521 --> 00:07:49,135
Yes!

167
00:07:49,419 --> 00:07:51,438
You'll never clear the net like that.

168
00:07:57,086 --> 00:07:59,486
Everyone else is clicking,
but Young In is...

169
00:07:59,952 --> 00:08:01,286
missing a beat.

170
00:08:01,552 --> 00:08:03,586
Something feels off with her.

171
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,719
As for Young In,

172
00:08:08,986 --> 00:08:14,536
she didn't seem to be
in the same form as last year.

173
00:08:15,986 --> 00:08:18,118
(Practicing serves)

174
00:08:18,119 --> 00:08:19,119
That's 52.

175
00:08:19,619 --> 00:08:21,468
Why can't you clear the net, Young In?

176
00:08:22,198 --> 00:08:23,136
Why?

177
00:08:23,578 --> 00:08:25,311
Is something wrong with your shoulder?

178
00:08:25,815 --> 00:08:27,140
What kind of serve was that?

179
00:08:31,521 --> 00:08:32,712
Put some drive into it.

180
00:08:34,481 --> 00:08:36,648
(Come on.)

181
00:08:36,739 --> 00:08:38,084
Hold up. Hey!

182
00:08:38,772 --> 00:08:39,719
Hey!

183
00:08:40,605 --> 00:08:42,204
Where were you aiming?

184
00:08:42,205 --> 00:08:43,205
Where?

185
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,439
The middle.

186
00:08:44,605 --> 00:08:46,026
- The middle?
- Down the line.

187
00:08:46,072 --> 00:08:48,061
- Right at Chae Rim.
- Why are you changing your answer?

188
00:08:48,205 --> 00:08:49,571
You need to know...

189
00:08:49,572 --> 00:08:51,938
whether you got stuffed
going down the line or cross-court.

190
00:08:51,939 --> 00:08:54,172
You're just swinging blindly!
I told you to keep your eyes open.

191
00:08:54,905 --> 00:08:55,905
Understood.

192
00:08:59,905 --> 00:09:01,638
For me,

193
00:09:01,639 --> 00:09:04,772
it's hard to keep up with this tempo.

194
00:09:05,305 --> 00:09:07,539
My timing on attacks is off,

195
00:09:08,039 --> 00:09:10,971
and I haven't settled into the pace,
so it feels overwhelming.

196
00:09:10,972 --> 00:09:12,372
(Young In struggles to find her rhythm.)

197
00:09:14,905 --> 00:09:17,605
We just need Young In to pick it up.

198
00:09:18,939 --> 00:09:20,238
She isn't quite there yet.

199
00:09:20,239 --> 00:09:21,805
(Worried about Young In)

200
00:09:24,239 --> 00:09:25,339
Side out.

201
00:09:27,172 --> 00:09:29,638
I believed she had more in her.

202
00:09:29,639 --> 00:09:32,904
I had complete faith in her,

203
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:36,171
so seeing her struggle hit hard.

204
00:09:36,172 --> 00:09:37,805
That worried me a lot.

205
00:09:38,739 --> 00:09:42,805
I realized things weren't going
according to plan.

206
00:09:45,005 --> 00:09:46,139
- Watch your steps.
- Hey!

207
00:09:46,814 --> 00:09:47,788
Set it up.

208
00:09:51,239 --> 00:09:52,272
What happened?

209
00:09:52,905 --> 00:09:53,939
What's wrong?

210
00:09:54,705 --> 00:09:55,739
Are you okay?

211
00:09:56,772 --> 00:09:57,772
Gosh.

212
00:09:58,205 --> 00:09:59,238
What happened?

213
00:09:59,239 --> 00:10:00,304
(Young In goes down.)

214
00:10:00,305 --> 00:10:01,339
My ankle!

215
00:10:05,305 --> 00:10:06,472
- Let's get her up.
- Did she twist it?

216
00:10:07,572 --> 00:10:09,138
- She landed on it funny and rolled it.
- Help her off the court.

217
00:10:09,139 --> 00:10:10,205
Easy, let's go.

218
00:10:12,339 --> 00:10:14,471
Let her lean on your shoulder.
Help her up.

219
00:10:14,472 --> 00:10:16,139
Put your arm around her.

220
00:10:16,472 --> 00:10:17,248
Hold on.

221
00:10:17,273 --> 00:10:19,180
(Taken off the court
to prevent further injury)

222
00:10:19,205 --> 00:10:20,487
Did she step on your foot?

223
00:10:21,139 --> 00:10:22,288
Not sure yet.

224
00:10:28,139 --> 00:10:30,472
- It took a pretty bad turn.
- Really?

225
00:10:37,039 --> 00:10:38,971
Young In should be all right.

226
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,005
- Really?
- Yes.

227
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:43,038
We'll check on her again tomorrow morning
and give an update.

228
00:10:43,039 --> 00:10:44,038
I'll leave the wrap on for now.

229
00:10:44,039 --> 00:10:45,339
(No structural damage suspected)

230
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:46,880
Please take good care of her.

231
00:10:48,539 --> 00:10:51,505
Whenever a player goes down injured,

232
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:56,304
I always feel responsible.

233
00:10:56,305 --> 00:10:58,139
It shook me up, but...

234
00:10:58,639 --> 00:11:01,971
I had to pull myself together...

235
00:11:01,972 --> 00:11:06,505
and quickly figure out our next move.

236
00:11:08,272 --> 00:11:10,938
The problem is, Young In went down.

237
00:11:10,939 --> 00:11:12,872
And our depth at opposite hitter is thin.

238
00:11:14,105 --> 00:11:15,838
We're in a tough spot.

239
00:11:15,839 --> 00:11:16,872
(Time is running out.)

240
00:11:18,872 --> 00:11:21,171
No use overthinking it.
We just have to make a move.

241
00:11:21,172 --> 00:11:23,072
(Time to make a call)

242
00:11:27,992 --> 00:11:31,525
(D-5 until the Shujitsu match)

243
00:11:33,758 --> 00:11:39,423
(A figure walks onto the quiet court)

244
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:41,782
(Let's soar, Wonder Dogs!)

245
00:11:46,239 --> 00:11:47,871
Good morning.

246
00:11:47,872 --> 00:11:50,572
(Coach Sang Hwa arrives on time as usual.)

247
00:11:51,705 --> 00:11:52,805
Jjing-jjing!

248
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:57,105
(Clearly great friends)

249
00:11:57,439 --> 00:11:59,118
How are your knees feeling?

250
00:11:59,143 --> 00:12:00,620
They're holding up fine.

251
00:12:01,605 --> 00:12:05,005
Though I haven't served a ball
in three months.

252
00:12:05,272 --> 00:12:06,759
My whole shoulder is tight.

253
00:12:07,191 --> 00:12:08,215
(Laughing)

254
00:12:14,513 --> 00:12:17,812
(The squad trickles in one by one.)

255
00:12:17,813 --> 00:12:18,738
Wait.

256
00:12:20,046 --> 00:12:21,374
Someone's already here.

257
00:12:21,913 --> 00:12:23,346
Over there.

258
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,980
- Who is that?
- No clue.

259
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,746
Morning, Yeon Joo.

260
00:12:30,046 --> 00:12:31,079
Morning.

261
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,620
- Hello!
- Good morning!

262
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:34,926
There's one more thing.

263
00:12:34,927 --> 00:12:36,960
(A twist hinted at
during the launch ceremony)

264
00:12:37,034 --> 00:12:38,124
This season,

265
00:12:38,552 --> 00:12:41,234
we're introducing an open roster system
with cuts and call-ups.

266
00:12:44,943 --> 00:12:48,342
If the squad needs reinforcements,
we'll sign new talent.

267
00:12:48,367 --> 00:12:49,999
(Roster additions permitted as needed)

268
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:53,667
Bringing in fresh reinforcements
will anchor the entire team.

269
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:58,900
We needed Yeon Joo's veteran presence...

270
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:02,966
and a proven leader on the floor.

271
00:13:02,967 --> 00:13:04,517
So we called her in for a workout.

272
00:13:05,334 --> 00:13:06,434
Yeon Joo is here.

273
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,499
- Good to see you.
- Hi there.

274
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:10,766
(One day earlier: Yeon Joo's tryout)

275
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:11,691
Hello.

276
00:13:12,134 --> 00:13:13,666
Let's get this workout started.

277
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:14,899
We'll open with serving.

278
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,295
You're not aiming for the cones.

279
00:13:16,467 --> 00:13:18,400
Aim for this pocket, right into Zone 1.

280
00:13:19,334 --> 00:13:21,300
Zone 2. Place it in the gap.

281
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:23,367
This section is Zone 3.

282
00:13:24,534 --> 00:13:26,000
And this back corner is Zone 4.

283
00:13:26,334 --> 00:13:27,506
Try dropping one right here.

284
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:28,628
Into the seam.

285
00:13:28,653 --> 00:13:30,176
Let me hit a couple
of standing serves first.

286
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:31,734
(Serve to the designated spot.)

287
00:13:32,134 --> 00:13:33,800
(The eagle-eyed coach locks in.)

288
00:13:38,134 --> 00:13:40,167
Targeting right here, correct?

289
00:13:41,967 --> 00:13:44,100
(Right on the spot)

290
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,800
(Nice.)

291
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,099
Got the feel for it now.

292
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:50,067
(Locks in the groove immediately)

293
00:13:56,967 --> 00:13:58,033
That's 66!

294
00:13:58,034 --> 00:13:59,233
(Spot serve drilled into Zone 4)

295
00:13:59,234 --> 00:14:00,267
- Good.
- That's 66!

296
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:04,666
Nice.

297
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:05,666
That one hit 70.

298
00:14:05,667 --> 00:14:06,934
(Fired at 70 km per hour)

299
00:14:07,234 --> 00:14:09,015
She gets genuine pop on the ball,
and her mechanics are so clean.

300
00:14:09,734 --> 00:14:12,418
She barely put anything into that swing
and it still clocked over 65.

301
00:14:13,267 --> 00:14:14,553
That was just an easy contact.

302
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,034
Good.

303
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,034
(Nods in approval)

304
00:14:23,167 --> 00:14:24,167
That pace was crisp.

305
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,700
(Pinpoint timing)

306
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:33,234
(She rips right through the double block.)

307
00:14:33,667 --> 00:14:36,299
(Next test: serve receive)

308
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,334
All right.

309
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,700
(Drops it cleanly into the target basket
on touch two)

310
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,000
Pretty ball.

311
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,734
(Smiles)

312
00:14:45,034 --> 00:14:46,242
Her touch hasn't gone anywhere, has it?

313
00:14:46,267 --> 00:14:47,253
Not a bit.

314
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:50,198
- She tracks it all the way in.
- Reads the flight before making contact.

315
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:51,201
(Class is permanent)

316
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:52,825
Now she just needs
to get her vertical back.

317
00:14:54,367 --> 00:14:56,599
(Next up: blocking drills)

318
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,266
Let's go! One, two, close!

319
00:14:58,267 --> 00:14:59,267
(Up for the block)

320
00:15:00,034 --> 00:15:01,133
(And again)

321
00:15:01,134 --> 00:15:02,133
One, two, up!

322
00:15:02,134 --> 00:15:03,767
(Relentless reps on the net)

323
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,471
Strong block. Good lateral read.

324
00:15:06,067 --> 00:15:07,066
One, two, plant!

325
00:15:07,067 --> 00:15:08,133
Clean.

326
00:15:08,134 --> 00:15:09,267
(Textbook blocking technique)

327
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,776
(Exhales heavily)

328
00:15:11,934 --> 00:15:13,066
(Gasping for air)

329
00:15:13,067 --> 00:15:13,779
Let's go!

330
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,133
One, two, jump!

331
00:15:15,134 --> 00:15:16,634
(Solid form at the net)

332
00:15:17,734 --> 00:15:18,733
(Deep breath in)

333
00:15:18,734 --> 00:15:19,734
(Blowing out air)

334
00:15:20,146 --> 00:15:21,887
What's got her looking that wiped out?

335
00:15:22,602 --> 00:15:23,635
Why is she struggling so much?

336
00:15:23,942 --> 00:15:25,691
Her stamina is the issue.

337
00:15:26,309 --> 00:15:27,593
Getting older is tough.

338
00:15:28,509 --> 00:15:30,408
(Panting)

339
00:15:30,409 --> 00:15:31,776
I'm so out of breath.

340
00:15:33,009 --> 00:15:34,908
Honestly, after retiring,

341
00:15:34,909 --> 00:15:37,575
I wanted to live a normal life,

342
00:15:37,576 --> 00:15:42,341
so I took time off
and completely stopped training.

343
00:15:42,342 --> 00:15:45,178
It feels about three times harder
than when I was active.

344
00:15:46,209 --> 00:15:49,209
I tire out much faster
than the younger players.

345
00:15:49,517 --> 00:15:50,249
Another round.

346
00:15:51,677 --> 00:15:52,318
Okay.

347
00:15:54,276 --> 00:15:56,875
(She still pushes
through the blocking drill.)

348
00:15:56,876 --> 00:15:58,676
- Good work.
- Great job today.

349
00:15:59,242 --> 00:16:00,608
How would you rate your fitness right now?

350
00:16:00,609 --> 00:16:02,475
Right now? Around 50 percent.

351
00:16:02,476 --> 00:16:04,275
- About 50 percent?
- Maybe 60 percent.

352
00:16:04,276 --> 00:16:06,908
So can you handle this training volume?

353
00:16:06,909 --> 00:16:08,108
- Absolutely, I can.
- Really?

354
00:16:08,109 --> 00:16:10,469
- Sure.
- All right. Got it.

355
00:16:10,642 --> 00:16:11,608
Good work today.

356
00:16:11,609 --> 00:16:14,675
During the workout,

357
00:16:14,676 --> 00:16:17,741
she wasn't quite at full fitness,

358
00:16:17,742 --> 00:16:19,641
so I'm a little concerned.

359
00:16:19,642 --> 00:16:24,108
Still, she brings skills
that only come with experience.

360
00:16:24,109 --> 00:16:26,909
She's exactly what this team needs.

361
00:16:27,509 --> 00:16:31,642
(Hwang Yeon Joo officially joins
the Wonder Dogs.)

362
00:16:32,576 --> 00:16:37,808
(Hwang Yeon Joo)

363
00:16:37,809 --> 00:16:40,575
I never imagined Yeon Joo and I...

364
00:16:40,576 --> 00:16:43,308
would end up as coach and player.

365
00:16:43,309 --> 00:16:46,941
We're practically the same age.

366
00:16:46,942 --> 00:16:50,908
It's amazing how things...

367
00:16:50,909 --> 00:16:52,675
turn out like this.

368
00:16:52,676 --> 00:16:57,409
I never saw it coming, but here we are.

369
00:16:58,109 --> 00:17:01,542
(Yeon Joo joins the squad
the very next day.)

370
00:17:02,009 --> 00:17:04,608
- I'd only ever seen her from afar.
- Same here.

371
00:17:04,609 --> 00:17:06,475
- Just from a distance.
- Me too.

372
00:17:06,476 --> 00:17:09,808
I'd never practiced with Yeon Joo before.

373
00:17:09,809 --> 00:17:11,508
I'd only watched her on TV...

374
00:17:11,509 --> 00:17:13,975
or seen her from across the arena.

375
00:17:13,976 --> 00:17:15,476
It still doesn't feel real.

376
00:17:15,876 --> 00:17:17,308
I was really looking forward to it...

377
00:17:17,309 --> 00:17:18,476
but pretty intimidated too.

378
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:22,409
What if she gets frustrated with us
every time we make a mistake?

379
00:17:23,009 --> 00:17:24,442
I was definitely worried.

380
00:17:25,609 --> 00:17:27,441
How's practice going? Are you having fun?

381
00:17:27,466 --> 00:17:29,933
It's demanding...

382
00:17:30,276 --> 00:17:31,708
- but fun.
- Yeah?

383
00:17:31,709 --> 00:17:32,908
- You're learning a ton, right?
- Definitely.

384
00:17:32,909 --> 00:17:34,809
- I had a feeling.
- The approach is totally different.

385
00:17:35,276 --> 00:17:36,555
I'm here to learn too.

386
00:17:37,042 --> 00:17:38,476
- You are?
- Absolutely.

387
00:17:39,609 --> 00:17:41,341
All right, everyone. Bring it in.

388
00:17:41,342 --> 00:17:42,395
- Yes.
- Yes, Coach.

389
00:17:44,509 --> 00:17:48,608
We have a special guest with us today.

390
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:51,808
We'll run drills
and play 6-on-6 together today. Got it?

391
00:17:51,809 --> 00:17:52,876
- Yes!
- Yes!

392
00:17:53,576 --> 00:17:55,641
Six-on-six. Split into two sides.

393
00:17:55,642 --> 00:17:57,242
One middle blocker per side.

394
00:17:57,742 --> 00:17:59,078
Outside hitter over here.

395
00:17:59,742 --> 00:18:00,947
Enkhsoyol, slide to the back row.

396
00:18:01,242 --> 00:18:02,341
Let's roll!

397
00:18:02,342 --> 00:18:05,209
(Team A: Enkhsoyol, Ho Bin, Young In,
Yu Kyung, Min Kyeong, Hyo Rim)

398
00:18:05,642 --> 00:18:07,241
Yeon Joo, take the opposite on the right.

399
00:18:07,242 --> 00:18:09,041
(Team B: Chae Rim, Ye Dam, Yeon Joo,
Seon Ah, Song Hee, Da Sol)

400
00:18:09,042 --> 00:18:10,142
- Let's go!
- Let's get it.

401
00:18:11,609 --> 00:18:13,476
(Nervous)

402
00:18:13,576 --> 00:18:14,908
Send it high if the pass comes up short.

403
00:18:14,909 --> 00:18:16,308
(The scrimmage begins.)

404
00:18:16,309 --> 00:18:17,776
- Setter!
- Mine!

405
00:18:18,276 --> 00:18:20,842
(Team A vs. Team B)

406
00:18:23,976 --> 00:18:25,841
(Team B)

407
00:18:25,842 --> 00:18:27,909
(Yeon Joo's first attack opportunity)

408
00:18:28,609 --> 00:18:29,575
(A heavy spike)

409
00:18:29,576 --> 00:18:31,341
(Team A)

410
00:18:31,342 --> 00:18:32,742
(Team A keeps the play alive.)

411
00:18:33,109 --> 00:18:34,809
(A transition chance for Team A)

412
00:18:38,076 --> 00:18:39,108
Nice dig!

413
00:18:39,109 --> 00:18:40,676
- Great read, Yeon Joo.
- Man.

414
00:18:41,342 --> 00:18:42,209
My fault.

415
00:18:42,752 --> 00:18:45,151
- Come on.
- I've got the set.

416
00:18:45,176 --> 00:18:46,076
Got it.

417
00:18:47,076 --> 00:18:49,542
(Team A vs. Team B)

418
00:18:50,449 --> 00:18:51,216
Swing through!

419
00:18:51,842 --> 00:18:52,809
One, two.

420
00:18:53,576 --> 00:18:54,767
That flew right past my head.

421
00:18:55,842 --> 00:18:56,709
Sorry.

422
00:18:57,609 --> 00:18:58,576
My bad.

423
00:18:59,142 --> 00:19:00,506
Sorry. One more step out.

424
00:19:01,776 --> 00:19:03,208
I can barely get off the floor.

425
00:19:03,209 --> 00:19:04,110
This is brutal.

426
00:19:08,176 --> 00:19:10,216
- Yeon Joo looks stiffer than yesterday.
- She does.

427
00:19:11,242 --> 00:19:12,242
She's really gassed.

428
00:19:13,476 --> 00:19:16,976
(Yeon Joo struggles to find her groove.)

429
00:19:21,709 --> 00:19:22,976
I'll call the play.

430
00:19:23,609 --> 00:19:24,442
Got it.

431
00:19:24,876 --> 00:19:26,309
Lock in!

432
00:19:27,076 --> 00:19:28,708
(Rallying the team)

433
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,109
Stay sharp.

434
00:19:30,276 --> 00:19:31,242
Run it back!

435
00:19:33,209 --> 00:19:36,076
(Play resumes.)

436
00:19:36,476 --> 00:19:37,242
Swing!

437
00:19:40,642 --> 00:19:42,942
(No block closing on the right)

438
00:19:43,409 --> 00:19:44,375
(A quick scan)

439
00:19:44,376 --> 00:19:45,275
Right-side pipe!

440
00:19:45,276 --> 00:19:46,276
Feed me!

441
00:19:51,509 --> 00:19:52,775
(Tool off the block and out)

442
00:19:52,776 --> 00:19:53,742
Great call, Yeon Joo.

443
00:19:54,042 --> 00:19:54,908
Attack.

444
00:19:54,909 --> 00:19:55,842
Nice.

445
00:19:56,742 --> 00:19:58,176
Let's run it back.

446
00:19:59,109 --> 00:20:00,266
Back-row attack again.

447
00:20:04,242 --> 00:20:06,009
Read the deep court!

448
00:20:07,109 --> 00:20:07,976
There you go!

449
00:20:08,342 --> 00:20:09,841
(Team B takes the point.)

450
00:20:09,842 --> 00:20:10,976
Good ball.

451
00:20:11,442 --> 00:20:13,208
- When the set is pushed inside,
- Cut across it.

452
00:20:13,209 --> 00:20:15,441
- don't swing full. Just drop a tip.
- Got it.

453
00:20:15,442 --> 00:20:16,449
Take it down the line.

454
00:20:16,809 --> 00:20:20,209
Yeon Joo breaks down
every single play for them.

455
00:20:20,709 --> 00:20:22,776
- Let's get a side-out!
- Stay locked in.

456
00:20:24,009 --> 00:20:25,341
Pop it up! Put it away!

457
00:20:25,342 --> 00:20:26,141
Move!

458
00:20:26,142 --> 00:20:27,541
Pop it up! Put it away!

459
00:20:27,542 --> 00:20:28,775
Set it out in front of me.

460
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:30,533
- Cover.
- Drive it deep!

461
00:20:31,042 --> 00:20:32,076
Right side!

462
00:20:32,676 --> 00:20:33,775
One, two.

463
00:20:33,776 --> 00:20:34,709
Mine!

464
00:20:36,242 --> 00:20:37,542
Right side! Go up!

465
00:20:40,809 --> 00:20:41,876
Nice!

466
00:20:42,676 --> 00:20:45,508
(Team B stacks back-to-back points.)

467
00:20:45,509 --> 00:20:46,342
Good.

468
00:20:46,676 --> 00:20:47,576
One more!

469
00:20:49,509 --> 00:20:52,009
(Another rally unfolds.)

470
00:20:52,809 --> 00:20:53,841
Yes!

471
00:20:53,842 --> 00:20:55,275
Great work.

472
00:20:55,276 --> 00:20:57,276
(Unlike the vocal Team B,)

473
00:20:58,742 --> 00:21:01,576
(Team A stays dead silent
after dropping the point.)

474
00:21:03,842 --> 00:21:04,976
- Ready!
- Ready!

475
00:21:09,235 --> 00:21:10,169
Sorry.

476
00:21:11,241 --> 00:21:12,004
Sorry.

477
00:21:12,176 --> 00:21:13,676
(An erratic set)

478
00:21:14,542 --> 00:21:16,909
(Team B gets another opening.)

479
00:21:18,309 --> 00:21:20,908
(Team A drops another point.)

480
00:21:20,909 --> 00:21:22,109
Sorry about that.

481
00:21:22,876 --> 00:21:25,076
My bad.

482
00:21:26,709 --> 00:21:30,476
(Still total silence on Team A)

483
00:21:31,409 --> 00:21:33,275
Hyo Rim, why didn't you jump-set
on a ball that high?

484
00:21:33,276 --> 00:21:34,841
- I told you to jump-set those.
- Yes, Coach.

485
00:21:34,842 --> 00:21:36,641
- Set your feet and jump-set.
- Understood.

486
00:21:36,642 --> 00:21:38,809
(Coach Kim finally steps in.)

487
00:21:42,776 --> 00:21:44,476
(Another inconsistent set)

488
00:21:44,742 --> 00:21:46,142
No, that's not it.

489
00:21:46,776 --> 00:21:47,642
One, two.

490
00:21:48,109 --> 00:21:49,076
(A beat of hesitation)

491
00:21:50,576 --> 00:21:51,442
Put it away!

492
00:21:52,442 --> 00:21:54,542
Hyo Rim, get to your spot faster!

493
00:21:55,476 --> 00:21:57,109
(Hesitates again)

494
00:22:04,576 --> 00:22:06,909
(The players exchange quiet glances.)

495
00:22:09,476 --> 00:22:12,142
- Hyo Rim, beat the ball to the spot.
- Yes.

496
00:22:12,542 --> 00:22:14,408
- You're consistently a step late.
- Yes, Coach.

497
00:22:14,409 --> 00:22:15,941
That's why your release is inconsistent.

498
00:22:15,942 --> 00:22:17,441
- Your sets are spraying everywhere.
- Yes, Coach.

499
00:22:17,442 --> 00:22:18,904
- Who can hit that?
- Understood.

500
00:22:19,676 --> 00:22:21,674
- How is anyone supposed to swing on that?
- Yes, Coach.

501
00:22:26,876 --> 00:22:28,242
(Hesitates once more)

502
00:22:28,376 --> 00:22:29,209
Swing!

503
00:22:30,509 --> 00:22:31,575
(Team A keeps bleeding points.)

504
00:22:31,576 --> 00:22:33,342
I think I pushed it too high.

505
00:22:36,609 --> 00:22:38,642
Sure, keep delivering sets like that.

506
00:22:39,042 --> 00:22:41,641
Keep putting your hitters
in impossible spots.

507
00:22:41,642 --> 00:22:43,162
See how long you stay on the losing end.

508
00:22:44,976 --> 00:22:47,754
And where are you supposed
to direct the first contact...

509
00:22:47,778 --> 00:22:49,167
if you want to score?

510
00:22:52,642 --> 00:22:54,108
- Play with some intent to win!
- Yes.

511
00:22:54,109 --> 00:22:55,108
It's the first touch.

512
00:22:55,109 --> 00:22:57,175
Where does that ball need to go
to set up a point?

513
00:22:57,176 --> 00:22:58,611
Think through the play!

514
00:23:05,176 --> 00:23:07,086
What does it take to win the rally?

515
00:23:11,442 --> 00:23:12,933
No matter what kind of pass
Yu Kyung delivers,

516
00:23:12,958 --> 00:23:14,092
Hyo Rim doesn't say a word.

517
00:23:14,642 --> 00:23:17,442
Nobody talks. Not Ye Dam, not Young In.

518
00:23:19,276 --> 00:23:21,741
It looks like you don't even care
about winning.

519
00:23:21,742 --> 00:23:23,875
Look across the net.

520
00:23:23,876 --> 00:23:25,671
Did you see what they were doing
over there?

521
00:23:26,142 --> 00:23:27,840
Did you hear how much
they were communicating?

522
00:23:34,242 --> 00:23:35,608
To wrap up today's session,

523
00:23:35,609 --> 00:23:38,808
the losing side stays on this floor
with us for an extra hour.

524
00:23:38,809 --> 00:23:40,709
- Whichever team drops this set.
- Yes, Coach.

525
00:23:43,209 --> 00:23:44,475
Come on, show some fight.

526
00:23:44,476 --> 00:23:45,976
Base positions.

527
00:23:54,376 --> 00:23:57,076
(The final rally kicks off.)

528
00:23:58,209 --> 00:23:59,575
- Song Hee!
- Get back on defense!

529
00:23:59,576 --> 00:24:00,642
- Move!
- Push it out!

530
00:24:01,342 --> 00:24:02,576
Got it! Great up!

531
00:24:02,976 --> 00:24:04,375
Finish it!

532
00:24:04,376 --> 00:24:05,542
(Communication ramps up across the floor.)

533
00:24:06,909 --> 00:24:09,141
(Nobody wants to drop this point.)

534
00:24:09,142 --> 00:24:11,342
Ye Dam, get a hand on it!

535
00:24:11,776 --> 00:24:12,909
Cover the pass!

536
00:24:13,383 --> 00:24:14,608
Put it to the floor!

537
00:24:15,088 --> 00:24:16,383
Put it to the floor!

538
00:24:17,242 --> 00:24:20,141
(The intensity reaches a fever pitch.)

539
00:24:20,142 --> 00:24:21,475
- Mine!
- Get the block up!

540
00:24:21,476 --> 00:24:22,941
- Run a C-quick!
- Enkhsoyol!

541
00:24:22,942 --> 00:24:24,476
Enkhsoyol, put it away!

542
00:24:25,209 --> 00:24:26,609
- Stay alert!
- Mine!

543
00:24:27,809 --> 00:24:29,168
- Watch the tip!
- Hey.

544
00:24:29,842 --> 00:24:30,709
- Nice pass.
- Yeon Joo!

545
00:24:31,763 --> 00:24:32,471
Mine!

546
00:24:32,642 --> 00:24:33,939
You've got to terminate that!

547
00:24:34,571 --> 00:24:35,374
Set it up!

548
00:24:35,809 --> 00:24:37,509
(The marathon rally keeps going.)

549
00:24:37,909 --> 00:24:39,809
Get back up!

550
00:24:40,076 --> 00:24:41,042
(Scrambles back to her feet)

551
00:24:41,210 --> 00:24:42,110
(Out of breath)

552
00:24:42,142 --> 00:24:43,176
One, two.

553
00:24:45,009 --> 00:24:47,042
(Another unreal defensive save)

554
00:24:54,309 --> 00:24:58,809
(Team B closes out a gritty battle.)

555
00:25:00,976 --> 00:25:02,167
Great job.

556
00:25:02,909 --> 00:25:04,275
Winners, you're off the court.

557
00:25:04,276 --> 00:25:06,209
Losers, you've got another hour
of drills with us.

558
00:25:07,742 --> 00:25:09,408
(Team B heads off the court.)

559
00:25:09,409 --> 00:25:10,776
Losing squad, line up over here.

560
00:25:13,109 --> 00:25:15,275
We're doing 100 reps.

561
00:25:15,276 --> 00:25:16,548
- A clean hundred.
- Yes, Coach.

562
00:25:17,642 --> 00:25:18,641
Defensive stance.

563
00:25:18,666 --> 00:25:21,433
(Punishment drills start:
100 digs and 100 sets each)

564
00:25:23,384 --> 00:25:24,523
Nice defense.

565
00:25:26,034 --> 00:25:27,468
How many?

566
00:25:27,903 --> 00:25:30,037
- Keep count yourselves!
- Got it!

567
00:25:32,674 --> 00:25:34,008
Six!

568
00:25:34,242 --> 00:25:35,175
Defense!

569
00:25:35,176 --> 00:25:36,511
- Thirty-seven!
- Thirty-seven!

570
00:25:36,512 --> 00:25:37,277
Good.

571
00:25:37,970 --> 00:25:39,179
- Forty-four!
- Forty-four!

572
00:25:39,314 --> 00:25:41,707
Your feet are too slow!

573
00:25:42,284 --> 00:25:43,684
Your timing is completely off!

574
00:25:43,685 --> 00:25:44,553
Forty-seven.

575
00:25:44,554 --> 00:25:46,254
- That was 47!
- Sorry, Coach!

576
00:25:46,255 --> 00:25:49,090
I'm honestly disappointed.

577
00:25:50,592 --> 00:25:52,539
During tryouts,

578
00:25:52,563 --> 00:25:58,166
every single one of them looked
genuinely hungry.

579
00:25:59,267 --> 00:26:01,368
They worked so hard.

580
00:26:01,369 --> 00:26:02,336
Nice!

581
00:26:03,071 --> 00:26:05,072
Now that they're on the court
together, though...

582
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,975
they're timid, and they're waiting
for things to happen.

583
00:26:07,976 --> 00:26:09,242
(Their passive demeanor
stood out during training.)

584
00:26:09,779 --> 00:26:10,991
Play like this,

585
00:26:11,015 --> 00:26:14,314
and they won't take a single set
off anyone.

586
00:26:14,315 --> 00:26:16,985
(They're not going to win like this.)

587
00:26:19,054 --> 00:26:20,012
Nice dig!

588
00:26:21,590 --> 00:26:23,724
- One hundred!
- One hundred.

589
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:25,359
Gather around.

590
00:26:31,032 --> 00:26:32,124
How should I put this...

591
00:26:35,237 --> 00:26:38,238
How do you actually feel
when you drop a point?

592
00:26:42,544 --> 00:26:43,877
From where I'm standing,

593
00:26:44,212 --> 00:26:47,281
it looks like losing doesn't
even bother you.

594
00:26:48,750 --> 00:26:51,452
I don't see any fire.

595
00:26:53,989 --> 00:26:56,657
I know some of you came from pro clubs
and some didn't.

596
00:26:57,525 --> 00:27:01,162
Maybe sitting out of real competition
dulled your edge.

597
00:27:02,029 --> 00:27:06,266
You play like you're comfortable
conceding the floor.

598
00:27:08,069 --> 00:27:10,396
If I knew you had this mindset,
I wouldn't have brought you in.

599
00:27:11,907 --> 00:27:13,766
This team has no room for passengers.

600
00:27:17,279 --> 00:27:21,115
If this is the energy you bring,

601
00:27:22,256 --> 00:27:24,349
I don't see how we can
move forward together.

602
00:27:29,157 --> 00:27:32,092
Tell me now,

603
00:27:33,262 --> 00:27:35,054
so we can part ways cleanly.

604
00:27:37,898 --> 00:27:39,358
If you want a spot on this roster,

605
00:27:39,467 --> 00:27:43,104
fix your attitude and your mindset.

606
00:27:51,246 --> 00:27:52,813
- Am I clear?
- Yes, Coach!

607
00:27:53,415 --> 00:27:55,383
- Thank you for your hard work!
- Thank you for your hard work!

608
00:28:01,268 --> 00:28:02,180
You worked hard today.

609
00:28:07,502 --> 00:28:08,320
(Sighing)

610
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:14,068
Her words hit like a ton of bricks,

611
00:28:16,172 --> 00:28:20,741
hearing that we looked
like losers who accepted defeat.

612
00:28:28,917 --> 00:28:30,784
Hyo Rim, why aren't
you getting off the floor?

613
00:28:30,785 --> 00:28:32,152
You need to jump-set!

614
00:28:32,153 --> 00:28:34,288
Hyo Rim, beat the ball to the spot!

615
00:28:34,289 --> 00:28:36,657
(Hyo Rim got called out the most.)

616
00:28:36,825 --> 00:28:38,492
How is anyone supposed to swing on that?

617
00:28:38,493 --> 00:28:39,293
Understood.

618
00:28:40,062 --> 00:28:42,655
I was just so disgusted with myself.

619
00:28:43,899 --> 00:28:46,667
Why do I keep pulling back?

620
00:28:46,668 --> 00:28:51,072
Why am I so comfortable riding the bench?

621
00:28:51,773 --> 00:28:54,274
Since when was settling for this okay?

622
00:28:54,275 --> 00:28:56,176
(Why do I feel so complacent?)

623
00:28:56,912 --> 00:28:59,780
I was just furious with myself.

624
00:29:04,887 --> 00:29:06,945
Six of you over here,
the rest across the net.

625
00:29:07,021 --> 00:29:08,755
We run the same lineups as yesterday.

626
00:29:08,756 --> 00:29:09,790
(Next day)

627
00:29:09,791 --> 00:29:11,150
Same rosters as yesterday.

628
00:29:12,328 --> 00:29:14,161
Have you already forgotten?

629
00:29:14,629 --> 00:29:15,963
- Let's get it.
- Let's lock in today.

630
00:29:15,964 --> 00:29:17,264
- We've got this.
- Yes, we can.

631
00:29:18,767 --> 00:29:19,667
We can do this!

632
00:29:19,668 --> 00:29:21,168
- Make sure to cover.
- We take this one!

633
00:29:21,169 --> 00:29:22,737
Cover it together!

634
00:29:22,738 --> 00:29:23,704
(Glance)

635
00:29:23,705 --> 00:29:25,673
- Hitters, load up early.
- Got it.

636
00:29:26,475 --> 00:29:27,332
One, two, three!

637
00:29:29,011 --> 00:29:30,803
Why are they hyping themselves up?

638
00:29:31,112 --> 00:29:32,438
What's got into them?

639
00:29:34,349 --> 00:29:36,858
- Let's go!
- Base positions!

640
00:29:36,883 --> 00:29:37,951
(Six-on-six like yesterday)

641
00:29:37,952 --> 00:29:39,486
- Ball up!
- Do it!

642
00:29:39,487 --> 00:29:40,388
Swing!

643
00:29:40,922 --> 00:29:42,047
Nice!

644
00:29:43,660 --> 00:29:46,260
(Energy not like yesterday)

645
00:29:46,261 --> 00:29:47,293
Min Kyeong, we're running our call.

646
00:29:47,294 --> 00:29:48,595
On three!

647
00:29:48,596 --> 00:29:49,939
- Read the tip!
- B!

648
00:29:50,422 --> 00:29:51,932
- Got it!
- Go!

649
00:29:52,133 --> 00:29:53,867
Dig, over there!

650
00:29:54,195 --> 00:29:57,964
Stick to the scouting report for Shujitsu.

651
00:29:58,339 --> 00:30:00,640
Every one of us came here
with something to prove.

652
00:30:00,641 --> 00:30:02,835
I want to show her
that I belong on this floor.

653
00:30:03,778 --> 00:30:04,711
Coach Bong Woo.

654
00:30:04,946 --> 00:30:06,413
Quick question.

655
00:30:08,349 --> 00:30:09,249
Base looks solid.

656
00:30:09,250 --> 00:30:10,743
They're grinding hard out there.

657
00:30:11,586 --> 00:30:14,821
- Good ball.
- Clean hands, Hyo Rim!

658
00:30:15,090 --> 00:30:15,735
Min Kyeong!

659
00:30:15,759 --> 00:30:16,390
Chae Rim!

660
00:30:16,391 --> 00:30:17,061
Ye Dam!

661
00:30:17,085 --> 00:30:18,851
- Stay ready!
- On it!

662
00:30:19,027 --> 00:30:20,628
Deep left is mine.

663
00:30:20,629 --> 00:30:22,696
Great pass! Perfect.

664
00:30:22,697 --> 00:30:23,530
Young In.

665
00:30:23,531 --> 00:30:24,665
There it is!

666
00:30:25,567 --> 00:30:26,967
Nice!

667
00:30:27,019 --> 00:30:29,303
- Two points.
- Clean contact.

668
00:30:29,304 --> 00:30:31,063
Great touch, Hyo Rim.

669
00:30:31,338 --> 00:30:33,774
Seal the net on that block.

670
00:30:33,775 --> 00:30:34,808
- Yes, Coach!
- Yes, Coach!

671
00:30:34,809 --> 00:30:36,710
- One-on-one.
- That's right. More!

672
00:30:36,711 --> 00:30:38,145
Hit the seam with precision.

673
00:30:38,146 --> 00:30:38,992
Good.

674
00:30:39,016 --> 00:30:40,847
- That's right.
- Nice!

675
00:30:40,848 --> 00:30:42,207
Right there.

676
00:30:48,002 --> 00:30:51,304
(The day of the match)

677
00:30:52,927 --> 00:30:54,261
We need a luxury charter bus.

678
00:30:54,262 --> 00:30:55,962
(Upgraded bus)

679
00:30:56,364 --> 00:30:58,132
Now that feels like true pro tier.

680
00:30:58,133 --> 00:31:00,793
These seats are plusher
than what the V-League clubs ride in.

681
00:31:02,670 --> 00:31:03,970
It's pretty warm today.

682
00:31:03,971 --> 00:31:08,675
(First game: home game)

683
00:31:09,970 --> 00:31:11,704
(Wonder Dogs' locker room)

684
00:31:16,918 --> 00:31:18,852
It looks way better than last year.

685
00:31:20,088 --> 00:31:22,056
(Locker room: 2025)

686
00:31:23,057 --> 00:31:24,824
(For the new season,)

687
00:31:24,825 --> 00:31:26,092
(the locker room got an upgrade.)

688
00:31:26,093 --> 00:31:27,027
No way.

689
00:31:27,529 --> 00:31:28,462
What's all this?

690
00:31:29,030 --> 00:31:31,632
(Redesigned uniforms)

691
00:31:31,633 --> 00:31:33,058
These are sharp.

692
00:31:33,968 --> 00:31:35,627
The kits look so much sleeker.

693
00:31:35,737 --> 00:31:36,637
What's this?

694
00:31:37,038 --> 00:31:38,939
(Bananas and energy bars)

695
00:31:39,474 --> 00:31:41,475
Manager Boo left these.

696
00:31:41,476 --> 00:31:42,776
His handwriting is adorable.

697
00:31:42,777 --> 00:31:44,812
(Let's win our first game, Wonder Dogs!
Good luck. Don't forget to stretch.)

698
00:31:45,119 --> 00:31:47,754
(A few hours ago)

699
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:50,242
Wait, what?

700
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:53,378
(Manager Boo was the first to get here.)

701
00:31:53,379 --> 00:31:54,712
Is this the new locker room?

702
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:59,083
It's way bigger and much nicer.

703
00:31:59,084 --> 00:31:59,750
(Glance)

704
00:32:00,185 --> 00:32:01,052
(Admiring)

705
00:32:01,053 --> 00:32:03,387
Takes me right back to the old days.

706
00:32:04,790 --> 00:32:07,158
Still, duty calls.

707
00:32:07,159 --> 00:32:08,292
(Knock knock)

708
00:32:08,293 --> 00:32:10,194
- Hello.
- Hello.

709
00:32:11,197 --> 00:32:12,998
- Who's there?
- Hello.

710
00:32:12,999 --> 00:32:16,134
I'm the newly appointed manager,
Ahn Jeong Hyeon.

711
00:32:16,135 --> 00:32:17,536
- Great to meet you!
- I'm really happy to join.

712
00:32:17,537 --> 00:32:19,738
I was the manager back in Season One.

713
00:32:19,739 --> 00:32:20,605
(A new manager?)

714
00:32:20,606 --> 00:32:22,707
After a lot of back-and-forth,

715
00:32:22,855 --> 00:32:25,623
we came to the decision...

716
00:32:25,711 --> 00:32:28,079
that we couldn't keep you on
as manager this season.

717
00:32:29,783 --> 00:32:32,050
Wait, am I getting cut?

718
00:32:33,786 --> 00:32:35,787
- You've been promoted.
- Promoted?

719
00:32:37,657 --> 00:32:38,757
(Accepted)

720
00:32:38,758 --> 00:32:39,658
Wait, really?

721
00:32:40,993 --> 00:32:43,027
- My heart is racing right now.
- Seriously?

722
00:32:43,028 --> 00:32:45,396
This is only day one.

723
00:32:45,397 --> 00:32:47,165
Kidding, just messing with you!

724
00:32:47,433 --> 00:32:50,368
I still need to pass down the torch.

725
00:32:50,369 --> 00:32:52,404
- I won't let you down.
- What do we tackle first?

726
00:32:52,638 --> 00:32:54,339
Truth be told,

727
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:57,241
I've only been doing
this sports management gig...

728
00:32:57,272 --> 00:33:01,075
for about two years myself,
counting last year.

729
00:33:01,547 --> 00:33:02,880
(Trying not to smile)

730
00:33:02,881 --> 00:33:05,116
I want the room set up
before the squad arrives.

731
00:33:05,117 --> 00:33:06,484
Didn't you bring your bags in?

732
00:33:07,453 --> 00:33:08,987
- I left the gear outside.
- You left it?

733
00:33:08,988 --> 00:33:10,688
- I'm sorry.
- Go grab it right now!

734
00:33:10,689 --> 00:33:12,090
- Yes, sir.
- Hustle!

735
00:33:14,519 --> 00:33:17,128
(Last year, when he was a rookie manager)

736
00:33:17,129 --> 00:33:20,998
Best to stay under the radar
before the game.

737
00:33:21,033 --> 00:33:23,067
Whatever you do, don't bump into them.

738
00:33:24,022 --> 00:33:25,864
(Manager Boo's rookie days)

739
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:28,039
She must be feeling the heat.

740
00:33:28,841 --> 00:33:29,874
There we go.

741
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:32,143
- Sorry about that.
- Don't sweat it.

742
00:33:33,313 --> 00:33:34,479
So my plan was...

743
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:36,080
we lay these out together.

744
00:33:36,081 --> 00:33:37,983
- Got it?
- I'm on it.

745
00:33:37,984 --> 00:33:40,285
Keep the presentation clean.

746
00:33:40,686 --> 00:33:44,523
Now let's hang up the jerseys
you brought in.

747
00:33:44,524 --> 00:33:46,558
Pay attention to the names.

748
00:33:46,725 --> 00:33:48,694
Hang a jersey in the wrong locker,

749
00:33:48,695 --> 00:33:50,395
and you're suspended on the spot.

750
00:33:51,831 --> 00:33:53,199
(Chuckling)

751
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:57,336
We'll leave a handwritten note
like Secret Santa.

752
00:33:57,569 --> 00:33:58,836
- Then we clear out.
- Okay.

753
00:33:59,705 --> 00:34:01,472
The squad is almost here.

754
00:34:01,473 --> 00:34:03,575
Time to bail.
Players will be walking in any second.

755
00:34:03,576 --> 00:34:05,843
If we get spotted, we're toast.

756
00:34:05,844 --> 00:34:07,812
Move, move!

757
00:34:08,347 --> 00:34:09,681
Get caught, and it's game over.

758
00:34:11,651 --> 00:34:13,184
How sweet is this, though?

759
00:34:13,209 --> 00:34:15,246
(Fortunately, the managers
escaped the encounter.)

760
00:34:16,589 --> 00:34:19,391
Should we signal the serve zones
from the bench?

761
00:34:19,392 --> 00:34:20,758
Or let them read the floor?

762
00:34:20,993 --> 00:34:22,560
What about calling 2 or 3?

763
00:34:22,762 --> 00:34:23,795
Zone 2 and 3, huh?

764
00:34:23,796 --> 00:34:26,156
If the target is 1, 4, or down the seam...

765
00:34:26,181 --> 00:34:27,332
Do we let them decide?

766
00:34:27,333 --> 00:34:28,767
Let's call it out when the look is there.

767
00:34:28,768 --> 00:34:30,235
The coaching staff will
chime in too, right?

768
00:34:30,236 --> 00:34:32,638
- Let me double-check with them.
- Please do.

769
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:34,405
What time do we take the floor again?

770
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:36,140
(Thinking only about the Shujitsu game)

771
00:34:36,141 --> 00:34:37,342
I like that look.

772
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:39,044
Once we hit 15 points...

773
00:34:39,878 --> 00:34:43,181
- Hey there.
- Look who showed up!

774
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:45,350
(Sportscaster Lee Ho Geun
visits the meeting room.)

775
00:34:45,818 --> 00:34:47,651
(Another person follows.)

776
00:34:47,787 --> 00:34:48,720
Wait, that's...

777
00:34:49,355 --> 00:34:50,622
Hello!

778
00:34:50,623 --> 00:34:51,756
Good to see you.

779
00:34:52,291 --> 00:34:53,324
Hello.

780
00:34:53,610 --> 00:34:56,342
Yeon Koung and I wore
the national team jersey together...

781
00:34:56,367 --> 00:34:57,522
for so many years.

782
00:34:57,685 --> 00:34:59,351
And we even shared a room,

783
00:34:59,918 --> 00:35:02,851
and experienced all the highs and lows
together.

784
00:35:03,185 --> 00:35:06,518
I know every side of her,

785
00:35:06,518 --> 00:35:10,351
and she's an irreplaceable part
of my life.

786
00:35:11,014 --> 00:35:13,947
(With commentator Lee Suk Ja
joining the national team as a coach,)

787
00:35:15,047 --> 00:35:18,347
(Commentator Yang Hyo Jin
makes her debut.)

788
00:35:18,981 --> 00:35:22,381
(Their first meeting
as commentator and head coach)

789
00:35:22,381 --> 00:35:24,147
(Still busy)

790
00:35:24,547 --> 00:35:26,581
The mood feels a bit more serious now.

791
00:35:31,681 --> 00:35:32,814
We're connected.

792
00:35:33,781 --> 00:35:36,181
Coach, show us a smile.

793
00:35:36,181 --> 00:35:37,847
Hyo Jin didn't sleep at all last night.

794
00:35:37,847 --> 00:35:39,347
I couldn't sleep a wink.

795
00:35:39,347 --> 00:35:40,848
- Really?
- I stayed up preparing.

796
00:35:41,547 --> 00:35:42,814
Not my problem.

797
00:35:43,414 --> 00:35:44,714
I knew you'd say that.

798
00:35:45,247 --> 00:35:47,714
Our focus has to be on the match
right now.

799
00:35:47,714 --> 00:35:50,981
We don't have time to worry
about the commentary booth.

800
00:35:51,247 --> 00:35:54,281
Do you know about the new face
joining our squad?

801
00:35:54,281 --> 00:35:56,647
- Yeon Joo?
- Right.

802
00:35:56,647 --> 00:35:58,147
I was genuinely surprised.

803
00:35:58,147 --> 00:36:01,081
She's the player I'm looking forward
to seeing the most today.

804
00:36:01,081 --> 00:36:03,614
She won't be suiting up today, though.

805
00:36:03,614 --> 00:36:05,914
She isn't at 100 percent yet.

806
00:36:06,481 --> 00:36:08,047
That's a bit...

807
00:36:08,814 --> 00:36:09,914
(Glance over)

808
00:36:09,914 --> 00:36:11,647
What's going on with your tie?

809
00:36:12,114 --> 00:36:14,134
(Designed by himself)

810
00:36:14,135 --> 00:36:16,114
- That mascot distracts me.
- Want one?

811
00:36:16,114 --> 00:36:17,714
Where am I even supposed to look?

812
00:36:17,714 --> 00:36:19,930
I keep looking at its eye.

813
00:36:19,964 --> 00:36:20,756
(Stare)

814
00:36:20,781 --> 00:36:21,847
Kind of annoying.

815
00:36:22,247 --> 00:36:24,147
I'm curious about this too.

816
00:36:24,147 --> 00:36:26,114
Our first opponent is
Shujitsu High School.

817
00:36:26,114 --> 00:36:29,447
What's your game plan?
How do you intend to break them down?

818
00:36:29,447 --> 00:36:31,581
We've scouted Shujitsu thoroughly,

819
00:36:31,581 --> 00:36:33,147
and our team has grown considerably.

820
00:36:33,147 --> 00:36:35,814
It's our first match today,
so it's incredibly important.

821
00:36:35,814 --> 00:36:39,881
More than anything,
I really want this win.

822
00:36:39,881 --> 00:36:43,014
I'll make sure we win.

823
00:36:46,947 --> 00:36:49,447
(Episode 2: A Revenge Match)

824
00:36:49,447 --> 00:36:50,714
From underdogs to wonders.

825
00:36:50,714 --> 00:36:53,881
The Wonder Dogs made
a miraculous run last year.

826
00:36:53,881 --> 00:36:58,347
Now, with new players,
they're ready to write a new chapter.

827
00:36:58,714 --> 00:37:02,681
Let's join commentator Yang Hyo Jin
for the Wonder Dogs' season opener.

828
00:37:02,681 --> 00:37:04,681
- Hello.
- Hello.

829
00:37:04,681 --> 00:37:06,514
Kim Yeon Koung is
no longer a rookie coach.

830
00:37:06,514 --> 00:37:09,179
She's now in her second year
as a head coach.

831
00:37:10,176 --> 00:37:14,747
We can look forward to seeing
her seasoned leadership in action.

832
00:37:15,314 --> 00:37:18,214
However, their first challenge is...

833
00:37:18,214 --> 00:37:20,414
none other than Shujitsu High School.

834
00:37:20,414 --> 00:37:25,181
In many ways, they represent
the Wonder Dogs' most painful scar.

835
00:37:25,181 --> 00:37:26,014
Exactly.

836
00:37:26,281 --> 00:37:28,714
Enkhsoyol, where should you hit it?

837
00:37:29,314 --> 00:37:30,481
Where should you hit it?

838
00:37:31,314 --> 00:37:32,114
Where?

839
00:37:33,681 --> 00:37:35,981
Maybe they're out of energy.

840
00:37:36,681 --> 00:37:38,381
They're completely exhausted.

841
00:37:40,947 --> 00:37:43,281
In the end, the set score was 3 to 2.

842
00:37:43,581 --> 00:37:46,847
Shujitsu High School
came from behind to win.

843
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:50,514
(An unexpected reverse sweep)

844
00:37:51,447 --> 00:37:53,147
It brought back the nightmare.

845
00:37:53,166 --> 00:37:54,346
They had totally drained us.

846
00:37:54,347 --> 00:37:56,047
We were ahead,

847
00:37:56,047 --> 00:37:59,013
but ended up losing 3 to 2.

848
00:37:59,013 --> 00:38:01,114
As a coach,
that stings with embarrassment.

849
00:38:01,981 --> 00:38:04,347
But this year will be different.

850
00:38:06,581 --> 00:38:09,347
Coach Kim Yeon Koung has fire
in her eyes today.

851
00:38:09,714 --> 00:38:11,681
Given that it's the opener,

852
00:38:11,681 --> 00:38:13,547
her preparation must have been relentless.

853
00:38:13,547 --> 00:38:16,714
- I'm excited.
- Absolutely.

854
00:38:16,714 --> 00:38:19,247
I'm calling a straight 3 to 0 sweep.

855
00:38:20,714 --> 00:38:24,081
I sincerely hope the Wonder Dogs...

856
00:38:24,081 --> 00:38:26,314
get off to a great start.

857
00:39:00,281 --> 00:39:02,481
We're a level above them.

858
00:39:03,881 --> 00:39:07,281
We'll show them our
energy and fighting spirit.

859
00:39:08,681 --> 00:39:11,581
This time, we're on the road in Korea.

860
00:39:12,047 --> 00:39:14,847
Just like last year,

861
00:39:16,981 --> 00:39:18,247
we'll definitely win.

862
00:39:27,481 --> 00:39:29,814
In their previous match
against Shujitsu High School,

863
00:39:29,814 --> 00:39:32,214
the Wonder Dogs jumped out
to a 2 to 0 set lead.

864
00:39:32,214 --> 00:39:34,247
Then they dropped the third, fourth,
and fifth frames,

865
00:39:34,247 --> 00:39:35,881
and suffered a reverse sweep.

866
00:39:36,514 --> 00:39:39,781
Now, Shujitsu is their
first opponent of the season.

867
00:39:40,981 --> 00:39:44,514
Shujitsu High School handed...

868
00:39:44,514 --> 00:39:47,514
the Wonder Dogs their most
gut-wrenching loss last season.

869
00:39:50,581 --> 00:39:54,647
Now, they must face
that nightmare head-on, one year later.

870
00:39:55,214 --> 00:39:57,681
You could feel their presence
the moment they stepped in.

871
00:39:57,681 --> 00:40:00,081
They walked onto the court
without cracking a single smile.

872
00:40:01,947 --> 00:40:05,814
We'll match that energy
and keep our game faces on too.

873
00:40:11,914 --> 00:40:15,047
I have total confidence.

874
00:40:15,514 --> 00:40:18,581
Thousands of teams compete
in Haruko every January,

875
00:40:18,581 --> 00:40:19,981
and they finished second this year.

876
00:40:19,981 --> 00:40:21,247
That's impressive.

877
00:40:21,247 --> 00:40:23,747
They also finished third
at last year's Inter-High.

878
00:40:23,747 --> 00:40:25,447
They're still a formidable team.

879
00:40:25,447 --> 00:40:27,847
That means they'll be tough opponents.

880
00:40:31,819 --> 00:40:33,802
Let's start shouting
from practice and do great.

881
00:40:33,803 --> 00:40:35,536
- All right, let's go!
- All right, let's go!

882
00:40:37,769 --> 00:40:40,703
(They start warming up.)

883
00:40:45,510 --> 00:40:47,944
Everyone, speak up.

884
00:40:49,510 --> 00:40:51,877
Speak up properly!

885
00:40:56,677 --> 00:40:59,010
Move your feet!

886
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:00,944
I said move your feet!

887
00:41:00,944 --> 00:41:01,744
You're too slow.

888
00:41:08,510 --> 00:41:10,277
Get up. Quickly!

889
00:41:14,610 --> 00:41:16,444
(Spring up)

890
00:41:16,444 --> 00:41:18,577
(Quick wipe)

891
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:23,552
(With just a single word,)

892
00:41:23,577 --> 00:41:28,010
(everything gets done perfectly.)

893
00:41:30,644 --> 00:41:33,444
They operate like a textbook machine.

894
00:41:33,710 --> 00:41:35,444
Watching them run their drills,

895
00:41:35,844 --> 00:41:37,910
their team identity hasn't changed at all.

896
00:41:38,377 --> 00:41:41,277
Those girls were fierce.

897
00:41:41,544 --> 00:41:43,610
Young as they are,

898
00:41:43,610 --> 00:41:46,177
their mindset is purely professional.

899
00:41:46,177 --> 00:41:48,344
"Home or away, makes no difference."

900
00:41:48,344 --> 00:41:49,744
"We're here to play our game."

901
00:41:49,744 --> 00:41:52,977
You could see that swagger
in every movement.

902
00:41:53,910 --> 00:41:56,977
(We won't let you win.)

903
00:41:59,844 --> 00:42:01,710
(We won't just sit back.)

904
00:42:01,711 --> 00:42:02,865
Oh, my.

905
00:42:05,977 --> 00:42:08,777
Gosh. Oh my gosh.

906
00:42:09,542 --> 00:42:11,976
(The intensity is already
rising before the match.)

907
00:42:13,009 --> 00:42:14,209
My bad!

908
00:42:14,209 --> 00:42:18,276
Who should we highlight
on Shujitsu's roster?

909
00:42:19,242 --> 00:42:21,842
(On top of their impenetrable defense...)

910
00:42:21,842 --> 00:42:23,842
Their back-row defense is
already top-tier,

911
00:42:23,842 --> 00:42:26,509
but this year, they've added
more firepower on offense.

912
00:42:27,009 --> 00:42:28,042
(The leader of last year's reverse sweep)

913
00:42:28,042 --> 00:42:31,976
Yoshimoto Kanade is
already an excellent player.

914
00:42:31,976 --> 00:42:32,742
Exactly.

915
00:42:34,642 --> 00:42:37,009
I just got hit in the head.

916
00:42:37,742 --> 00:42:41,009
And Onishi Yukiji is a newcomer.

917
00:42:41,009 --> 00:42:44,376
Her skill ceiling is remarkable
for a first-year.

918
00:42:44,376 --> 00:42:46,409
She is so promising.

919
00:42:48,976 --> 00:42:51,509
It's crucial to figure out how to stop
their number one and two.

920
00:42:51,509 --> 00:42:52,909
Unbelievable.

921
00:42:52,909 --> 00:42:55,676
She's the one who won the award.

922
00:42:55,676 --> 00:42:57,409
- Is that her?
- Yes.

923
00:42:58,376 --> 00:43:00,642
I just got hit in the head
by their number one attacker.

924
00:43:00,642 --> 00:43:02,409
I got hit again.

925
00:43:03,076 --> 00:43:06,276
She's 2026 Nations Winter Cup MVP.

926
00:43:07,076 --> 00:43:09,909
(Shujitsu's dominant ace)

927
00:43:09,909 --> 00:43:11,742
I am the best in the world.

928
00:43:12,142 --> 00:43:15,409
I know Kim Yeon Koung held
the world's number one spot.

929
00:43:16,142 --> 00:43:17,742
I'm here to take...

930
00:43:18,976 --> 00:43:20,509
that crown from her.

931
00:43:21,742 --> 00:43:24,476
(Stares intently)

932
00:43:25,209 --> 00:43:27,942
(So it's you.)

933
00:43:28,209 --> 00:43:30,409
She claims she's the best in the world?

934
00:43:30,409 --> 00:43:32,442
I've sat at the very top plenty of times.

935
00:43:33,109 --> 00:43:34,642
From someone who lived it,

936
00:43:34,642 --> 00:43:36,109
staying there is another story.

937
00:43:37,442 --> 00:43:40,242
Onishi boldly declared that...

938
00:43:40,242 --> 00:43:42,276
she would take
the world's number one spot.

939
00:43:42,542 --> 00:43:46,242
Yeon Koung is keeping a close eye on her.

940
00:43:52,676 --> 00:43:55,109
It seems Yeon Koung is aware of her.

941
00:43:55,109 --> 00:43:56,309
Absolutely.

942
00:43:57,019 --> 00:43:58,910
Our players should be heading...

943
00:43:58,911 --> 00:44:00,846
into their opener riding high
on confidence,

944
00:44:00,847 --> 00:44:02,414
but we have some very disappointing news.

945
00:44:02,415 --> 00:44:04,148
I heard someone got injured
during training.

946
00:44:04,149 --> 00:44:05,350
That's right.

947
00:44:05,751 --> 00:44:08,853
- She had heavy tape around her knee.
- Right.

948
00:44:09,021 --> 00:44:13,524
Song Hee picked up an injury
and has been ruled out for today.

949
00:44:14,360 --> 00:44:17,195
(During yesterday's training)

950
00:44:18,598 --> 00:44:19,398
Wait.

951
00:44:19,999 --> 00:44:21,766
What's wrong?

952
00:44:23,836 --> 00:44:25,403
Hold on.

953
00:44:26,839 --> 00:44:27,605
It hurts.

954
00:44:27,606 --> 00:44:30,575
Don't move. Take it slow.

955
00:44:30,977 --> 00:44:31,976
What happened?

956
00:44:31,977 --> 00:44:33,077
It buckled.

957
00:44:33,078 --> 00:44:33,912
Hold on.

958
00:44:34,480 --> 00:44:36,580
Give her space.

959
00:44:36,581 --> 00:44:38,116
Let's give her some time.

960
00:44:38,418 --> 00:44:39,918
Take it slow.

961
00:44:41,521 --> 00:44:42,587
In 1, 2, 3.

962
00:44:43,823 --> 00:44:44,756
In 1, 2, 3.

963
00:44:44,757 --> 00:44:46,224
I'm so sorry.

964
00:44:50,196 --> 00:44:52,264
I think I was really shaken up.

965
00:44:52,265 --> 00:44:53,098
(An unexpected hole in the lineup)

966
00:44:53,099 --> 00:44:54,132
It's okay. Don't cry.

967
00:44:55,534 --> 00:45:00,338
(Song Hee was in even better shape
than last season.)

968
00:45:00,640 --> 00:45:03,342
She was one
of our strongest attacking options,

969
00:45:03,542 --> 00:45:05,076
so this is a pretty serious blow.

970
00:45:05,544 --> 00:45:08,213
Losing Song Hee leaves a glaring void.

971
00:45:08,582 --> 00:45:12,551
Her form was sharp enough to earn a spot
in the starting rotation,

972
00:45:12,853 --> 00:45:13,886
only for this injury to derail it.

973
00:45:15,588 --> 00:45:20,124
Coach Yeon Koung had high expectations
for Song Hee too,

974
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:21,826
so it's such a shame.

975
00:45:21,827 --> 00:45:24,162
Just imagine
how badly she must want to play.

976
00:45:24,163 --> 00:45:25,029
That's right.

977
00:45:25,030 --> 00:45:26,230
(An ace sidelined
before the opening whistle even blows.)

978
00:45:26,365 --> 00:45:28,399
On top of that, Seung Ju is not
on the floor this season either.

979
00:45:28,400 --> 00:45:29,334
Right.

980
00:45:29,468 --> 00:45:32,236
She was the undisputed go-to hitter,

981
00:45:32,237 --> 00:45:35,339
the anchor who shouldered the burden
whenever the team needed a clutch point.

982
00:45:36,208 --> 00:45:38,008
(Even so, there is still...)

983
00:45:38,009 --> 00:45:40,878
(unfinished business.)

984
00:45:41,547 --> 00:45:42,414
(A rematch they've waited a full year for)

985
00:45:42,415 --> 00:45:44,849
For the revenge on Shujitsu High School,

986
00:45:45,384 --> 00:45:48,186
we have game-planned for every scenario
from top to bottom.

987
00:45:48,187 --> 00:45:49,420
I believe we have what it takes.

988
00:45:50,523 --> 00:45:52,723
Our only goal today is to win.

989
00:45:52,724 --> 00:45:54,363
That's the one thing I've been focused on.

990
00:45:55,728 --> 00:45:58,329
They handed us that bitter defeat.

991
00:46:00,431 --> 00:46:02,500
And they have
one of the best hitters in the world.

992
00:46:02,501 --> 00:46:05,341
(Total powerhouse)

993
00:46:05,805 --> 00:46:07,072
Still, this is where the fun begins,

994
00:46:08,173 --> 00:46:09,207
so we'll just do it.

995
00:46:10,576 --> 00:46:11,509
We're definitely...

996
00:46:12,445 --> 00:46:13,412
going to win today.

997
00:46:14,613 --> 00:46:18,783
The rebuilt Pilseung Wonder Dogs take
the court for their season opener.

998
00:46:18,784 --> 00:46:20,518
(The first match begins.)

999
00:46:27,259 --> 00:46:28,859
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1000
00:46:28,860 --> 00:46:29,927
Louder!

1001
00:46:30,096 --> 00:46:32,797
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1002
00:46:39,138 --> 00:46:41,706
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1003
00:46:43,542 --> 00:46:45,743
Listen to that Wonder Dogs crowd!

1004
00:46:46,879 --> 00:46:49,180
Shujitsu's supporters brought
immense energy last year.

1005
00:46:49,181 --> 00:46:52,083
This time, however,
we are right here in Ansan.

1006
00:46:52,084 --> 00:46:54,553
- That's right.
- This is the Wonder Dogs' home floor.

1007
00:46:54,554 --> 00:46:56,955
A lot of the players' families are
here too.

1008
00:46:57,190 --> 00:46:58,857
And a lot of their friends came as well.

1009
00:46:58,959 --> 00:47:01,627
With all this support behind us,
we should be able...

1010
00:47:01,628 --> 00:47:03,328
to enjoy a bit of a home-court advantage.

1011
00:47:03,329 --> 00:47:05,163
If their families give them
that extra boost,

1012
00:47:05,430 --> 00:47:08,299
it'll help them find more energy
during the match.

1013
00:47:08,300 --> 00:47:10,501
(Go for it! Let's do this! No regrets!)

1014
00:47:11,771 --> 00:47:13,672
(Wonder Dogs)

1015
00:47:13,673 --> 00:47:15,607
(Let's go, Kim Bo Been!)

1016
00:47:15,941 --> 00:47:19,110
(The Wonder Dogs' family-and-friends
cheering squad is out in full force!)

1017
00:47:19,879 --> 00:47:22,147
Focus even harder
than you think you need to.

1018
00:47:22,148 --> 00:47:24,549
Block out whatever noise
comes from their side of the net.

1019
00:47:24,550 --> 00:47:26,488
Focus on what you have to do.

1020
00:47:26,489 --> 00:47:28,502
Come what may,
stick to our identity and play your game!

1021
00:47:29,355 --> 00:47:30,856
Even if you're on the road,
just play your game!

1022
00:47:30,857 --> 00:47:33,592
It is alright. The final result is not
what defines this moment.

1023
00:47:33,593 --> 00:47:36,528
Go out there, play with energy,
and show them some great volleyball!

1024
00:47:37,229 --> 00:47:38,930
Let's be vocal
and build the energy right away!

1025
00:47:38,931 --> 00:47:40,798
- All right! Let's go!
- All right! Let's go!

1026
00:47:43,135 --> 00:47:45,570
(Loud cheering)

1027
00:47:47,106 --> 00:47:49,174
(They bow...)

1028
00:47:49,175 --> 00:47:50,743
(and head onto the court.)

1029
00:47:50,744 --> 00:47:52,378
Don't forget
everything we've talked about.

1030
00:47:52,379 --> 00:47:54,045
Keep the communication loud
and active out there. Understood?

1031
00:47:54,046 --> 00:47:54,879
- Yes.
- Let's go.

1032
00:47:55,413 --> 00:47:57,648
- Pilseung!
- Wonder Dogs!

1033
00:48:00,820 --> 00:48:03,121
Let's take a look
at the Wonder Dogs' starting rotation.

1034
00:48:03,456 --> 00:48:04,988
Middle blocker Lee Ho Bin.

1035
00:48:04,989 --> 00:48:06,758
Opposite Yoon Young In.

1036
00:48:06,759 --> 00:48:08,593
Outside hitter Back Chae Rim.

1037
00:48:08,594 --> 00:48:10,261
Middle blocker Kim Bo Been.

1038
00:48:10,397 --> 00:48:11,597
Setter Ha Hyo Rim.

1039
00:48:11,598 --> 00:48:13,432
Outside hitter Enkhsoyol.

1040
00:48:13,433 --> 00:48:15,734
Liberos Chae Seon Ah and Seo Yu Kyung.

1041
00:48:17,603 --> 00:48:20,205
Here is
Shujitsu High School's starting rotation.

1042
00:48:20,539 --> 00:48:21,874
Setter Kato Uta.

1043
00:48:21,875 --> 00:48:24,142
Outside hitter Yoshimoto Kanade.

1044
00:48:24,143 --> 00:48:25,944
Middle blocker Miyake Hina.

1045
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:27,778
Opposite hitter Abe Mei.

1046
00:48:27,779 --> 00:48:30,114
Outside hitter Onishi Yukiji.

1047
00:48:30,115 --> 00:48:32,149
Middle blocker Miyamoto Rio.

1048
00:48:32,150 --> 00:48:34,118
Libero Hanbara Suzuko.

1049
00:48:39,158 --> 00:48:41,993
- Do you know about the Wonder Dogs' jinx?
- What is it?

1050
00:48:41,994 --> 00:48:44,362
In all seven matches last season,

1051
00:48:44,363 --> 00:48:46,931
they never once scored the opening point.

1052
00:48:46,932 --> 00:48:48,933
Oh, right.

1053
00:48:48,934 --> 00:48:50,268
And it didn't stop there.

1054
00:48:50,269 --> 00:48:53,404
They'd often fall behind,
sometimes even going down 0-7,

1055
00:48:53,405 --> 00:48:55,140
and had to fight their way back
into the match.

1056
00:48:55,141 --> 00:48:56,908
- That's right.
- So this time,

1057
00:48:57,244 --> 00:48:59,177
I really hope
they can get out in front early.

1058
00:48:59,178 --> 00:49:02,447
We'll have to see whether they can take...

1059
00:49:02,448 --> 00:49:04,015
an early lead this time.

1060
00:49:04,016 --> 00:49:06,484
(Can they finally score
the opening point this time?)

1061
00:49:07,753 --> 00:49:10,655
The Wonder Dogs are
about to turn a new page.

1062
00:49:11,257 --> 00:49:17,129
(Cheering)

1063
00:49:17,130 --> 00:49:18,363
The match begins.

1064
00:49:22,468 --> 00:49:23,668
They send it over.

1065
00:49:23,669 --> 00:49:24,469
Do it!

1066
00:49:25,404 --> 00:49:26,771
She keeps it alive with an underhand set.

1067
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:28,839
(They have to take the first point!)

1068
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:29,774
Spike!

1069
00:49:30,042 --> 00:49:31,709
- Do it!
- Get it up!

1070
00:49:31,710 --> 00:49:32,644
You need to go!

1071
00:49:33,922 --> 00:49:35,556
(Out)

1072
00:49:35,581 --> 00:49:36,481
It's out.

1073
00:49:39,151 --> 00:49:40,952
Sorry, guys.

1074
00:49:42,321 --> 00:49:45,323
(What a shame.)

1075
00:49:45,324 --> 00:49:46,391
It's okay.

1076
00:49:47,760 --> 00:49:50,462
Just take a little more time on the set.

1077
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:56,867
The second-ball connection wasn't clean,
and that led to the error.

1078
00:49:56,868 --> 00:49:58,069
(They give up the point
on a second-ball setting error.)

1079
00:49:58,738 --> 00:49:59,676
So once again,

1080
00:49:59,963 --> 00:50:02,673
they begin their first match
by giving up...

1081
00:50:02,674 --> 00:50:04,175
- the very opening point.
- They let it slip away.

1082
00:50:05,377 --> 00:50:08,412
- Gosh, I'm nervous.
- Settle down and provide cover!

1083
00:50:08,413 --> 00:50:10,049
- Immediately!
- Don't hesitate!

1084
00:50:10,050 --> 00:50:12,283
- Get it done!
- Move immediately!

1085
00:50:12,284 --> 00:50:13,362
I'll keep my eyes on the net.

1086
00:50:14,186 --> 00:50:16,287
(The answer is...)

1087
00:50:16,288 --> 00:50:19,257
Start with the basic play!

1088
00:50:19,658 --> 00:50:20,958
Okay! The basic!

1089
00:50:20,959 --> 00:50:21,792
(The core strategy is...)

1090
00:50:21,793 --> 00:50:22,827
I'll go.

1091
00:50:22,828 --> 00:50:23,694
(received loud and clear.)

1092
00:50:23,897 --> 00:50:25,696
It'll probably be an A.

1093
00:50:26,198 --> 00:50:28,266
- Okay.
- Okay, good.

1094
00:50:28,267 --> 00:50:29,233
Young In!

1095
00:50:29,234 --> 00:50:30,301
(Hand signal)

1096
00:50:30,869 --> 00:50:31,936
Short A.

1097
00:50:31,937 --> 00:50:34,371
- Chae Rim.
- Enkhsoyol.

1098
00:50:34,473 --> 00:50:36,407
Push it toward the net!

1099
00:50:36,408 --> 00:50:37,642
(Hyo Rim, the setter,
calls out the A play.)

1100
00:50:40,145 --> 00:50:41,946
(Number One, Yoshimoto Kanade)

1101
00:50:44,950 --> 00:50:46,317
- Now!
- She receives it safely.

1102
00:50:48,420 --> 00:50:49,153
Pass!

1103
00:50:49,455 --> 00:50:50,989
(That's it!)

1104
00:50:53,525 --> 00:50:54,758
Spike!

1105
00:50:55,027 --> 00:50:56,027
Chae Rim scores!

1106
00:50:56,328 --> 00:50:58,329
(Chae Rim puts the attack away.)

1107
00:50:58,831 --> 00:51:01,365
(The Wonder Dogs' first point
of Season Two)

1108
00:51:01,366 --> 00:51:04,736
An immediate answer from the Wonder Dogs
this time around.

1109
00:51:04,737 --> 00:51:05,737
Right on!

1110
00:51:07,940 --> 00:51:10,408
Hyo Rim, nice set!

1111
00:51:12,811 --> 00:51:14,121
Setter distribution...

1112
00:51:15,215 --> 00:51:16,577
That will be the deciding factor.

1113
00:51:16,915 --> 00:51:18,849
That's why, against Shujitsu,

1114
00:51:18,850 --> 00:51:22,086
you always have to think
about setting the ball farther out.

1115
00:51:22,087 --> 00:51:24,688
So, off an A, go to a C.
Off a B, go to a back C...

1116
00:51:24,689 --> 00:51:27,091
(A, B, C?)

1117
00:51:28,794 --> 00:51:33,798
(A, B, and C refer
to different types of sets.)

1118
00:51:34,099 --> 00:51:38,135
(Classified by the distance
of the set from the setter)

1119
00:51:39,104 --> 00:51:42,506
(A set: approximately 1m)

1120
00:51:43,909 --> 00:51:47,745
(B set: approximately 2m)

1121
00:51:48,380 --> 00:51:52,817
(C set: approximately 3m or more)

1122
00:51:54,186 --> 00:52:02,060
(Back sets are likewise classified
as back A, back B, and back C.)

1123
00:52:02,194 --> 00:52:05,263
(So what exactly is
the "A-to-C" strategy?)

1124
00:52:06,532 --> 00:52:10,635
(Also known
as the "blocker bait" strategy)

1125
00:52:11,036 --> 00:52:18,142
(The setter uses a decoy hitter...)

1126
00:52:18,544 --> 00:52:23,448
(to pull the opposing middle blocker
out of position.)

1127
00:52:23,749 --> 00:52:24,849
(Selling the jump
as if committing to the A quick)

1128
00:52:24,850 --> 00:52:26,851
Once the middle commits to the quick...

1129
00:52:28,353 --> 00:52:31,088
(After drawing the opposing blocker in)

1130
00:52:31,089 --> 00:52:34,058
You release the C ball with pace,
driving it clear to the antenna.

1131
00:52:34,059 --> 00:52:35,292
(The real set fires out
to the C on the pin.)

1132
00:52:35,427 --> 00:52:37,462
How many blockers is
our outside hitter looking at then?

1133
00:52:37,463 --> 00:52:38,463
(She bought the fake!)

1134
00:52:38,831 --> 00:52:39,831
Just one.

1135
00:52:39,832 --> 00:52:42,200
(A one-on-one blocking situation!)

1136
00:52:43,402 --> 00:52:45,837
(An easy kill)

1137
00:52:46,605 --> 00:52:47,638
Off a B, go to a back C...

1138
00:52:47,639 --> 00:52:48,673
(The same goes
for a B-to-back-C combination.)

1139
00:52:49,097 --> 00:52:53,010
(Selling the B set...)

1140
00:52:53,011 --> 00:52:55,379
(to draw the blocker in)

1141
00:52:55,380 --> 00:52:57,114
Keep pushing the set all the way out.

1142
00:52:57,115 --> 00:52:58,415
In the actual game too. Okay?

1143
00:52:58,617 --> 00:53:01,118
(She falls for it again!)

1144
00:53:01,753 --> 00:53:04,622
(An easy point...)

1145
00:53:04,623 --> 00:53:07,223
(against a single blocker)

1146
00:53:07,224 --> 00:53:09,493
That's exactly why we practiced this.

1147
00:53:09,494 --> 00:53:11,528
(Wonder Coach's tactical blueprint
pays off early)

1148
00:53:13,391 --> 00:53:14,825
(Replaying the scoring sequence
from moments ago)

1149
00:53:14,833 --> 00:53:15,733
(Bait)

1150
00:53:15,734 --> 00:53:17,902
(Using the A quick as the decoy runner)

1151
00:53:18,337 --> 00:53:20,772
(The bait goes up...)

1152
00:53:20,773 --> 00:53:22,640
(above the net!)

1153
00:53:22,641 --> 00:53:23,810
(I told you so.)

1154
00:53:23,811 --> 00:53:26,544
The blocker can't close over in time.

1155
00:53:26,545 --> 00:53:27,545
That's right.

1156
00:53:27,546 --> 00:53:28,646
(Bait taken!)

1157
00:53:29,014 --> 00:53:31,349
(The ball shoots wide to the C
on the outside pin.)

1158
00:53:31,583 --> 00:53:33,918
(Open court!)

1159
00:53:34,219 --> 00:53:37,588
They isolate a single blocker
and convert the kill with authority.

1160
00:53:39,691 --> 00:53:41,058
Sorry.

1161
00:53:41,059 --> 00:53:43,427
Blockers, stay disciplined on both pins!

1162
00:53:43,962 --> 00:53:45,897
Keep talking to each other!

1163
00:53:45,898 --> 00:53:47,164
That's it!

1164
00:53:47,165 --> 00:53:49,166
(The setter's decisions can determine
the flow of the match.)

1165
00:53:49,167 --> 00:53:51,369
Hyo Rim, give your sets just a touch
more height across the board.

1166
00:53:51,370 --> 00:53:53,137
Their blocker is still committing
hard to the A quick.

1167
00:53:53,406 --> 00:53:54,939
It's okay to show the A first
and then switch to another option.

1168
00:53:54,940 --> 00:53:56,040
A back set, for example.

1169
00:53:56,708 --> 00:53:57,543
Okay!

1170
00:53:57,544 --> 00:53:58,427
Enkhsoyol!

1171
00:53:58,428 --> 00:53:59,700
(We fight back with our setters.)

1172
00:53:59,700 --> 00:54:02,067
I heard Coach Kim
has trained setters extensively.

1173
00:54:02,067 --> 00:54:03,167
That's right.

1174
00:54:04,244 --> 00:54:05,866
(Cheer for Young In)

1175
00:54:05,867 --> 00:54:07,400
- Yoon Young In!
- Yoon Young In!

1176
00:54:08,434 --> 00:54:09,800
It's 1 to 1.

1177
00:54:09,800 --> 00:54:11,834
Young In of the Wonder Dogs serves.

1178
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:16,500
(After a clean pass,)

1179
00:54:17,167 --> 00:54:19,467
(Onishi steps up.)

1180
00:54:19,534 --> 00:54:20,700
And a straight shot!

1181
00:54:24,434 --> 00:54:25,500
She digs it out.

1182
00:54:25,734 --> 00:54:26,867
A line shot!

1183
00:54:26,867 --> 00:54:28,634
She defends. Another tip.

1184
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:30,200
Slow down!

1185
00:54:30,200 --> 00:54:32,367
High ball! Hit it deep!

1186
00:54:32,834 --> 00:54:34,600
(A high ball means a high-arcing set.)

1187
00:54:34,600 --> 00:54:35,700
Hyo Rim's underhand toss.

1188
00:54:35,700 --> 00:54:37,200
Swing with confidence!

1189
00:54:38,100 --> 00:54:40,134
A powerful smash!

1190
00:54:40,134 --> 00:54:41,167
(Counterattack)

1191
00:54:41,167 --> 00:54:43,434
That's it!

1192
00:54:45,300 --> 00:54:47,500
Chae Rim goes on a scoring run.

1193
00:54:47,500 --> 00:54:49,567
(Chae Rim scores two points in a row.)

1194
00:54:50,934 --> 00:54:54,000
If you see a chance to score,
call for the ball!

1195
00:54:54,000 --> 00:54:55,034
Chae Rim!

1196
00:54:55,034 --> 00:54:56,300
(Good.)

1197
00:54:56,967 --> 00:54:59,467
- Bo Been, wait! They're going wide.
- Yes, Coach!

1198
00:55:00,367 --> 00:55:01,900
It's okay! One point at a time!

1199
00:55:03,134 --> 00:55:05,200
- There goes number two.
- Got it.

1200
00:55:05,200 --> 00:55:06,200
(Watch out for number two.)

1201
00:55:06,200 --> 00:55:08,000
Bo Been, number two!

1202
00:55:08,600 --> 00:55:10,167
Watch number two first!

1203
00:55:10,734 --> 00:55:11,734
Okay!

1204
00:55:11,734 --> 00:55:13,200
(Number two...)

1205
00:55:13,200 --> 00:55:14,934
(checked.)

1206
00:55:15,100 --> 00:55:16,500
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1207
00:55:17,500 --> 00:55:18,534
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1208
00:55:18,534 --> 00:55:19,600
It's 2 to 1.

1209
00:55:22,167 --> 00:55:23,200
Number two!

1210
00:55:24,600 --> 00:55:27,200
(As expected,
the ball is fed to number two.)

1211
00:55:29,300 --> 00:55:30,334
Spike!

1212
00:55:31,034 --> 00:55:32,267
Onishi Yukiji.

1213
00:55:32,267 --> 00:55:34,567
(Onishi Yukiji scores.)

1214
00:55:34,567 --> 00:55:35,600
My bad.

1215
00:55:36,067 --> 00:55:38,500
(They scored despite being read.)

1216
00:55:38,767 --> 00:55:40,367
I'm the best in the world.

1217
00:55:41,167 --> 00:55:42,667
- Sorry.
- It's fine!

1218
00:55:43,200 --> 00:55:44,867
- That was too fast.
- Yes, Coach!

1219
00:55:45,476 --> 00:55:46,599
We read them, though.

1220
00:55:46,600 --> 00:55:47,634
What a shame.

1221
00:55:47,634 --> 00:55:48,767
We could've scored.

1222
00:55:54,934 --> 00:55:56,034
Eyes on number two!

1223
00:55:57,467 --> 00:55:58,467
Number two!

1224
00:55:59,567 --> 00:56:01,000
A deep, direct attack!

1225
00:56:01,500 --> 00:56:02,500
(Onishi terminates.)

1226
00:56:02,500 --> 00:56:04,067
She scored with a straight shot.

1227
00:56:04,067 --> 00:56:06,134
(Bo Been's parents in the stands)

1228
00:56:06,134 --> 00:56:09,234
Onishi's attacks sure are powerful.

1229
00:56:09,234 --> 00:56:10,867
Yes. It's still early in the match,

1230
00:56:10,867 --> 00:56:14,134
but her attacks are
unbelievably aggressive...

1231
00:56:14,134 --> 00:56:16,400
for a tenth grader.

1232
00:56:16,400 --> 00:56:17,600
Number two!

1233
00:56:18,000 --> 00:56:20,467
Watch number two!

1234
00:56:20,834 --> 00:56:21,900
Number two, C!

1235
00:56:21,900 --> 00:56:23,367
They keep setting her up.

1236
00:56:23,368 --> 00:56:25,191
- We should watch number two.
- Eyes on number two!

1237
00:56:25,192 --> 00:56:26,223
(Onishi alert here and there)

1238
00:56:29,300 --> 00:56:30,967
(The libero's perfect reception)

1239
00:56:32,134 --> 00:56:33,434
There! Number two!

1240
00:56:34,067 --> 00:56:36,634
- Number two is hitting it!
- Number two!

1241
00:56:40,467 --> 00:56:41,534
Spike!

1242
00:56:41,534 --> 00:56:42,734
(First set, Shujitsu High 4
: Wonder Dogs 3)

1243
00:56:44,700 --> 00:56:46,067
I'm sorry.

1244
00:56:46,067 --> 00:56:47,300
(Scoring three points alone)

1245
00:56:48,500 --> 00:56:49,734
Man, seriously.

1246
00:56:50,934 --> 00:56:52,767
(Chuckling)

1247
00:56:53,400 --> 00:56:54,767
Onishi unleashes her explosive power...

1248
00:56:54,767 --> 00:56:56,667
bent on claiming Coach Kim's throne.

1249
00:56:57,134 --> 00:56:58,500
Stay calm. It's okay.

1250
00:56:58,500 --> 00:57:00,534
Whenever Onishi scores,

1251
00:57:00,534 --> 00:57:03,934
- Coach Kim seems to keep her in check.
- All right!

1252
00:57:05,300 --> 00:57:06,334
Yes!

1253
00:57:07,167 --> 00:57:10,834
Even I was surprised
at how good number two was,

1254
00:57:10,834 --> 00:57:14,834
especially her outstanding attacks.

1255
00:57:15,300 --> 00:57:19,800
There were so many times
when she was on a scoring streak.

1256
00:57:20,667 --> 00:57:21,834
"I am the best in the world."

1257
00:57:22,167 --> 00:57:23,434
"I'm ready today. Bring it."

1258
00:57:23,900 --> 00:57:26,434
I guess that's
where her confidence comes from.

1259
00:57:28,334 --> 00:57:31,634
I had to admit it.

1260
00:57:32,334 --> 00:57:35,967
(The next-generation number one
challenges the all-time number one.)

1261
00:57:36,300 --> 00:57:38,300
(The veteran coach chooses to...)

1262
00:57:38,300 --> 00:57:40,567
Hey! Why are you in a rush?

1263
00:57:40,567 --> 00:57:41,667
Slow down.

1264
00:57:41,667 --> 00:57:43,500
Check who's in front of you.

1265
00:57:43,500 --> 00:57:44,600
- Yes!
- Yes, Coach.

1266
00:57:44,600 --> 00:57:45,600
Sorry.

1267
00:57:45,734 --> 00:57:47,367
Guys, slow down!

1268
00:57:48,934 --> 00:57:53,034
(Abe Mei serves.)

1269
00:57:55,334 --> 00:57:57,167
- Seon Ah, Hyo Rim.
- Hit it!

1270
00:57:57,434 --> 00:57:58,500
A right-side attack.

1271
00:57:59,367 --> 00:58:00,467
(Long!)

1272
00:58:00,467 --> 00:58:01,600
There!

1273
00:58:02,034 --> 00:58:03,567
- Over!
- Over!

1274
00:58:03,567 --> 00:58:04,567
It's coming over!

1275
00:58:05,000 --> 00:58:06,300
Why are you in a rush?

1276
00:58:06,300 --> 00:58:07,367
(Judge slowly.)

1277
00:58:07,367 --> 00:58:09,000
Check who's in front of you.

1278
00:58:09,971 --> 00:58:11,534
(Attack fast.)

1279
00:58:11,534 --> 00:58:12,534
She scores.

1280
00:58:13,467 --> 00:58:15,500
Bo Been scored with a direct smash.

1281
00:58:15,500 --> 00:58:16,667
- Nice, Bo Been!
- Way to go!

1282
00:58:17,300 --> 00:58:18,667
(Satisfied)

1283
00:58:23,067 --> 00:58:24,734
(It's a tie again!)

1284
00:58:25,267 --> 00:58:27,144
(Bo Been's dad)

1285
00:58:27,534 --> 00:58:29,234
(Bo Been serves.)

1286
00:58:32,067 --> 00:58:33,934
(Onishi again?)

1287
00:58:33,934 --> 00:58:35,500
Watch number seven.

1288
00:58:36,367 --> 00:58:37,500
Number seven!

1289
00:58:38,100 --> 00:58:39,134
(Whistling)

1290
00:58:40,167 --> 00:58:42,067
(The Wonder Dogs concede a point.)

1291
00:58:42,267 --> 00:58:45,900
Why did you touch the net?

1292
00:58:45,900 --> 00:58:47,134
Slow down.

1293
00:58:48,300 --> 00:58:50,634
She's calling out the Wonder Dogs' error.

1294
00:58:50,634 --> 00:58:53,200
(Net touch: a fault for touching the net
during play)

1295
00:58:53,200 --> 00:58:55,467
Enkhsoyol gets called
for the net violation.

1296
00:58:57,167 --> 00:58:58,667
- My bad.
- Slowly. Nice defense.

1297
00:58:58,667 --> 00:59:00,700
- Get this point!
- Next one!

1298
00:59:00,700 --> 00:59:01,900
It's 5 to 4, one point apart.

1299
00:59:01,900 --> 00:59:02,900
How intense.

1300
00:59:05,279 --> 00:59:06,800
(Onishi prepares to serve.)

1301
00:59:06,800 --> 00:59:09,200
Onishi Yukiji gets ready to serve.

1302
00:59:12,800 --> 00:59:14,100
She serves short. Step up!

1303
00:59:14,100 --> 00:59:15,167
To the attack line!

1304
00:59:15,167 --> 00:59:16,200
Position!

1305
00:59:16,200 --> 00:59:19,300
(Red alert for Onishi)

1306
00:59:19,300 --> 00:59:23,300
- I remember she had a tricky serve.
- You're right.

1307
00:59:23,700 --> 00:59:28,567
I don't think the Wonder Dogs
can dig Onishi's serve.

1308
00:59:28,867 --> 00:59:31,367
They need to be ready
when Onishi steps up to serve.

1309
00:59:32,174 --> 00:59:34,074
(Smiling)

1310
00:59:35,234 --> 00:59:37,167
Serve hard, as usual.

1311
00:59:37,167 --> 00:59:38,167
Yes!

1312
00:59:39,334 --> 00:59:41,334
(Ready to unleash a cannon)

1313
00:59:41,700 --> 00:59:43,800
Serve, Yukiji!

1314
00:59:45,067 --> 00:59:47,467
She's a bit quick.

1315
00:59:50,734 --> 00:59:55,034
Onishi's serve is her ultimate weapon.

1316
01:00:00,067 --> 01:00:01,100
A fierce spike!

1317
01:00:01,334 --> 01:00:02,634
No.

1318
01:00:04,100 --> 01:00:06,267
(They barely pop it up.)

1319
01:00:06,800 --> 01:00:07,934
It immediately goes over.

1320
01:00:07,934 --> 01:00:08,967
(But it goes over right away.)

1321
01:00:08,967 --> 01:00:09,967
Kato Uta.

1322
01:00:10,400 --> 01:00:11,834
A spike down the middle!

1323
01:00:13,034 --> 01:00:15,334
(Off Enkhsoyol's hand)

1324
01:00:15,334 --> 01:00:19,567
(Block touch out)

1325
01:00:20,300 --> 01:00:22,100
Bo Been, watch for short serves!

1326
01:00:22,700 --> 01:00:24,034
Enkhsoyol, call the play!

1327
01:00:24,800 --> 01:00:25,867
It had great power...

1328
01:00:26,234 --> 01:00:28,267
and was very effective
when it came to attacks.

1329
01:00:28,900 --> 01:00:30,173
Whoa, what's with that serve?

1330
01:00:30,416 --> 01:00:31,582
How's that possible?

1331
01:00:33,034 --> 01:00:36,100
That was Onishi Yukiji's serve.

1332
01:00:36,100 --> 01:00:39,600
Yes. She's an impressive server too.

1333
01:00:39,600 --> 01:00:40,600
(Scored with a hard serve)

1334
01:00:40,600 --> 01:00:42,800
Chae Rim, it's okay. Focus again.

1335
01:00:42,800 --> 01:00:44,600
Number two was so good.

1336
01:00:44,600 --> 01:00:48,867
She seemed to have great control
to mess with her opponents.

1337
01:00:50,367 --> 01:00:51,700
That was a monster serve,

1338
01:00:52,467 --> 01:00:55,967
and Shujitsu High School now leads 6 to 4.

1339
01:00:56,967 --> 01:01:01,567
We may have struggled
with number two's serve,

1340
01:01:02,167 --> 01:01:05,367
but the setters
and I have prepared a lot for this.

1341
01:01:05,367 --> 01:01:08,067
So I believe we'll do just fine.

1342
01:01:09,467 --> 01:01:11,534
We're sticking to our plan. It's okay.

1343
01:01:11,534 --> 01:01:12,667
Okay!

1344
01:01:12,967 --> 01:01:14,767
Let's get one point right away!

1345
01:01:14,767 --> 01:01:15,767
(Do what we've prepared.)

1346
01:01:15,767 --> 01:01:17,434
It's fine. We just have to score!

1347
01:01:19,867 --> 01:01:20,900
Young In!

1348
01:01:21,367 --> 01:01:23,034
Chae Rim!

1349
01:01:43,234 --> 01:01:44,267
Another hard serve.

1350
01:01:44,600 --> 01:01:45,734
Good reception this time.

1351
01:01:46,100 --> 01:01:48,967
(Open space!)

1352
01:01:49,300 --> 01:01:52,100
(The decoy runner goes up.)

1353
01:01:53,267 --> 01:01:55,200
(Bit on the fake!)

1354
01:01:55,200 --> 01:01:56,534
Okay!

1355
01:01:56,534 --> 01:01:58,867
(Going for the right side!)

1356
01:01:59,400 --> 01:02:01,367
(Stopping suddenly)

1357
01:02:01,834 --> 01:02:03,000
Back C!

1358
01:02:03,000 --> 01:02:04,667
(A bad toss?)

1359
01:02:14,067 --> 01:02:15,667
A fake back set!

1360
01:02:16,667 --> 01:02:17,867
Bravo!

1361
01:02:19,400 --> 01:02:20,400
Let's go!

1362
01:02:21,467 --> 01:02:23,167
(Let's go!)

1363
01:02:23,167 --> 01:02:24,700
(Let's go, my girl!)

1364
01:02:24,700 --> 01:02:26,434
Nice!

1365
01:02:27,267 --> 01:02:28,267
Nice!

1366
01:02:28,267 --> 01:02:29,834
(The mood changes after one shot.)

1367
01:02:30,767 --> 01:02:32,667
She found the open space perfectly.

1368
01:02:32,667 --> 01:02:34,434
Hyo Rim is good at that.

1369
01:02:34,434 --> 01:02:35,967
- That's true.
- All right.

1370
01:02:37,334 --> 01:02:39,300
She had that open space in mind...

1371
01:02:39,300 --> 01:02:40,800
- when she attacked.
- Yes.

1372
01:02:40,800 --> 01:02:43,067
She made it look like a regular set.

1373
01:02:43,067 --> 01:02:44,100
Of course, they fell for it.

1374
01:02:44,100 --> 01:02:45,100
Exactly.

1375
01:02:46,800 --> 01:02:47,867
Awesome!

1376
01:02:47,867 --> 01:02:48,867
(Speechless)

1377
01:02:49,934 --> 01:02:52,800
- Onishi looks a bit flustered.
- She does.

1378
01:02:53,667 --> 01:02:54,834
It felt great...

1379
01:02:54,834 --> 01:02:57,767
to take a risk
when we were at a disadvantage.

1380
01:02:57,767 --> 01:02:59,134
Hyo Rim, nice!

1381
01:03:00,867 --> 01:03:02,567
I thought this would definitely work.

1382
01:03:02,567 --> 01:03:03,667
(Hyo Rim's bold move)

1383
01:03:04,267 --> 01:03:06,234
(Followed by the fake pass
that earns a round of applause,)

1384
01:03:06,234 --> 01:03:08,267
Hyo Rim, way to go!

1385
01:03:08,267 --> 01:03:09,367
Great one, Hyo Rim!

1386
01:03:09,367 --> 01:03:10,567
(Hyo Rim serves this time.)

1387
01:03:11,367 --> 01:03:12,900
It's 6 to 5, one point apart.

1388
01:03:15,234 --> 01:03:17,967
(Roaring)

1389
01:03:17,967 --> 01:03:19,000
Hyo Rim serves.

1390
01:03:19,000 --> 01:03:20,534
That's it. Nice serve.

1391
01:03:20,534 --> 01:03:21,600
Shaky pass off the platform.

1392
01:03:21,867 --> 01:03:22,967
(Out of system)

1393
01:03:22,967 --> 01:03:24,300
Number one is going for it!

1394
01:03:24,300 --> 01:03:25,467
(A set to number one)

1395
01:03:30,600 --> 01:03:31,600
It drops again.

1396
01:03:31,600 --> 01:03:32,834
(Yoshimoto scores.)

1397
01:03:32,834 --> 01:03:33,934
Nice!

1398
01:03:33,934 --> 01:03:36,000
She is quite a threat too.

1399
01:03:36,000 --> 01:03:37,034
Indeed.

1400
01:03:38,067 --> 01:03:41,567
(They forgot about number one,
the other ace.)

1401
01:03:42,900 --> 01:03:44,067
Even if they shut down one side,

1402
01:03:44,067 --> 01:03:46,467
- the other gets to strike.
- That's right.

1403
01:03:46,467 --> 01:03:47,467
(They have two aces.)

1404
01:03:47,467 --> 01:03:49,767
Shujitsu's two weapons sure are scary.

1405
01:03:49,767 --> 01:03:52,100
Hyo Rim, there's A!

1406
01:03:52,100 --> 01:03:54,167
Ho Bin, run A!

1407
01:03:54,734 --> 01:03:58,046
(Preparing to fool the blockers again)

1408
01:03:58,522 --> 01:04:00,436
It's a 7 to 5 ball game now,
with a 2-point gap.

1409
01:04:02,028 --> 01:04:02,861
Put it away!

1410
01:04:02,862 --> 01:04:03,795
- Mine!
- An overhand reception.

1411
01:04:03,796 --> 01:04:04,697
(A decoy)

1412
01:04:04,698 --> 01:04:05,688
Go!

1413
01:04:06,070 --> 01:04:06,903
Hit it!

1414
01:04:06,904 --> 01:04:07,737
(Flailing)

1415
01:04:07,772 --> 01:04:08,838
They took the bait.

1416
01:04:09,373 --> 01:04:10,640
Set a C!

1417
01:04:11,275 --> 01:04:12,302
Push the C!

1418
01:04:12,644 --> 01:04:13,644
Hit it!

1419
01:04:13,645 --> 01:04:15,512
Put it away. Now!

1420
01:04:15,746 --> 01:04:16,679
A spike!

1421
01:04:19,016 --> 01:04:20,350
(That felt good!)

1422
01:04:20,351 --> 01:04:21,751
- Nice!
- Keep it up!

1423
01:04:21,986 --> 01:04:22,919
That's it!

1424
01:04:22,920 --> 01:04:24,801
(The blockers fall for every decoy.)

1425
01:04:25,851 --> 01:04:26,984
(Falling for the decoy...)

1426
01:04:26,985 --> 01:04:29,754
(yet again)

1427
01:04:30,089 --> 01:04:33,488
(No blockers in sight?)

1428
01:04:33,552 --> 01:04:35,319
(Thanks for the opening!)

1429
01:04:35,995 --> 01:04:38,396
You got the block wrong again.

1430
01:04:38,731 --> 01:04:40,065
Jump for the A again.

1431
01:04:40,066 --> 01:04:42,967
(Hyo Rim, the master of the decoy)

1432
01:04:43,869 --> 01:04:47,271
(Against number two's powerful serve,)

1433
01:04:47,272 --> 01:04:50,074
(she responds with a clever set.)

1434
01:04:50,576 --> 01:04:53,879
(Against number one's powerful spike,)

1435
01:04:53,880 --> 01:04:56,681
(she fools the blockers again.)

1436
01:04:57,984 --> 01:05:00,118
(Will it be the hitter...)

1437
01:05:00,419 --> 01:05:02,787
(or the setter?)

1438
01:05:02,788 --> 01:05:04,722
Go right away!

1439
01:05:04,723 --> 01:05:07,626
(A fierce, evenly matched rally)

1440
01:05:07,627 --> 01:05:10,695
Young In, you can pull it.

1441
01:05:10,830 --> 01:05:14,666
Get it together! Stop giving up points.
Play some defense.

1442
01:05:15,569 --> 01:05:16,835
It's 7 to 6. A 1-point game.

1443
01:05:16,836 --> 01:05:17,769
(Back to a one-point game)

1444
01:05:17,770 --> 01:05:19,238
Now Enkhsoyol steps up to serve.

1445
01:05:19,239 --> 01:05:20,072
(Enkhsoyol serves.)

1446
01:05:22,742 --> 01:05:25,110
Kato Uta with the back set.
A powerful spike up the middle!

1447
01:05:25,411 --> 01:05:27,379
Yu Kyung takes the second contact.

1448
01:05:27,380 --> 01:05:28,346
Send it over.

1449
01:05:28,915 --> 01:05:29,948
They send it over for now.

1450
01:05:29,949 --> 01:05:31,016
(Hesitating)

1451
01:05:31,017 --> 01:05:32,217
Abe Mei receives the ball.

1452
01:05:32,218 --> 01:05:33,018
No touch.

1453
01:05:33,586 --> 01:05:35,386
Yu Kyung digs it again.

1454
01:05:35,988 --> 01:05:37,255
Chae Rim hammers it!

1455
01:05:37,256 --> 01:05:38,957
(The fierce rally continues.)

1456
01:05:39,492 --> 01:05:40,325
Middle!

1457
01:05:40,593 --> 01:05:41,426
Block!

1458
01:05:41,427 --> 01:05:42,260
(Another chance for the Wonder Dogs)

1459
01:05:42,261 --> 01:05:43,428
Give me a B set!

1460
01:05:44,397 --> 01:05:45,697
Coming from the right.

1461
01:05:45,931 --> 01:05:47,465
That's it.

1462
01:05:47,466 --> 01:05:48,433
Nice!

1463
01:05:48,634 --> 01:05:49,367
The right side.

1464
01:05:49,368 --> 01:05:50,368
Do it again!

1465
01:05:50,369 --> 01:05:51,569
Set it to Young In.

1466
01:05:52,071 --> 01:05:53,239
Behind you!

1467
01:05:53,240 --> 01:05:54,406
Where will it go?

1468
01:05:54,407 --> 01:05:55,340
(To the right?)

1469
01:05:55,341 --> 01:05:57,042
- Hit it!
- A back-row attack up the middle!

1470
01:05:57,443 --> 01:05:58,743
(So close!)

1471
01:05:59,545 --> 01:06:00,478
(Shujitsu gets the next chance.)

1472
01:06:00,479 --> 01:06:01,780
They keep it alive.

1473
01:06:01,781 --> 01:06:03,148
(Yoshimoto fires a powerful spike.)

1474
01:06:03,149 --> 01:06:04,015
And this one...

1475
01:06:04,650 --> 01:06:06,684
They can't stop it.

1476
01:06:07,219 --> 01:06:08,820
Yoshimoto Kanade scores.

1477
01:06:08,821 --> 01:06:13,791
(A point lost after a hard-fought rally)

1478
01:06:14,761 --> 01:06:16,928
Shujitsu takes an 8-6 lead,

1479
01:06:17,096 --> 01:06:19,898
and we reach the first technical timeout
of the first set.

1480
01:06:22,068 --> 01:06:23,201
(Turning to the side)

1481
01:06:23,469 --> 01:06:24,903
(Sneaking a glance)

1482
01:06:27,907 --> 01:06:30,108
Until we build a bigger lead,

1483
01:06:30,109 --> 01:06:31,576
stick to high-percentage shots.

1484
01:06:31,577 --> 01:06:32,577
Yes, Coach.

1485
01:06:32,745 --> 01:06:34,512
You can be more deliberate
with your shots.

1486
01:06:34,513 --> 01:06:36,181
(Nodding)

1487
01:06:37,983 --> 01:06:41,786
Know exactly what we're supposed to do,
and don't let your guard down.

1488
01:06:43,522 --> 01:06:44,222
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1489
01:06:44,890 --> 01:06:47,892
Keep talking to each other out there.

1490
01:06:49,362 --> 01:06:50,395
Shujitsu High...

1491
01:06:50,596 --> 01:06:53,698
leads the Wonder Dogs by two points.

1492
01:06:53,699 --> 01:06:54,666
(First set,
Shujitsu High 8 : Wonder Dogs 6)

1493
01:07:00,974 --> 01:07:03,875
Shujitsu captain Kato Uta steps up
to serve.

1494
01:07:08,114 --> 01:07:09,514
A shaky reception.

1495
01:07:09,982 --> 01:07:11,316
(A faint smile)

1496
01:07:12,485 --> 01:07:14,386
Hyo Rim tips it to the right.

1497
01:07:14,687 --> 01:07:15,887
Oh, come on.

1498
01:07:16,922 --> 01:07:18,390
Hanbara gets it up.

1499
01:07:19,658 --> 01:07:20,391
(Yoshimoto tips it.)

1500
01:07:20,392 --> 01:07:21,192
Quick!

1501
01:07:21,193 --> 01:07:22,593
She drops to her knees for the dig.

1502
01:07:22,660 --> 01:07:23,860
Seon Ah with the second contact.

1503
01:07:24,563 --> 01:07:25,429
The spike!

1504
01:07:27,066 --> 01:07:28,366
It's out.

1505
01:07:30,169 --> 01:07:30,935
Enkhsoyol.

1506
01:07:32,304 --> 01:07:34,206
That serve wasn't even hard.
Move your feet.

1507
01:07:34,207 --> 01:07:35,007
Yes, Coach.

1508
01:07:36,343 --> 01:07:39,511
Hyo Rim, what set should you use
to get Young In involved?

1509
01:07:39,612 --> 01:07:41,280
- An A.
- Why an A? It's a B.

1510
01:07:41,281 --> 01:07:43,181
I told you not to back-set an A.

1511
01:07:43,182 --> 01:07:44,049
Understood.

1512
01:07:44,050 --> 01:07:45,784
(Frustrated)

1513
01:07:46,418 --> 01:07:48,052
(A short set to the right...)

1514
01:07:48,654 --> 01:07:50,188
(draws two blockers.)

1515
01:07:50,956 --> 01:07:53,491
(The decoy fails.)

1516
01:07:54,160 --> 01:07:58,263
(To draw the blockers away,
the set has to go farther.)

1517
01:07:59,098 --> 01:08:01,132
An attack error makes it 9 to 6.
Shujitsu leads by 3.

1518
01:08:03,869 --> 01:08:05,703
Serve to the same spot.

1519
01:08:08,340 --> 01:08:09,807
(Got it.)

1520
01:08:10,442 --> 01:08:13,010
That was a missed opportunity.
We need the points.

1521
01:08:13,011 --> 01:08:15,212
Keep your feet moving.

1522
01:08:15,781 --> 01:08:17,982
(Kato Uta serves again.)

1523
01:08:18,284 --> 01:08:19,017
Mine!

1524
01:08:19,018 --> 01:08:20,485
Enkhsoyol struggles
with the reception again.

1525
01:08:20,486 --> 01:08:22,320
- Mine!
- Cover!

1526
01:08:23,255 --> 01:08:24,355
Seon Ah with the second contact.

1527
01:08:24,857 --> 01:08:26,023
A powerful swing!

1528
01:08:26,292 --> 01:08:27,392
A diving dig keeps it alive.

1529
01:08:28,393 --> 01:08:29,994
Watch number one on the left!

1530
01:08:30,529 --> 01:08:31,362
One more!

1531
01:08:31,797 --> 01:08:32,764
The spike!

1532
01:08:36,302 --> 01:08:37,702
The players get in each other's way.

1533
01:08:38,103 --> 01:08:41,239
That ball was playable,
but nobody called it cleanly.

1534
01:08:44,276 --> 01:08:46,544
Serve receive is completely breaking down.

1535
01:08:46,545 --> 01:08:47,845
It's 10-6. A 4-point lead.

1536
01:08:50,349 --> 01:08:52,550
Same spot.

1537
01:08:56,422 --> 01:08:57,255
Behind you!

1538
01:08:57,256 --> 01:08:58,723
(The Wonder Dogs are rattled.)

1539
01:08:58,724 --> 01:08:59,557
Hit it!

1540
01:09:00,593 --> 01:09:01,492
To the right.

1541
01:09:02,294 --> 01:09:03,995
Young In gets blocked.

1542
01:09:03,996 --> 01:09:06,130
(The attack fails.)

1543
01:09:06,433 --> 01:09:10,001
The lead grows to five points.

1544
01:09:10,970 --> 01:09:14,005
- Ye Eun.
- Ye Eun!

1545
01:09:16,743 --> 01:09:19,177
Enkhsoyol comes off, and Ye Eun checks in.

1546
01:09:19,178 --> 01:09:21,179
(Enkhsoyol out, Ye Eun in)

1547
01:09:21,814 --> 01:09:23,281
Ye Eun is solid defensively.

1548
01:09:23,282 --> 01:09:26,217
Coach Kim picked her
for her defensive skills.

1549
01:09:26,819 --> 01:09:29,788
That serve was coming in so slowly.
Why wait to move?

1550
01:09:29,789 --> 01:09:31,790
If you can't even return that,
what are we supposed to do?

1551
01:09:34,093 --> 01:09:35,293
Move your feet!

1552
01:09:35,427 --> 01:09:37,161
Ye Eun, keep your feet moving.

1553
01:09:37,162 --> 01:09:39,096
- Let's go!
- Let's do it!

1554
01:09:39,097 --> 01:09:39,997
(Locked in on the serve)

1555
01:09:42,701 --> 01:09:43,701
- In the back.
- Right away!

1556
01:09:43,702 --> 01:09:44,502
(A clean pass this time!)

1557
01:09:44,503 --> 01:09:45,369
That's it!

1558
01:09:46,172 --> 01:09:47,838
(Only one hitter on the left)

1559
01:09:47,839 --> 01:09:49,007
Left!

1560
01:09:49,008 --> 01:09:50,342
- There we go.
- Get it!

1561
01:09:51,944 --> 01:09:54,045
(A double block on the right)

1562
01:09:54,046 --> 01:09:54,879
Hey!

1563
01:09:55,347 --> 01:09:57,581
Kato Uta gets another block touch.

1564
01:09:59,018 --> 01:10:00,285
A great save as she goes to the floor.

1565
01:10:00,286 --> 01:10:01,620
- Again!
- Go for it.

1566
01:10:01,621 --> 01:10:02,721
Let's go!

1567
01:10:02,722 --> 01:10:03,688
(Another double block)

1568
01:10:03,689 --> 01:10:05,056
Two players go for the same ball.

1569
01:10:06,325 --> 01:10:07,358
Here.

1570
01:10:07,359 --> 01:10:08,326
Oh, man.

1571
01:10:08,327 --> 01:10:10,128
- Abe scores.
- She's changing direction.

1572
01:10:12,264 --> 01:10:14,532
(First set,
Shujitsu High 13 : Wonder Dogs 6)

1573
01:10:14,533 --> 01:10:15,399
Hyo Rim.

1574
01:10:15,801 --> 01:10:17,435
I told you not to set it short.

1575
01:10:17,436 --> 01:10:19,304
When it's short,
you have to set it farther out.

1576
01:10:19,305 --> 01:10:20,938
- Their right-side blocker follows you.
- Yes.

1577
01:10:23,141 --> 01:10:25,076
The Wonder Dogs started off so well.

1578
01:10:25,077 --> 01:10:26,310
(The setter struggles
to distribute the ball.)

1579
01:10:27,279 --> 01:10:28,145
Oh, gosh.

1580
01:10:28,146 --> 01:10:29,747
But since the technical timeout,

1581
01:10:29,748 --> 01:10:31,616
they haven't scored a single point.

1582
01:10:32,017 --> 01:10:34,185
(First set, Shujitsu High 15
: Wonder Dogs 8)

1583
01:10:34,519 --> 01:10:36,454
This is quite a shock.

1584
01:10:36,455 --> 01:10:38,055
(Points slipping away in a flash)

1585
01:10:39,658 --> 01:10:43,927
So many things I should've been able
to do just weren't working.

1586
01:10:43,928 --> 01:10:45,963
It was upsetting...

1587
01:10:46,465 --> 01:10:47,966
and frustrating.

1588
01:10:48,934 --> 01:10:52,503
I could feel my chest tightening
from the pressure.

1589
01:10:53,206 --> 01:10:56,674
Your mental resilience is
what comes to mind.

1590
01:10:57,376 --> 01:11:00,011
(Even with a third opportunity,)

1591
01:11:00,012 --> 01:11:04,315
(will anything fundamentally change?)

1592
01:11:07,987 --> 01:11:08,853
Timeout.

1593
01:11:12,458 --> 01:11:15,427
Coach Kim calls a timeout
for the Wonder Dogs.

1594
01:11:25,070 --> 01:11:27,838
Isn't this our home court?
Aren't we in Korea?

1595
01:11:27,839 --> 01:11:29,474
- That's right.
- Aren't these all our supporters?

1596
01:11:29,475 --> 01:11:31,042
- Don't we know everyone here?
- Yes.

1597
01:11:31,677 --> 01:11:33,344
Then why are you so nervous?

1598
01:11:33,345 --> 01:11:35,146
Shouldn't they be the nervous ones?

1599
01:11:35,147 --> 01:11:37,315
- Exactly.
- Shouldn't they be feeling the heat?

1600
01:11:37,316 --> 01:11:38,183
Yes!

1601
01:11:39,051 --> 01:11:40,351
This is our home court, isn't it?

1602
01:11:43,756 --> 01:11:46,458
(When we're playing well)

1603
01:11:46,625 --> 01:11:47,291
(Cheering)

1604
01:11:49,728 --> 01:11:50,962
(Even when we're struggling)

1605
01:11:51,363 --> 01:11:53,331
(Applause)

1606
01:11:53,332 --> 01:11:56,133
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1607
01:11:56,301 --> 01:11:58,369
(This is our home court.)

1608
01:11:58,504 --> 01:12:00,638
- Don't we train here every day?
- Yes.

1609
01:12:00,639 --> 01:12:02,473
So why are we the ones getting rattled?

1610
01:12:02,474 --> 01:12:05,276
They're the ones who should be nervous!

1611
01:12:05,611 --> 01:12:06,644
Why are you guys so nervous?

1612
01:12:06,645 --> 01:12:08,746
What are you afraid of?

1613
01:12:08,881 --> 01:12:10,682
Is anyone going to kill you
for making a mistake?

1614
01:12:11,650 --> 01:12:13,151
Just relax and play.

1615
01:12:13,152 --> 01:12:14,185
- Yes, Coach.
- Yes, Coach.

1616
01:12:14,821 --> 01:12:16,621
Let's get back out there.

1617
01:12:16,622 --> 01:12:18,656
Let's fight to the end.

1618
01:12:18,958 --> 01:12:23,227
I believed that if Hyo Rim
could regain her composure...

1619
01:12:23,228 --> 01:12:26,364
and play her game, we could win.

1620
01:12:27,132 --> 01:12:30,268
Hearing her tell me
not to lose confidence...

1621
01:12:30,269 --> 01:12:31,936
grounded me instantly.

1622
01:12:33,038 --> 01:12:34,472
Young In!

1623
01:12:35,474 --> 01:12:37,175
(Receiving a signal)

1624
01:12:37,476 --> 01:12:39,410
Read what's happening in front of you.

1625
01:12:39,411 --> 01:12:41,512
Get ready!

1626
01:12:41,647 --> 01:12:43,648
They need to break this streak.

1627
01:12:45,451 --> 01:12:46,484
Ho Bin delivers the serve.

1628
01:12:48,854 --> 01:12:50,087
(A shaky reception)

1629
01:12:50,088 --> 01:12:51,656
They manage to get a back set up.

1630
01:12:51,657 --> 01:12:52,824
(Yoshimoto fires a powerful spike.)

1631
01:12:52,825 --> 01:12:54,492
They keep it alive. Now Hyo Rim.

1632
01:12:54,760 --> 01:12:56,527
- Set it deep!
- Get in there!

1633
01:12:57,296 --> 01:12:59,497
(Behind me...)

1634
01:12:59,498 --> 01:13:01,599
(is our home court.)

1635
01:13:01,900 --> 01:13:02,867
Hit it!

1636
01:13:02,868 --> 01:13:04,335
(A deep set, just as Coach Kim ordered)

1637
01:13:10,109 --> 01:13:11,042
Off the block!

1638
01:13:11,043 --> 01:13:12,343
That's it.

1639
01:13:12,344 --> 01:13:13,278
(Off the block and out)

1640
01:13:15,647 --> 01:13:16,580
Nice!

1641
01:13:20,686 --> 01:13:21,719
Hyo Rim.

1642
01:13:23,922 --> 01:13:26,023
That was a good set,
but you could've gone here too.

1643
01:13:26,024 --> 01:13:27,224
Here's what you need to understand.

1644
01:13:27,225 --> 01:13:29,093
The blockers follow where you go.

1645
01:13:29,094 --> 01:13:30,495
(The opponents read Hyo Rim's set.)

1646
01:13:30,496 --> 01:13:32,496
Go that way, set it wide.
Come this way, set it wide.

1647
01:13:32,497 --> 01:13:33,330
Try that.

1648
01:13:33,331 --> 01:13:34,098
They're crowding the left.

1649
01:13:34,099 --> 01:13:36,133
It can go higher. You can use Bo Been.

1650
01:13:36,134 --> 01:13:37,701
(Coach Kim calls for a middle attack.)

1651
01:13:38,203 --> 01:13:40,271
(An opening...)

1652
01:13:41,440 --> 01:13:44,408
(right down the middle)

1653
01:13:44,409 --> 01:13:47,045
If their middle doesn't move,
you can set Bo Been.

1654
01:13:47,046 --> 01:13:48,046
Check first.

1655
01:13:48,047 --> 01:13:48,947
(The middle is the way through.)

1656
01:13:49,615 --> 01:13:50,448
B.

1657
01:13:51,350 --> 01:13:53,952
(She signals to Bo Been in advance.)

1658
01:13:54,753 --> 01:13:55,820
Yoshimoto Kanade.

1659
01:13:55,821 --> 01:13:56,688
(First set, Shujitsu High 16
: Wonder Dogs 9)

1660
01:13:59,435 --> 01:14:00,735
(Nice reception)

1661
01:14:02,602 --> 01:14:03,735
To the left!

1662
01:14:05,602 --> 01:14:07,068
Bo Been!

1663
01:14:07,335 --> 01:14:08,401
The ball takes off from Hyo Rim!

1664
01:14:08,402 --> 01:14:10,092
(A quick attack
to the middle as instructed)

1665
01:14:10,435 --> 01:14:12,167
- She got it.
- There it is.

1666
01:14:12,168 --> 01:14:13,702
- Nice, Kim Bo Been!
- There you go!

1667
01:14:14,135 --> 01:14:15,735
That's it!

1668
01:14:19,102 --> 01:14:19,968
Let's go!

1669
01:14:20,268 --> 01:14:21,802
- Nice job!
- Nice!

1670
01:14:22,535 --> 01:14:24,334
(Hyo Rim's parents)

1671
01:14:24,335 --> 01:14:26,468
Nice set, Hyo Rim!

1672
01:14:27,935 --> 01:14:30,402
I did a quick attack...

1673
01:14:31,235 --> 01:14:32,202
just as Coach instructed.

1674
01:14:32,203 --> 01:14:34,002
That just resulted in a score.

1675
01:14:35,035 --> 01:14:38,135
I felt like I reached another level.

1676
01:14:39,021 --> 01:14:40,586
Try to win!

1677
01:14:40,587 --> 01:14:42,620
Think about where the ball
should go to score.

1678
01:14:42,621 --> 01:14:43,720
Think!

1679
01:14:43,721 --> 01:14:44,820
(Although guarded, the words resonate.)

1680
01:14:44,821 --> 01:14:46,221
Since that day,

1681
01:14:47,387 --> 01:14:49,654
something has changed.

1682
01:14:51,187 --> 01:14:52,854
Let's end it here for today.

1683
01:14:53,554 --> 01:14:56,521
If anyone has anything to share,
feel free to do so.

1684
01:14:59,021 --> 01:15:00,053
(Raises hand)

1685
01:15:00,054 --> 01:15:01,086
Okay, Hyo Rim.

1686
01:15:01,087 --> 01:15:04,021
Tomorrow, I'm going to play to win...

1687
01:15:04,387 --> 01:15:07,454
and show a more aggressive side.

1688
01:15:09,354 --> 01:15:10,653
I would like that for you.

1689
01:15:10,654 --> 01:15:12,787
(Small cracks begin to show
in Hyo Rim's shell.)

1690
01:15:13,654 --> 01:15:16,187
(Tossing)

1691
01:15:17,721 --> 01:15:19,054
Hyo Rim just threw the towel.

1692
01:15:20,021 --> 01:15:22,521
(Coach Yeon Koung notices too.)

1693
01:15:22,787 --> 01:15:23,754
I like that.

1694
01:15:24,521 --> 01:15:27,286
But in my opinion,
mental states can change...

1695
01:15:27,287 --> 01:15:31,287
depending on the leadership.

1696
01:15:31,521 --> 01:15:33,921
If she meets a leader who supports her,

1697
01:15:34,854 --> 01:15:37,387
she can definitely improve.

1698
01:15:37,687 --> 01:15:38,821
My ball!

1699
01:15:39,621 --> 01:15:41,020
Go!

1700
01:15:41,021 --> 01:15:42,286
Block it! One more!

1701
01:15:42,287 --> 01:15:43,621
Hit it!

1702
01:15:44,687 --> 01:15:48,454
(The once reserved Hyo Rim begins
to change.)

1703
01:15:48,987 --> 01:15:51,387
(She begins to break out of her shell,)

1704
01:15:52,021 --> 01:15:55,554
(and slowly spreads her wings to fly.)

1705
01:15:56,721 --> 01:15:59,020
Nice!

1706
01:15:59,021 --> 01:16:00,287
That was nice.

1707
01:16:01,987 --> 01:16:03,921
Send the ball up.

1708
01:16:04,154 --> 01:16:07,421
I want to just keep faith in our coach
and do as she says.

1709
01:16:10,154 --> 01:16:11,554
Bo Been!

1710
01:16:14,287 --> 01:16:15,787
Bo Been sends a long back toss.

1711
01:16:25,187 --> 01:16:26,587
That's it!

1712
01:16:31,654 --> 01:16:34,021
Hyo Rim did such a good job with the ball.

1713
01:16:34,887 --> 01:16:37,253
Hyo Rim just scored.

1714
01:16:37,254 --> 01:16:39,154
Hyo Rim, that was a good pass.

1715
01:16:41,687 --> 01:16:45,554
Hyo Rim has her ups and downs,

1716
01:16:45,854 --> 01:16:49,821
but she tries to do everything
I ask her to do.

1717
01:16:50,287 --> 01:16:52,887
I want to give her credit for that.

1718
01:16:54,521 --> 01:16:55,321
Hyo Rim!

1719
01:16:56,554 --> 01:16:57,421
Get it!

1720
01:16:58,421 --> 01:16:59,287
Give it to Bo Been!

1721
01:17:02,787 --> 01:17:04,421
(Bo Been jumps.)

1722
01:17:04,921 --> 01:17:06,520
She takes a shot!

1723
01:17:06,521 --> 01:17:08,420
- That's it!
- Nice, Bo Been!

1724
01:17:08,421 --> 01:17:10,887
That's it!

1725
01:17:11,821 --> 01:17:13,886
(Thanks to Hyo Rim's efforts...)

1726
01:17:13,887 --> 01:17:15,787
There was a quick attack up front
and movement in the back.

1727
01:17:16,287 --> 01:17:18,654
Was Hyo Rim always this good at attacks?

1728
01:17:19,987 --> 01:17:21,487
Nice set, Hyo Rim.

1729
01:17:24,287 --> 01:17:27,987
Since things started working out
as our coach instructed,

1730
01:17:30,054 --> 01:17:31,754
volleyball has become fun again.

1731
01:17:33,087 --> 01:17:35,054
Nice set, Hyo Rim.

1732
01:17:36,287 --> 01:17:37,620
The current score is 18 to 13.

1733
01:17:37,621 --> 01:17:39,287
The two teams are just five points apart.

1734
01:17:40,254 --> 01:17:41,420
Kim Bo Been will serve now.

1735
01:17:41,421 --> 01:17:43,154
Time to show off the serve.

1736
01:17:43,587 --> 01:17:46,986
Let's go, Kim Bo Been!

1737
01:17:46,987 --> 01:17:49,354
(Wonder Dogs, Kim Bo Been!)

1738
01:17:49,854 --> 01:17:51,720
We need to ride the flow now.

1739
01:17:51,721 --> 01:17:53,454
We've definitely got this!

1740
01:17:53,721 --> 01:17:55,720
Get the defense ready!

1741
01:17:55,721 --> 01:17:56,753
Don't let your guard down.

1742
01:17:56,754 --> 01:17:57,621
Serve!

1743
01:17:59,354 --> 01:18:00,321
Kim Bo Been serves!

1744
01:18:02,621 --> 01:18:03,454
The ball is set.

1745
01:18:03,455 --> 01:18:04,654
(Onishi gets the ball.)

1746
01:18:05,021 --> 01:18:06,187
A shot to the left!

1747
01:18:07,721 --> 01:18:08,754
Chae Rim digs.

1748
01:18:08,987 --> 01:18:10,054
Nice!

1749
01:18:10,953 --> 01:18:12,253
(Enkhsoyol connects with a second touch.)

1750
01:18:12,619 --> 01:18:13,553
A back attack!

1751
01:18:15,119 --> 01:18:16,486
To the left. Onishi!

1752
01:18:18,486 --> 01:18:19,453
It rebounds off their hands.

1753
01:18:19,454 --> 01:18:20,619
She did it!

1754
01:18:21,319 --> 01:18:22,486
It's a free ball!

1755
01:18:23,153 --> 01:18:24,486
(Young In for the attack)

1756
01:18:25,386 --> 01:18:26,819
The Wonder Dogs strike back!

1757
01:18:27,519 --> 01:18:29,386
- Young In!
- Let's go!

1758
01:18:32,186 --> 01:18:33,253
The ball falls to the right.

1759
01:18:33,786 --> 01:18:34,886
(Flying high)

1760
01:18:35,353 --> 01:18:36,519
The ball's coming over.

1761
01:18:38,519 --> 01:18:39,786
It goes over the net!

1762
01:18:43,886 --> 01:18:45,786
The ball will go over the net!

1763
01:18:46,186 --> 01:18:47,919
I said it would go over from the back!

1764
01:18:50,253 --> 01:18:51,386
The ball will go over!

1765
01:18:51,853 --> 01:18:53,586
I said it would go over from the back!

1766
01:19:00,286 --> 01:19:03,718
(Suddenly a somber atmosphere)

1767
01:19:03,719 --> 01:19:05,519
Nice pass-point!

1768
01:19:07,253 --> 01:19:09,685
- We had a few chances too.
- Right.

1769
01:19:09,686 --> 01:19:11,319
That lost point was disappointing.

1770
01:19:12,219 --> 01:19:14,618
Let's bounce back! Let's do it.

1771
01:19:14,619 --> 01:19:16,619
We just have to turn it around.

1772
01:19:17,919 --> 01:19:20,719
(But the next serve is...)

1773
01:19:21,019 --> 01:19:22,152
Onishi Yukiji is serving.

1774
01:19:22,153 --> 01:19:23,253
They need to be on their toes.

1775
01:19:25,553 --> 01:19:27,852
Her serves are quick!

1776
01:19:27,853 --> 01:19:29,652
It'll be a drop-serve.

1777
01:19:29,653 --> 01:19:31,453
- Okay!
- It's a drop-serve!

1778
01:19:37,619 --> 01:19:38,453
She received it!

1779
01:19:39,219 --> 01:19:40,153
We got it.

1780
01:19:40,886 --> 01:19:42,119
Enkhsoyol attacks.

1781
01:19:43,253 --> 01:19:44,219
Yoshimoto saves it.

1782
01:19:44,686 --> 01:19:46,253
(She saved that?)

1783
01:19:46,519 --> 01:19:48,086
(Yoshimoto gets ready to attack.)

1784
01:19:51,053 --> 01:19:53,453
(Targets the open spot)

1785
01:19:54,153 --> 01:19:57,152
(Disappointed)

1786
01:19:57,153 --> 01:19:58,519
That was your chance.

1787
01:19:58,886 --> 01:20:00,652
Onishi serves, thinking ahead.

1788
01:20:00,653 --> 01:20:02,986
She's a strategic player.

1789
01:20:05,287 --> 01:20:07,419
(Onishi's strong serve...)

1790
01:20:08,719 --> 01:20:10,819
(coupled with the powerful Yoshimoto)

1791
01:20:11,719 --> 01:20:13,086
The score is 21 to 13.

1792
01:20:21,019 --> 01:20:23,085
Guys, you can't block
without thinking about defense.

1793
01:20:23,086 --> 01:20:24,718
Try to synchronize your blocks.

1794
01:20:24,719 --> 01:20:25,619
Enkhsoyol!

1795
01:20:26,086 --> 01:20:27,653
Think about the timing.

1796
01:20:29,786 --> 01:20:33,519
(She pointed out block timing
a while ago.)

1797
01:20:33,786 --> 01:20:35,053
Think about the timing!

1798
01:20:36,653 --> 01:20:40,153
(Their block timing leaves the team open
to Shujitsu attacks.)

1799
01:20:40,719 --> 01:20:42,118
Watch the timing for our blocks.

1800
01:20:42,119 --> 01:20:43,886
A little bit later.

1801
01:20:45,553 --> 01:20:48,185
(But the next serve still comes from...)

1802
01:20:48,186 --> 01:20:50,819
It's another serve from Onishi.

1803
01:20:52,353 --> 01:20:53,153
All together!

1804
01:20:53,753 --> 01:20:56,119
We can't lose again like the last time.

1805
01:20:57,019 --> 01:20:58,952
We can't lose this time.

1806
01:20:58,953 --> 01:21:00,386
We have to win.

1807
01:21:08,053 --> 01:21:09,085
(Nice reception)

1808
01:21:09,086 --> 01:21:09,953
That's it.

1809
01:21:11,419 --> 01:21:12,253
Where is it going?

1810
01:21:13,086 --> 01:21:14,486
Enkhsoyol takes a shot!

1811
01:21:16,186 --> 01:21:18,853
(The ball moves to the middle.)

1812
01:21:19,886 --> 01:21:22,453
Let's delay the blocks a little.

1813
01:21:26,553 --> 01:21:29,352
- She spikes, and it's blocked!
- Nice!

1814
01:21:29,353 --> 01:21:31,453
She spikes, and it's blocked!

1815
01:21:32,919 --> 01:21:38,219
(Good job, Enkhsoyol!)

1816
01:21:40,653 --> 01:21:41,785
Nice block!

1817
01:21:41,786 --> 01:21:44,719
That was good timing!

1818
01:21:45,153 --> 01:21:47,986
I think she's finally getting
the hang of it.

1819
01:21:50,219 --> 01:21:53,752
Enkhsoyol's block worked perfectly.

1820
01:21:53,753 --> 01:21:54,553
Right.

1821
01:21:55,719 --> 01:21:57,886
(A swift counterattack through blocking)

1822
01:21:59,188 --> 01:22:01,487
Think about the timing.

1823
01:22:01,488 --> 01:22:03,020
Think about where the gaps are.

1824
01:22:03,021 --> 01:22:04,920
One more!

1825
01:22:04,921 --> 01:22:06,520
Let's get another one!

1826
01:22:06,521 --> 01:22:07,621
(Defense to save the day)

1827
01:22:08,388 --> 01:22:09,755
Ha Hyo Rim serves.

1828
01:22:13,988 --> 01:22:14,955
A back attack!

1829
01:22:16,790 --> 01:22:18,021
An attack to center-back!

1830
01:22:19,421 --> 01:22:22,021
(Full-body defense?)

1831
01:22:23,288 --> 01:22:24,421
She saved the ball.

1832
01:22:24,588 --> 01:22:26,421
Look at the ball!

1833
01:22:27,022 --> 01:22:28,256
(Moving back)

1834
01:22:29,122 --> 01:22:30,521
- It flies in the air.
- You got this!

1835
01:22:30,522 --> 01:22:31,256
(Young In's spike)

1836
01:22:31,556 --> 01:22:32,356
A hard hit!

1837
01:22:32,889 --> 01:22:33,889
Shujitsu saves the ball.

1838
01:22:34,156 --> 01:22:35,089
Hurry up and block!

1839
01:22:40,042 --> 01:22:41,430
They receive it from the back.

1840
01:22:41,670 --> 01:22:44,501
She fights hard to keep that ball alive.

1841
01:22:45,328 --> 01:22:46,662
(Great defense)

1842
01:22:46,663 --> 01:22:47,429
Let's go.

1843
01:22:47,970 --> 01:22:49,071
They need to get it over.

1844
01:22:50,632 --> 01:22:53,969
(Yoshimoto prepares to attack.)

1845
01:22:54,877 --> 01:22:56,311
(Getting ready to block)

1846
01:22:56,312 --> 01:22:57,946
(Getting ready to defend)

1847
01:22:58,047 --> 01:22:59,114
It's a free ball.

1848
01:23:01,991 --> 01:23:03,625
(This time...)

1849
01:23:03,626 --> 01:23:05,927
(we must save it!)

1850
01:23:12,287 --> 01:23:13,035
Look at that!

1851
01:23:19,675 --> 01:23:22,577
They did everything right, but...

1852
01:23:23,279 --> 01:23:26,248
Kato Uta is playing smart.

1853
01:23:27,750 --> 01:23:33,436
(Her unconventional plays keep
catching them off guard.)

1854
01:23:35,558 --> 01:23:38,360
(Shujitsu's overwhelming play)

1855
01:23:39,648 --> 01:23:41,229
At this rate,

1856
01:23:41,597 --> 01:23:43,631
today's match is going to be tough.

1857
01:23:44,100 --> 01:23:47,469
Their defense was just too good,

1858
01:23:48,203 --> 01:23:50,938
and their attacks were
incredibly powerful sometimes.

1859
01:23:51,540 --> 01:23:53,341
They were playing so well.

1860
01:23:54,177 --> 01:23:56,811
Maybe because the match wasn't going...

1861
01:23:56,846 --> 01:24:00,816
the way our players had expected,

1862
01:24:00,817 --> 01:24:03,318
they seemed pretty flustered.

1863
01:24:03,919 --> 01:24:05,753
So I kept thinking about it.

1864
01:24:05,754 --> 01:24:07,722
(We need a new strategy.)

1865
01:24:09,064 --> 01:24:11,277
Young In, you keep setting the ball
to the right.

1866
01:24:11,278 --> 01:24:13,329
It's a high ball.
Keep the ball on your left hand.

1867
01:24:13,354 --> 01:24:14,572
- Okay.
- Enkhsoyol.

1868
01:24:14,597 --> 01:24:16,898
It's not that complicated. Move your feet.

1869
01:24:17,292 --> 01:24:19,801
Chae Rim, they're serving
to Enkhsoyol a lot,

1870
01:24:19,802 --> 01:24:21,402
so move over a little more to cover her.

1871
01:24:21,403 --> 01:24:22,370
- Understand?
- Yes.

1872
01:24:22,939 --> 01:24:25,239
I thought about...

1873
01:24:25,240 --> 01:24:29,010
how I would've worked with the girls
if I were still a player.

1874
01:24:29,631 --> 01:24:32,214
I tried to put myself in their shoes.

1875
01:24:32,621 --> 01:24:34,516
That's how I guided them.

1876
01:24:35,730 --> 01:24:37,151
Hyo Rim.

1877
01:24:37,653 --> 01:24:38,586
Hyo Rim.

1878
01:24:38,587 --> 01:24:40,221
(Instructions delivered)

1879
01:24:42,992 --> 01:24:44,159
- Nice.
- Do what she said.

1880
01:24:46,595 --> 01:24:49,730
Both middle blockers, cover together.

1881
01:24:50,399 --> 01:24:53,167
(Keeping a close eye on Ho Bin)

1882
01:24:58,166 --> 01:24:59,373
Takiguchi Rin is serving.

1883
01:25:01,529 --> 01:25:02,143
Get it.

1884
01:25:02,144 --> 01:25:03,144
Get it up.

1885
01:25:03,612 --> 01:25:05,346
- Get it up.
- Great reception.

1886
01:25:05,347 --> 01:25:06,414
(Chae Rim gets it nicely.)

1887
01:25:06,415 --> 01:25:07,381
Get it.

1888
01:25:07,483 --> 01:25:09,551
(Hyo Rim sets it.)

1889
01:25:10,726 --> 01:25:11,620
Enkhsoyol spikes!

1890
01:25:13,088 --> 01:25:14,355
Watch your block timing.

1891
01:25:17,026 --> 01:25:17,892
Blocking.

1892
01:25:18,227 --> 01:25:19,761
(Nice block!)

1893
01:25:24,433 --> 01:25:26,534
She threw herself
at the ball and stopped it.

1894
01:25:26,535 --> 01:25:27,780
Get ready for the second block.

1895
01:25:29,872 --> 01:25:31,139
(Another block)

1896
01:25:31,307 --> 01:25:32,240
Blocked right back.

1897
01:25:32,775 --> 01:25:33,975
They keep it alive!

1898
01:25:33,976 --> 01:25:36,177
Their defense is rock-solid.

1899
01:25:37,405 --> 01:25:38,646
It's a free ball.

1900
01:25:38,671 --> 01:25:40,082
(It's our turn to attack again.)

1901
01:25:41,416 --> 01:25:42,150
Use the decoy.

1902
01:25:42,490 --> 01:25:43,217
Go with C.

1903
01:25:43,752 --> 01:25:44,586
Right away!

1904
01:25:44,587 --> 01:25:45,687
(Decoy)

1905
01:25:46,855 --> 01:25:48,222
(Flapping)

1906
01:25:53,808 --> 01:25:55,764
Enkhsoyol! Nice!

1907
01:25:56,398 --> 01:25:57,567
- Nice!
- They are catching up.

1908
01:25:58,359 --> 01:26:03,538
(That's what I'm talking about!)

1909
01:26:04,933 --> 01:26:06,974
Great job.

1910
01:26:09,378 --> 01:26:10,952
(Before the rally even begins...)

1911
01:26:11,447 --> 01:26:14,543
Hyo Rim, go with A-C.

1912
01:26:16,252 --> 01:26:18,353
(Ho Bin draws the blockers
toward the middle.)

1913
01:26:18,754 --> 01:26:19,721
Enkhsoyol.

1914
01:26:21,223 --> 01:26:23,691
(The hand signal calls
for a left-side attack.)

1915
01:26:24,627 --> 01:26:26,394
(They pretend to attack
through the middle.)

1916
01:26:27,496 --> 01:26:30,531
(But the left side attacks again.)

1917
01:26:31,300 --> 01:26:32,633
There's still a gap,

1918
01:26:32,634 --> 01:26:34,502
but our performance has improved a lot,

1919
01:26:34,503 --> 01:26:36,638
- so we can definitely catch up.
- I agree.

1920
01:26:37,025 --> 01:26:40,742
Each of the players is
playing their role very well.

1921
01:26:41,910 --> 01:26:43,244
(The rally continues.)

1922
01:26:43,612 --> 01:26:45,279
(We'll play how we want.)

1923
01:26:48,550 --> 01:26:50,685
Spike! That's right.

1924
01:26:51,854 --> 01:26:53,087
Well done.

1925
01:26:53,088 --> 01:26:55,857
(The Wonder Dogs are gaining momentum.)

1926
01:26:56,151 --> 01:26:56,858
A great reception.

1927
01:26:59,929 --> 01:27:01,062
They couldn't save it.

1928
01:27:01,063 --> 01:27:02,831
(Shujitsu strikes back again.)

1929
01:27:04,433 --> 01:27:06,434
(A fierce battle for every point)

1930
01:27:06,902 --> 01:27:08,269
Spike! Block!

1931
01:27:09,911 --> 01:27:11,073
They're off balance.

1932
01:27:11,074 --> 01:27:12,240
Got it.

1933
01:27:12,241 --> 01:27:13,642
Their defense is falling apart.

1934
01:27:16,613 --> 01:27:17,980
They managed to save that one.

1935
01:27:20,316 --> 01:27:22,250
(So close!)

1936
01:27:22,251 --> 01:27:23,251
Oh, my.

1937
01:27:23,685 --> 01:27:24,786
Their coverage is no joke.

1938
01:27:25,854 --> 01:27:27,720
- It's our free ball.
- Free ball.

1939
01:27:29,058 --> 01:27:30,191
Ha Hyo Rim.

1940
01:27:31,360 --> 01:27:33,194
(Drawing a double block with a decoy,)

1941
01:27:34,363 --> 01:27:35,730
(then exploiting the gap)

1942
01:27:36,065 --> 01:27:36,764
Get through.

1943
01:27:39,101 --> 01:27:40,033
Spike.

1944
01:27:40,168 --> 01:27:41,102
It's kept alive again.

1945
01:27:41,103 --> 01:27:42,670
(Saved again)

1946
01:27:42,771 --> 01:27:43,871
Great.

1947
01:27:45,174 --> 01:27:46,475
(Shujitsu connects with a second touch.)

1948
01:27:46,734 --> 01:27:48,074
They can attack through the middle.

1949
01:27:51,272 --> 01:27:52,947
A strong hit to the middle.

1950
01:28:04,627 --> 01:28:05,660
There. Move to the outside!

1951
01:28:13,035 --> 01:28:17,038
(They concede another crucial point.)

1952
01:28:20,542 --> 01:28:23,777
It's 24 to 16. It's set point
for Shujitsu in the first set.

1953
01:28:23,778 --> 01:28:25,046
(First set, Shujitsu High 24
: Wonder Dogs 16)

1954
01:28:25,047 --> 01:28:27,281
Let's go again. Next point.

1955
01:28:27,282 --> 01:28:28,482
It's okay. Next point.

1956
01:28:29,143 --> 01:28:29,917
Come on.

1957
01:28:31,253 --> 01:28:33,769
(But the next server is...)

1958
01:28:35,203 --> 01:28:36,324
Yoshimoto Kanade is serving.

1959
01:28:37,479 --> 01:28:38,560
We have to play well.

1960
01:28:39,547 --> 01:28:43,264
Their serves can be shaky.
Keep your feet moving.

1961
01:28:45,934 --> 01:28:46,967
Yoshimoto Kanade.

1962
01:28:52,241 --> 01:28:53,575
Thank goodness.

1963
01:28:53,576 --> 01:28:54,375
It's out.

1964
01:28:56,945 --> 01:29:00,461
(Raising their spirits)

1965
01:29:00,849 --> 01:29:02,952
- Let's keep going.
- Keep going.

1966
01:29:03,318 --> 01:29:04,952
We have to take this chance
to break through.

1967
01:29:04,953 --> 01:29:05,953
Absolutely.

1968
01:29:07,055 --> 01:29:08,491
(Clapping)

1969
01:29:08,492 --> 01:29:10,291
- Wonder Dogs!
- Wonder Dogs!

1970
01:29:10,726 --> 01:29:13,628
(The crowd cheers with all their hearts.)

1971
01:29:14,416 --> 01:29:15,229
Young In serves.

1972
01:29:19,101 --> 01:29:20,435
The reception is shaky.

1973
01:29:20,936 --> 01:29:22,570
Nice serve.

1974
01:29:23,038 --> 01:29:24,306
No.

1975
01:29:24,907 --> 01:29:25,940
To center!

1976
01:29:26,141 --> 01:29:27,374
It's our free ball.

1977
01:29:27,743 --> 01:29:29,478
- Go up.
- It's in the air.

1978
01:29:30,979 --> 01:29:32,480
(Bo Been is in the middle.)

1979
01:29:33,882 --> 01:29:36,484
(The blockers move toward the middle.)

1980
01:29:39,355 --> 01:29:42,657
Spike! Another one!

1981
01:29:43,225 --> 01:29:47,895
(You can do this.)

1982
01:29:49,324 --> 01:29:50,064
Well done.

1983
01:29:50,532 --> 01:29:51,432
Bravo.

1984
01:29:57,251 --> 01:29:58,205
Nice job, Hyo Rim.

1985
01:29:58,474 --> 01:29:59,507
(Thumbs up)

1986
01:29:59,508 --> 01:30:01,076
Keep fighting until the very end.

1987
01:30:01,343 --> 01:30:02,476
Let's get another one.

1988
01:30:02,477 --> 01:30:03,311
(Until the very end)

1989
01:30:03,312 --> 01:30:04,745
Go for it.

1990
01:30:06,682 --> 01:30:07,915
Young In serves again.

1991
01:30:11,259 --> 01:30:12,286
Smash!

1992
01:30:14,056 --> 01:30:14,922
There's Kato Uta.

1993
01:30:15,257 --> 01:30:16,991
She rushes in for the next attack.

1994
01:30:17,760 --> 01:30:19,160
Reception from the back!

1995
01:30:19,161 --> 01:30:21,396
Take your time.

1996
01:30:22,064 --> 01:30:23,031
Chae Rim tips the ball.

1997
01:30:24,500 --> 01:30:25,400
It's blocked.

1998
01:30:25,401 --> 01:30:26,534
(The ball goes high.)

1999
01:30:26,635 --> 01:30:28,569
It's coming over!

2000
01:30:35,604 --> 01:30:36,978
- It's over.
- It's crossing the net.

2001
01:30:41,950 --> 01:30:46,253
(They concede the final point
all too easily.)

2002
01:30:48,957 --> 01:30:49,957
Nice job.

2003
01:30:51,794 --> 01:30:54,729
Shujitsu High takes the first set.

2004
01:30:57,733 --> 01:30:59,734
(Sighing)

2005
01:31:01,670 --> 01:31:05,439
They chose Shujitsu
as their first opponent...

2006
01:31:05,440 --> 01:31:07,341
to put last year's nightmare behind them.

2007
01:31:07,444 --> 01:31:10,078
But they couldn't break
that curse in the first set.

2008
01:31:11,132 --> 01:31:13,715
What's frustrating is
that the Wonder Dogs' performance...

2009
01:31:13,716 --> 01:31:15,049
improved as the set went on.

2010
01:31:15,383 --> 01:31:16,719
Their attack success rate was...

2011
01:31:16,720 --> 01:31:18,953
actually two percentage points higher.

2012
01:31:18,954 --> 01:31:20,054
Exactly.

2013
01:31:20,055 --> 01:31:21,188
(Despite their higher attack
success rate,)

2014
01:31:22,357 --> 01:31:27,428
(they still lost the first set.)

2015
01:31:28,063 --> 01:31:29,296
Nice job.

2016
01:31:30,065 --> 01:31:33,501
The players who competed last year look
especially disappointed.

2017
01:31:35,370 --> 01:31:36,003
Get over here now!

2018
01:31:36,798 --> 01:31:38,339
Come on! Hurry up!

2019
01:31:38,986 --> 01:31:40,908
Just get over here!

2020
01:31:40,909 --> 01:31:41,909
(No time for regrets)

2021
01:31:41,910 --> 01:31:43,344
(Rushing over)

2022
01:31:43,679 --> 01:31:44,645
(Springing up)

2023
01:31:44,646 --> 01:31:45,680
Quickly.

2024
01:31:45,681 --> 01:31:47,882
(Feedback instead of regret)

2025
01:31:47,983 --> 01:31:49,050
(Strategic timeout for the second set)

2026
01:31:49,051 --> 01:31:50,151
Come here, guys.

2027
01:31:50,152 --> 01:31:52,787
What do you think isn't working right now?
Tell me.

2028
01:31:53,147 --> 01:31:54,948
- Tell me.
- Our reception and attacks.

2029
01:31:54,956 --> 01:31:58,025
Our reception wasn't that bad.

2030
01:31:58,026 --> 01:32:00,561
I think our connections
and finishing attacks aren't working.

2031
01:32:00,562 --> 01:32:02,096
Our attacks are okay,

2032
01:32:02,097 --> 01:32:05,533
but we haven't used
our third-Zone tips or pushes.

2033
01:32:05,901 --> 01:32:08,602
(During the video session
preparing for Shujitsu)

2034
01:32:08,937 --> 01:32:11,605
This is where they position
for our attacks.

2035
01:32:11,773 --> 01:32:15,060
When they set up a double block,
this is their setup.

2036
01:32:15,711 --> 01:32:21,717
(Zone 3 is left open
when the opponent blocks.)

2037
01:32:21,718 --> 01:32:24,452
We should always look
to tip or push into Zone Three.

2038
01:32:24,686 --> 01:32:25,219
Hyo Rim.

2039
01:32:25,554 --> 01:32:29,257
(Their Zone 3 tip actually scored
a point in the first set.)

2040
01:32:29,764 --> 01:32:32,305
Whether it's a push down the middle
or a tip into Zone Three,

2041
01:32:32,306 --> 01:32:33,327
it doesn't have to score directly.

2042
01:32:33,475 --> 01:32:36,346
The opponents will have a hard time
keeping the ball in play.

2043
01:32:36,347 --> 01:32:39,233
Then they'll send us an easier ball,
and we can use that to our advantage.

2044
01:32:39,234 --> 01:32:41,634
A middle push or tip
to Zone Three always works.

2045
01:32:42,401 --> 01:32:43,733
Let's say we have two over here.

2046
01:32:43,734 --> 01:32:46,533
That's when you push and tip
to Zone Three.

2047
01:32:46,534 --> 01:32:47,800
That's fine. Understand?

2048
01:32:47,801 --> 01:32:48,833
And the serves, too.

2049
01:32:48,834 --> 01:32:50,400
Send them lower.

2050
01:32:50,401 --> 01:32:51,601
You know where the target is.

2051
01:32:52,267 --> 01:32:53,934
The target of our serves is...

2052
01:32:54,901 --> 01:32:56,533
Zone One, as we mentioned.

2053
01:32:56,534 --> 01:32:59,801
We're aiming for Zone 1 or Zone 4.

2054
01:33:00,434 --> 01:33:01,700
How much did their libero get?

2055
01:33:01,701 --> 01:33:02,966
It's over 60 percent.

2056
01:33:02,967 --> 01:33:04,600
Their libero's reception rate is
over 60 percent.

2057
01:33:04,601 --> 01:33:05,367
Got it?

2058
01:33:05,454 --> 01:33:07,467
(Every serve goes...)

2059
01:33:07,867 --> 01:33:10,966
(to the infallible libero.)

2060
01:33:10,967 --> 01:33:14,333
Wonder Dogs are sending
the serve to the libero.

2061
01:33:14,334 --> 01:33:17,101
Attack the opposite side of the libero.
Got it?

2062
01:33:17,698 --> 01:33:20,601
(Key strategy for the second set:
push and serve)

2063
01:33:21,201 --> 01:33:24,701
(Meanwhile, the Shujitsu team, which is
currently leading the game)

2064
01:33:34,934 --> 01:33:36,100
Natsuki,

2065
01:33:36,101 --> 01:33:39,266
you're going to struggle
in the Inter-High Championship.

2066
01:33:39,267 --> 01:33:41,200
Their middle blocker is 180cm tall.

2067
01:33:41,201 --> 01:33:44,166
If you hit it when the blockers are
closing in, it will get blocked.

2068
01:33:44,167 --> 01:33:46,733
Try to be strategic.

2069
01:33:46,734 --> 01:33:48,633
Despite winning the first set
by a significant gap,

2070
01:33:48,634 --> 01:33:50,401
Coach Nishihata doesn't seem satisfied.

2071
01:33:51,401 --> 01:33:55,734
(Despite leading the score,
Shujitsu stays alert.)

2072
01:33:55,967 --> 01:33:56,834
One, two, three!

2073
01:33:56,835 --> 01:33:59,400
(The Wonder Dogs get ready
to strike back.)

2074
01:33:59,401 --> 01:34:02,367
We have to win the second set.

2075
01:34:04,934 --> 01:34:06,900
(The revenge match is not over yet.)

2076
01:34:06,901 --> 01:34:08,033
Make it short.

2077
01:34:08,034 --> 01:34:08,967
Get ready to cover.

2078
01:34:08,968 --> 01:34:12,367
(It's time to strike back.)

2079
01:34:13,067 --> 01:34:14,334
The second set begins.

2080
01:34:14,667 --> 01:34:16,501
(Kato Uta serves.)

2081
01:34:18,701 --> 01:34:19,634
Put it up!

2082
01:34:20,634 --> 01:34:21,567
(A set to Chae Rim)

2083
01:34:21,567 --> 01:34:22,401
Hit it!

2084
01:34:22,402 --> 01:34:24,867
Push and tip to Zone Three.

2085
01:34:25,767 --> 01:34:26,634
(Middle push)

2086
01:34:27,234 --> 01:34:28,167
A push shot.

2087
01:34:28,366 --> 01:34:29,266
(The ball passes over.)

2088
01:34:29,267 --> 01:34:30,034
That's it.

2089
01:34:30,701 --> 01:34:32,267
(A free ball flies over.)

2090
01:34:33,367 --> 01:34:34,201
Let's go with A!

2091
01:34:35,301 --> 01:34:36,434
(Bo Been is a decoy.)

2092
01:34:37,101 --> 01:34:37,934
(Oh shoot!)

2093
01:34:38,867 --> 01:34:40,434
(Chae Rim is the real target.)

2094
01:34:40,834 --> 01:34:41,767
Hit it!

2095
01:34:42,901 --> 01:34:44,366
Spike!

2096
01:34:44,367 --> 01:34:45,334
A success!

2097
01:34:45,701 --> 01:34:47,333
(Let's get the second set!)

2098
01:34:47,334 --> 01:34:48,234
That's it.

2099
01:34:48,235 --> 01:34:49,933
(A smooth combination)

2100
01:34:49,934 --> 01:34:51,067
Good job!

2101
01:34:52,634 --> 01:34:55,200
This is the middle push
Coach Kim mentioned.

2102
01:34:55,201 --> 01:34:56,833
They're following along very well.

2103
01:34:56,834 --> 01:34:58,734
(A free ball follows.)

2104
01:34:58,967 --> 01:35:01,334
(Another decoy block)

2105
01:35:02,101 --> 01:35:06,167
(Evading the blockers
and forcing a single block)

2106
01:35:06,634 --> 01:35:09,667
(Hitting the gap for a successful point)

2107
01:35:11,134 --> 01:35:12,734
That was the same attack from before.

2108
01:35:13,801 --> 01:35:15,200
(The second set is off to a good start.)

2109
01:35:15,201 --> 01:35:18,001
Let's go!

2110
01:35:18,367 --> 01:35:19,467
Get ready.

2111
01:35:19,834 --> 01:35:21,434
Let's take this slowly.

2112
01:35:22,067 --> 01:35:24,101
(The rally continues right away.)

2113
01:35:24,234 --> 01:35:25,266
Mine!

2114
01:35:25,267 --> 01:35:26,666
Enkhsoyol gets the ball.

2115
01:35:26,667 --> 01:35:27,667
Hit it!

2116
01:35:28,834 --> 01:35:29,734
Mine!

2117
01:35:29,734 --> 01:35:30,567
A tip!

2118
01:35:30,934 --> 01:35:32,766
(Shaky defense again)

2119
01:35:32,767 --> 01:35:33,734
Cover quickly!

2120
01:35:34,801 --> 01:35:35,967
She saved the ball.

2121
01:35:36,267 --> 01:35:37,267
(Yoshimoto's back attack)

2122
01:35:37,901 --> 01:35:39,433
Yoshimoto! And they save it.

2123
01:35:39,434 --> 01:35:40,367
Let's go A!

2124
01:35:43,634 --> 01:35:44,701
Left!

2125
01:35:46,067 --> 01:35:47,234
(Not middle)

2126
01:35:47,434 --> 01:35:48,234
(Left again)

2127
01:35:49,867 --> 01:35:51,366
A powerful hit!

2128
01:35:51,367 --> 01:35:52,334
And it's successful!

2129
01:35:53,034 --> 01:35:54,934
(Chae Rim scores again!)

2130
01:35:55,334 --> 01:35:56,433
All right!

2131
01:35:56,434 --> 01:35:57,434
(Relieved)

2132
01:35:57,801 --> 01:36:00,033
That's it!

2133
01:36:00,034 --> 01:36:01,633
(This is what I'm talking about!)

2134
01:36:01,634 --> 01:36:02,534
That's it.

2135
01:36:04,834 --> 01:36:08,567
(A push that shakes up the defense again)

2136
01:36:09,801 --> 01:36:13,134
(A spike gets through the block.)

2137
01:36:14,807 --> 01:36:15,840
Currently, the score is 1 to 2.

2138
01:36:15,867 --> 01:36:17,333
Chae Rim serves.

2139
01:36:17,334 --> 01:36:19,534
(Chae Rim carries out the strategy.)

2140
01:36:21,101 --> 01:36:22,467
Let's go, Baek Chae Rim!

2141
01:36:24,067 --> 01:36:25,401
Baek Chae Rim!

2142
01:36:26,734 --> 01:36:28,600
(Now it's time...)

2143
01:36:28,601 --> 01:36:30,600
(for the serve strategy.)

2144
01:36:30,601 --> 01:36:32,233
Avoid the libero.

2145
01:36:32,234 --> 01:36:34,501
Aim for either side, Zone 1 or Zone 4!

2146
01:36:35,067 --> 01:36:37,601
(Serve target)

2147
01:36:38,034 --> 01:36:39,233
(Serve to...)

2148
01:36:39,234 --> 01:36:41,633
(lead the second set)

2149
01:36:41,634 --> 01:36:45,467
(Crowd cheering)

2150
01:36:45,934 --> 01:36:46,767
Shoot.

2151
01:36:48,082 --> 01:36:49,433
(Unfortunately lands on the libero)

2152
01:36:49,434 --> 01:36:51,401
I said avoid the libero.

2153
01:36:52,201 --> 01:36:54,434
(The ball leaves the libero...)

2154
01:36:55,234 --> 01:36:56,201
(and goes to Onishi.)

2155
01:36:56,202 --> 01:36:57,267
This is our chance!

2156
01:37:01,667 --> 01:37:02,534
Onishi!

2157
01:37:02,734 --> 01:37:03,734
It's a touch out.

2158
01:37:04,934 --> 01:37:05,801
Sorry.

2159
01:37:07,367 --> 01:37:09,234
Onishi clearly has power.

2160
01:37:11,167 --> 01:37:13,533
Because the serve keeps
going to the libero,

2161
01:37:13,534 --> 01:37:16,267
the ball keeps safely making it to Onishi.

2162
01:37:17,567 --> 01:37:21,901
(An easy serve gives the opponent a chance
to strike back.)

2163
01:37:23,967 --> 01:37:24,767
It's tied at two points.

2164
01:37:26,567 --> 01:37:28,834
(Eventually allowing the tie)

2165
01:37:30,367 --> 01:37:31,434
(Glancing)

2166
01:37:31,934 --> 01:37:34,033
Their straight lane is open.

2167
01:37:34,034 --> 01:37:35,200
(Nodding)

2168
01:37:35,201 --> 01:37:36,933
We're all warmed up now! Let's go!

2169
01:37:36,934 --> 01:37:37,801
Okay.

2170
01:37:40,534 --> 01:37:41,933
(Shujitsu serves again.)

2171
01:37:41,934 --> 01:37:43,001
Miyake Hina serves.

2172
01:37:45,067 --> 01:37:46,167
(A safe reception)

2173
01:37:48,567 --> 01:37:49,467
Enkhsoyol!

2174
01:37:50,234 --> 01:37:51,201
Shujitsu saves the ball.

2175
01:37:52,467 --> 01:37:54,734
(Yoshimoto's back attack)

2176
01:37:56,067 --> 01:37:57,466
(A tip to Zone 3 in response)

2177
01:37:57,467 --> 01:37:58,301
That's it.

2178
01:37:58,767 --> 01:37:59,933
A middle strike.

2179
01:37:59,934 --> 01:38:01,401
(Another defense-shaking play)

2180
01:38:02,267 --> 01:38:03,134
(Barely saved)

2181
01:38:03,134 --> 01:38:04,034
(Hard spike)

2182
01:38:04,267 --> 01:38:05,034
Over here!

2183
01:38:05,634 --> 01:38:07,734
(Onishi gets the ball again.)

2184
01:38:08,434 --> 01:38:10,133
(Onishi jumps once more.)

2185
01:38:10,134 --> 01:38:12,366
Their straight lane is open.

2186
01:38:12,367 --> 01:38:14,734
(Pushing straight)

2187
01:38:14,901 --> 01:38:17,101
This time, it was a tip.

2188
01:38:18,901 --> 01:38:21,833
(It's in.)

2189
01:38:21,834 --> 01:38:24,934
(Onishi's unconventional push scores
a point.)

2190
01:38:25,967 --> 01:38:28,200
Onishi just responded
to a push from Wonder Dogs...

2191
01:38:28,201 --> 01:38:29,933
with another push.

2192
01:38:29,934 --> 01:38:31,233
She's not just strong,

2193
01:38:31,234 --> 01:38:33,101
but she's also smart.

2194
01:38:33,967 --> 01:38:36,467
(Second set, Shujitsu High 3
: Wonder Dogs 2)

2195
01:38:36,901 --> 01:38:39,667
(A tight point-for-point match)

2196
01:38:40,088 --> 01:38:42,401
(One mistake will...)

2197
01:38:43,034 --> 01:38:45,434
(widen the gap.)

2198
01:38:45,667 --> 01:38:48,900
Bo Been, go for a little run...

2199
01:38:48,901 --> 01:38:50,433
when there are two attackers.

2200
01:38:50,434 --> 01:38:52,234
(Coach Kim directs Bo Been to do
a moving attack.)

2201
01:38:52,534 --> 01:38:53,434
Hyo Rim!

2202
01:38:54,634 --> 01:38:56,533
Go for C.

2203
01:38:56,534 --> 01:38:58,000
The setter sets low.

2204
01:38:58,001 --> 01:38:58,834
Okay.

2205
01:39:00,667 --> 01:39:03,934
(Revising the strategy to the left?)

2206
01:39:07,367 --> 01:39:09,334
(Miyake Hina serves.)

2207
01:39:12,634 --> 01:39:15,434
Push it up!

2208
01:39:15,701 --> 01:39:16,534
Hit it!

2209
01:39:16,534 --> 01:39:17,524
(Slides left)

2210
01:39:18,001 --> 01:39:19,801
Back up!

2211
01:39:20,334 --> 01:39:21,733
(Another one is coming.)

2212
01:39:21,734 --> 01:39:23,134
(Slowly moving to the left)

2213
01:39:24,867 --> 01:39:26,667
(It's not Enkhsoyol?)

2214
01:39:28,834 --> 01:39:29,667
There she goes.

2215
01:39:29,668 --> 01:39:31,001
(It's to Bo Been!)

2216
01:39:31,601 --> 01:39:33,334
(Unconventional combination attack)

2217
01:39:33,654 --> 01:39:34,933
(Dopamine rush)

2218
01:39:34,934 --> 01:39:35,901
That's it!

2219
01:39:39,734 --> 01:39:42,067
(The sign was a ruse.)

2220
01:39:42,501 --> 01:39:44,467
(Calling for left attack)

2221
01:39:45,301 --> 01:39:47,701
(Gesturing for a combination attack)

2222
01:39:48,001 --> 01:39:50,131
(Shujitsu only guards the left.)

2223
01:39:50,534 --> 01:39:52,934
(A single block on the right side.)

2224
01:39:53,401 --> 01:39:54,801
(Aiming for the opening)

2225
01:39:55,301 --> 01:39:57,934
(Another attack variant fools the blocker)

2226
01:39:58,234 --> 01:40:00,366
(Let's go! Kim Bo Been!)

2227
01:40:00,367 --> 01:40:03,867
Stay focused!

2228
01:40:04,601 --> 01:40:05,501
(Time for us to serve again)

2229
01:40:05,501 --> 01:40:06,434
Hyo Rim serves.

2230
01:40:07,067 --> 01:40:08,501
Aim for Zone Four.

2231
01:40:09,134 --> 01:40:10,267
Zone Four.

2232
01:40:10,698 --> 01:40:11,901
(Shujitsu's blind spot is...)

2233
01:40:12,134 --> 01:40:14,567
(Zone 4, far away from the libero.)

2234
01:40:17,567 --> 01:40:19,033
Please, don't send it to the libero.

2235
01:40:19,034 --> 01:40:20,667
Please, don't send it to the libero.

2236
01:40:24,567 --> 01:40:25,501
She shouldn't have served...

2237
01:40:25,501 --> 01:40:26,434
to the libero again!

2238
01:40:26,901 --> 01:40:28,601
(The ball goes to the libero again...)

2239
01:40:30,001 --> 01:40:31,966
(and moves to Onishi without a hitch.)

2240
01:40:31,967 --> 01:40:33,134
A tip to the left!

2241
01:40:35,300 --> 01:40:36,233
Come on!

2242
01:40:36,268 --> 01:40:38,035
(Onishi pushes to the middle.)

2243
01:40:38,267 --> 01:40:40,034
Come on in!

2244
01:40:42,867 --> 01:40:46,034
Coach Kim's other strategies are working,

2245
01:40:46,667 --> 01:40:49,167
but the serve strategy keeps missing.

2246
01:40:49,667 --> 01:40:52,500
At this rate,
the ball will keep going to Onishi.

2247
01:40:52,501 --> 01:40:55,000
Be it spikes or tips,

2248
01:40:55,001 --> 01:40:56,800
she can do it all.

2249
01:40:56,801 --> 01:40:58,767
That tells you how composed she is.

2250
01:40:59,734 --> 01:41:02,967
(Nobody can stop her.)

2251
01:41:03,534 --> 01:41:06,401
(Now, she's serving.)

2252
01:41:06,834 --> 01:41:08,033
It's now 5 to 4.

2253
01:41:08,034 --> 01:41:09,434
Onishi Yukiji serves.

2254
01:41:09,934 --> 01:41:10,701
Young In,

2255
01:41:10,702 --> 01:41:13,101
count down for the block timing.

2256
01:41:13,401 --> 01:41:15,634
(The lead goes
to the opposing team again.)

2257
01:41:16,034 --> 01:41:20,067
(They must take back control.)

2258
01:41:23,301 --> 01:41:24,134
A strong serve.

2259
01:41:25,567 --> 01:41:26,766
(Received!)

2260
01:41:26,767 --> 01:41:28,401
That's it.

2261
01:41:29,467 --> 01:41:30,601
(They save the ball.)

2262
01:41:32,367 --> 01:41:33,767
A strong straight shot that's defended.

2263
01:41:33,934 --> 01:41:35,401
(But Shujitsu saves again.)

2264
01:41:35,967 --> 01:41:36,767
Yoshimoto swoops in!

2265
01:41:37,501 --> 01:41:38,567
Delay the block!

2266
01:41:40,034 --> 01:41:41,101
Think about the timing!

2267
01:41:44,067 --> 01:41:45,834
She rushes in, and it's blocked!

2268
01:41:47,134 --> 01:41:49,966
(Ho Bin's block gets a point!)

2269
01:41:49,967 --> 01:41:51,034
Nice!

2270
01:41:51,534 --> 01:41:53,567
That's it!

2271
01:41:54,834 --> 01:41:56,201
Let's look at Lee Ho Bin's block.

2272
01:41:56,801 --> 01:41:59,567
It's one move like this
that turns the game around.

2273
01:42:00,767 --> 01:42:02,234
Let's go!

2274
01:42:02,701 --> 01:42:03,934
That was nice.

2275
01:42:04,467 --> 01:42:05,900
Push down more when you jump.

2276
01:42:05,901 --> 01:42:06,867
That was nicely played.

2277
01:42:07,734 --> 01:42:09,533
(Second set, Shujitsu High 5
: Wonder Dogs 5)

2278
01:42:09,534 --> 01:42:11,567
We really have to take the lead here.

2279
01:42:13,034 --> 01:42:14,833
All they have to do is serve properly.

2280
01:42:14,834 --> 01:42:15,601
Here I go.

2281
01:42:21,067 --> 01:42:22,334
Bummer.

2282
01:42:24,101 --> 01:42:25,733
(Enkhsoyol misses the serve.)

2283
01:42:25,734 --> 01:42:27,601
Enkhsoyol,

2284
01:42:28,134 --> 01:42:29,533
it's okay if it goes out.

2285
01:42:29,534 --> 01:42:31,533
- Just hit it deep.
- Got it.

2286
01:42:31,534 --> 01:42:32,833
You can afford to hit it out.

2287
01:42:32,834 --> 01:42:34,533
Hit it deep.

2288
01:42:34,534 --> 01:42:37,066
(The serve strategy is not working.)

2289
01:42:37,067 --> 01:42:38,567
(Sighing)

2290
01:42:39,120 --> 01:42:40,941
(Every time they close the gap,)

2291
01:42:41,749 --> 01:42:43,984
(Shujitsu answers right back.)

2292
01:42:44,752 --> 01:42:47,087
(The Wonder Dogs fall behind again.)

2293
01:42:47,688 --> 01:42:49,455
(Ho Bin serves again.)

2294
01:42:50,057 --> 01:42:51,758
(Straight to the libero again)

2295
01:42:51,759 --> 01:42:53,393
Zone Four!

2296
01:42:53,894 --> 01:42:55,561
(Another solid pass by the libero...)

2297
01:42:56,297 --> 01:42:57,430
(sets Onishi up for an attack.)

2298
01:42:57,431 --> 01:42:58,231
There's an opening.

2299
01:42:59,033 --> 01:42:59,899
Off the block and out.

2300
01:43:00,534 --> 01:43:02,135
(Second set, Shujitsu High 8
: Wonder Dogs 6)

2301
01:43:02,703 --> 01:43:04,337
This is driving me nuts.

2302
01:43:05,973 --> 01:43:08,608
(The gap just won't close.)

2303
01:43:09,109 --> 01:43:11,577
It's the first technical timeout.

2304
01:43:12,880 --> 01:43:14,313
It's simple, guys.

2305
01:43:14,648 --> 01:43:15,948
Where should we serve?

2306
01:43:15,949 --> 01:43:17,817
- Away from the libero.
- Away from the libero!

2307
01:43:17,818 --> 01:43:20,420
Their libero's
reception success rate is...

2308
01:43:20,421 --> 01:43:21,420
over 60 percent.

2309
01:43:21,622 --> 01:43:23,355
- So stay away from the libero.
- Yes.

2310
01:43:23,356 --> 01:43:25,691
And when the ball gets past us, defend!

2311
01:43:25,692 --> 01:43:27,694
The libero is their best passer.

2312
01:43:27,695 --> 01:43:29,229
So serve away from her,

2313
01:43:29,230 --> 01:43:31,097
then be ready to defend and block.

2314
01:43:31,098 --> 01:43:32,365
- Yes, Coach!
- You understand?

2315
01:43:32,366 --> 01:43:34,267
Pick up anything that gets through.

2316
01:43:34,568 --> 01:43:35,535
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2317
01:43:35,536 --> 01:43:37,637
- We can do this!
- Got it.

2318
01:43:40,040 --> 01:43:42,074
(Kato Uta gets ready to serve.)

2319
01:43:42,676 --> 01:43:45,278
(Seven straight serves in the first set)

2320
01:43:45,480 --> 01:43:47,881
Move left. Keep your feet moving!

2321
01:43:52,353 --> 01:43:53,219
Mine!

2322
01:43:53,387 --> 01:43:54,721
A pinpoint pass by Enkhsoyol.

2323
01:43:57,491 --> 01:43:58,825
(Setting another trap for the blockers)

2324
01:43:58,826 --> 01:44:00,126
(They jump for it!)

2325
01:44:01,428 --> 01:44:02,662
(A 1-on-1 blocking opportunity)

2326
01:44:03,063 --> 01:44:04,363
Nice!

2327
01:44:04,765 --> 01:44:06,699
Chae Rim scores off the block!

2328
01:44:07,368 --> 01:44:08,301
(Experts at baiting blockers)

2329
01:44:08,302 --> 01:44:09,602
Nice!

2330
01:44:10,304 --> 01:44:12,171
(They really know their stuff.)

2331
01:44:12,172 --> 01:44:13,306
That's it!

2332
01:44:15,843 --> 01:44:17,444
You jump too early.

2333
01:44:17,945 --> 01:44:20,280
The ball keeps going off our hands!

2334
01:44:23,017 --> 01:44:24,518
(The Wonder Dogs finally get to serve.)

2335
01:44:24,519 --> 01:44:27,254
Easy, Young In. Think about your target.

2336
01:44:27,454 --> 01:44:28,320
Yes, Coach.

2337
01:44:30,491 --> 01:44:32,025
(Young In calmly surveys the court.)

2338
01:44:32,026 --> 01:44:33,727
(She's told them...)

2339
01:44:33,728 --> 01:44:35,462
(again and again...)

2340
01:44:35,463 --> 01:44:37,364
(exactly where to serve.)

2341
01:44:37,698 --> 01:44:39,966
(Now it's time to put it into action.)

2342
01:44:40,501 --> 01:44:41,768
Young In serves.

2343
01:44:41,902 --> 01:44:43,803
(The target area for the serve)

2344
01:44:45,005 --> 01:44:47,607
(Locked on target)

2345
01:44:47,708 --> 01:44:48,941
(The home crowd cheers in unison.)

2346
01:44:49,543 --> 01:44:50,576
(Let's go!)

2347
01:44:52,279 --> 01:44:53,879
There! That's the spot.

2348
01:44:55,716 --> 01:44:56,549
Okay, cover!

2349
01:44:56,717 --> 01:44:58,318
(The ball goes high.)

2350
01:44:58,319 --> 01:44:59,152
It's coming over!

2351
01:44:59,153 --> 01:45:00,687
(It's coming over.)

2352
01:45:03,023 --> 01:45:06,092
Chae Rim slams down the floater!

2353
01:45:07,795 --> 01:45:09,662
- Yes!
- That's what I'm talking about!

2354
01:45:09,997 --> 01:45:11,030
There you go!

2355
01:45:14,435 --> 01:45:15,802
(Right into the open space!)

2356
01:45:15,803 --> 01:45:17,237
Nice one!

2357
01:45:17,238 --> 01:45:20,907
Coach Kim has been calling for this.

2358
01:45:20,908 --> 01:45:22,042
And they finally pull it off.

2359
01:45:22,476 --> 01:45:25,511
They have to keep putting pressure
on Shujitsu with their serves.

2360
01:45:27,247 --> 01:45:28,180
It's 9 to 8.

2361
01:45:28,916 --> 01:45:30,183
Let's get another right away!

2362
01:45:30,184 --> 01:45:32,118
(The Wonder Dogs are fired up again.)

2363
01:45:32,119 --> 01:45:34,454
It's about the timing of the block.

2364
01:45:34,555 --> 01:45:37,090
(Yoshimoto steps up to serve.)

2365
01:45:37,691 --> 01:45:39,859
The serve is coming in slow.

2366
01:45:40,160 --> 01:45:42,294
Keep your feet moving.

2367
01:45:42,863 --> 01:45:45,465
Be ready. Cover!

2368
01:45:49,871 --> 01:45:50,803
Hey!

2369
01:45:54,808 --> 01:45:57,643
(The ball drops untouched.)

2370
01:45:58,512 --> 01:46:00,747
(Not a single player...)

2371
01:46:00,748 --> 01:46:02,782
(goes for the reception.)

2372
01:46:04,551 --> 01:46:05,451
It was in.

2373
01:46:10,090 --> 01:46:12,225
(The whole arena falls silent.)

2374
01:46:12,226 --> 01:46:13,826
Move!

2375
01:46:13,961 --> 01:46:15,528
It's a free ball! Hey!

2376
01:46:20,401 --> 01:46:21,368
Focus!

2377
01:46:21,369 --> 01:46:25,972
- What happened there?
- That's a costly mistake.

2378
01:46:26,940 --> 01:46:29,575
- That was...
- That's just unbelievable.

2379
01:46:29,576 --> 01:46:31,210
That serve came in so slowly.

2380
01:46:33,414 --> 01:46:35,081
It's a free ball! Hey!

2381
01:46:35,682 --> 01:46:39,119
(The reception calls break down.)

2382
01:46:39,120 --> 01:46:40,152
That was such an easy ball.

2383
01:46:43,391 --> 01:46:45,091
Enkhsoyol.

2384
01:46:45,338 --> 01:46:46,605
What are you doing? That was yours.

2385
01:46:48,896 --> 01:46:50,096
My bad.

2386
01:46:51,265 --> 01:46:54,300
(Coach Kim is speechless.)

2387
01:46:55,302 --> 01:46:57,803
I definitely made a lot of errors.

2388
01:46:57,905 --> 01:47:01,541
I was so nervous that I let
a lot of balls get away from me.

2389
01:47:01,542 --> 01:47:03,343
I was really disappointed in myself.

2390
01:47:03,344 --> 01:47:06,446
I told myself every set I got...

2391
01:47:06,447 --> 01:47:08,648
had to be a point.

2392
01:47:09,116 --> 01:47:10,516
So I made up my mind...

2393
01:47:10,517 --> 01:47:12,618
to give it everything I had.

2394
01:47:16,123 --> 01:47:17,190
It's okay.

2395
01:47:18,058 --> 01:47:19,759
(The serve finds Zone Four.)

2396
01:47:20,060 --> 01:47:20,860
(A hurried tip)

2397
01:47:20,861 --> 01:47:21,661
She can't get a clean hit.

2398
01:47:23,797 --> 01:47:24,764
The Wonder Dogs.

2399
01:47:24,765 --> 01:47:26,098
(They have a chance.)

2400
01:47:26,500 --> 01:47:27,433
Enkhsoyol.

2401
01:47:27,434 --> 01:47:28,534
(Enkhsoyol takes flight.)

2402
01:47:28,535 --> 01:47:30,103
Send it deep.

2403
01:47:34,541 --> 01:47:36,976
(Enkhsoyol commits an attack error.)

2404
01:47:36,977 --> 01:47:39,912
The errors just keep coming.

2405
01:47:39,913 --> 01:47:42,280
Errors at a time like this...

2406
01:47:42,281 --> 01:47:43,716
make it so much harder to fight back.

2407
01:47:43,717 --> 01:47:46,419
(Back-to-back errors blow their chances
to take the lead.)

2408
01:47:46,720 --> 01:47:47,920
(The match continues.)

2409
01:47:47,921 --> 01:47:48,854
Mine!

2410
01:47:49,756 --> 01:47:50,723
Set a C!

2411
01:47:51,024 --> 01:47:51,957
Set a C!

2412
01:47:51,958 --> 01:47:53,125
(A set to the left)

2413
01:47:54,061 --> 01:47:55,395
That set is short.

2414
01:47:55,596 --> 01:47:56,696
Hyo Rim!

2415
01:47:57,764 --> 01:48:00,532
(They can only send it back over.)

2416
01:48:00,801 --> 01:48:02,201
Set it left.

2417
01:48:02,436 --> 01:48:04,404
(The ball goes straight to Onishi.)

2418
01:48:05,439 --> 01:48:08,241
(Onishi spots the opening instantly.)

2419
01:48:08,408 --> 01:48:11,443
We're throwing away too many points!

2420
01:48:13,080 --> 01:48:15,448
Let's go!

2421
01:48:16,783 --> 01:48:17,716
A clean reception.

2422
01:48:18,051 --> 01:48:18,984
A second-ball set to the left.

2423
01:48:19,653 --> 01:48:20,586
Onishi.

2424
01:48:21,688 --> 01:48:23,722
(Only one blocker in front of her?)

2425
01:48:25,125 --> 01:48:27,661
(Second set, Shujitsu High 13
: Wonder Dogs 10)

2426
01:48:27,662 --> 01:48:28,995
It's a high ball,

2427
01:48:29,229 --> 01:48:31,163
but Hyo Rim goes up alone.

2428
01:48:32,667 --> 01:48:34,701
She jumps, and you just stand there!

2429
01:48:34,768 --> 01:48:36,502
You leave her to block alone again!

2430
01:48:37,838 --> 01:48:38,671
Sorry.

2431
01:48:39,506 --> 01:48:42,041
The gap keeps growing.

2432
01:48:43,877 --> 01:48:46,313
(And now a reception error)

2433
01:48:46,314 --> 01:48:48,114
And it's a service ace.

2434
01:48:51,251 --> 01:48:55,254
There are too many errors
from the Wonder Dogs.

2435
01:48:55,255 --> 01:48:56,855
(The lead is now four points.)

2436
01:48:58,325 --> 01:48:59,592
Why are they so frazzled?

2437
01:48:59,927 --> 01:49:02,161
They're nervous and completely lost.

2438
01:49:02,162 --> 01:49:03,496
They can't even hear us calling.

2439
01:49:05,833 --> 01:49:08,234
- Chae Rim.
- Chae Rim!

2440
01:49:08,802 --> 01:49:09,735
(She doesn't hear them.)

2441
01:49:09,736 --> 01:49:11,637
- Was that a serve out?
- Chae Rim!

2442
01:49:11,638 --> 01:49:14,573
It was in. Move your feet!

2443
01:49:14,574 --> 01:49:16,308
- Yes, Coach.
- It was in. Stay on your toes!

2444
01:49:17,611 --> 01:49:19,278
Even Chae Rim is out of it.

2445
01:49:20,681 --> 01:49:22,015
Hyo Rim!

2446
01:49:22,282 --> 01:49:24,316
- A short serve right at you!
- Hyo Rim, over there!

2447
01:49:24,317 --> 01:49:25,718
Hyo Rim! Enkhsoyol!

2448
01:49:27,020 --> 01:49:28,887
This is maddening.

2449
01:49:28,888 --> 01:49:29,688
(She doesn't hear them.)

2450
01:49:32,893 --> 01:49:33,826
Something was wrong.

2451
01:49:36,096 --> 01:49:38,531
I was trying to communicate with them,

2452
01:49:38,765 --> 01:49:40,366
so I called out to Chae Rim.

2453
01:49:41,201 --> 01:49:42,067
She looked my way,

2454
01:49:42,936 --> 01:49:46,071
but it felt like she was
looking straight through me.

2455
01:49:49,209 --> 01:49:50,409
And when we called out to them...

2456
01:49:50,577 --> 01:49:51,477
Young In!

2457
01:49:52,046 --> 01:49:54,747
They never even turned around.
They just stared into space.

2458
01:49:56,183 --> 01:49:58,017
I had no idea what was happening.

2459
01:49:59,786 --> 01:50:01,887
We were making so many unusual mistakes,

2460
01:50:02,489 --> 01:50:03,756
and I think it caught me off guard.

2461
01:50:03,757 --> 01:50:04,624
It's out.

2462
01:50:04,625 --> 01:50:08,094
(Second set, Shujitsu High 15
: Wonder Dogs 10)

2463
01:50:08,362 --> 01:50:11,998
Any wider, and it's like the first set
all over again.

2464
01:50:11,999 --> 01:50:12,966
Exactly.

2465
01:50:16,870 --> 01:50:18,037
They're making a lot of mistakes.

2466
01:50:18,038 --> 01:50:18,704
Yes.

2467
01:50:19,606 --> 01:50:23,976
We weren't executing
any of what we'd practiced.

2468
01:50:26,019 --> 01:50:27,780
I'd never been in this situation before.

2469
01:50:29,082 --> 01:50:30,315
It was so frustrating.

2470
01:50:31,952 --> 01:50:33,953
What could I do? Yell at them?

2471
01:50:35,589 --> 01:50:38,624
I was getting angrier by the minute.

2472
01:50:39,426 --> 01:50:40,994
Let's speed things up!

2473
01:50:40,995 --> 01:50:42,194
Then,

2474
01:50:42,629 --> 01:50:44,496
I decided to try something different.

2475
01:50:52,072 --> 01:50:53,706
It's okay, everyone.

2476
01:50:53,874 --> 01:50:55,741
It's okay, everyone.

2477
01:50:57,111 --> 01:51:01,446
Relax. It's okay. You can do it.

2478
01:51:02,021 --> 01:51:02,948
Nothing was okay,

2479
01:51:03,250 --> 01:51:06,652
but I kept telling them it was,
and that they were doing well.

2480
01:51:06,720 --> 01:51:08,020
It's okay. You can do this.

2481
01:51:08,021 --> 01:51:09,923
Don't worry. You've got this.

2482
01:51:09,924 --> 01:51:11,057
- Yes, Coach.
- It's okay.

2483
01:51:11,058 --> 01:51:12,124
Yes, Coach.

2484
01:51:12,125 --> 01:51:13,759
We have to make it happen.

2485
01:51:14,061 --> 01:51:18,531
I'm not really one for giving pep talks.

2486
01:51:20,100 --> 01:51:21,801
It's okay.

2487
01:51:21,802 --> 01:51:23,369
(Coach Kim turns to encouragement.)

2488
01:51:23,370 --> 01:51:27,973
I knew yelling at them would
only make them more withdrawn.

2489
01:51:28,909 --> 01:51:30,009
Man, this is rough.

2490
01:51:32,045 --> 01:51:33,045
It's blocked.

2491
01:51:33,613 --> 01:51:34,513
No!

2492
01:51:35,082 --> 01:51:36,015
Hey!

2493
01:51:37,050 --> 01:51:38,484
I was furious.

2494
01:51:39,019 --> 01:51:42,121
You're okay. Keep going.

2495
01:51:43,490 --> 01:51:45,057
But I kept a lid on it.

2496
01:51:46,727 --> 01:51:48,561
Even when they were struggling...

2497
01:51:48,562 --> 01:51:50,730
Enkhsoyol, nice job!

2498
01:51:50,731 --> 01:51:52,799
I tried to build them up with praise.

2499
01:51:52,800 --> 01:51:55,234
- Send it deep.
- I'll go deep. My bad.

2500
01:51:58,605 --> 01:51:59,605
A back-row attack up the middle.

2501
01:52:00,874 --> 01:52:02,141
And it drops in.

2502
01:52:08,515 --> 01:52:11,650
You can do it. I know you can!

2503
01:52:12,152 --> 01:52:13,152
Enkhsoyol!

2504
01:52:13,153 --> 01:52:15,321
Enkhsoyol, hit over the block.

2505
01:52:15,655 --> 01:52:16,588
Through the middle!

2506
01:52:19,359 --> 01:52:20,659
And it drops in again.

2507
01:52:20,660 --> 01:52:21,694
(Another point conceded)

2508
01:52:21,695 --> 01:52:23,162
- Oh, gosh.
- Hey!

2509
01:52:23,730 --> 01:52:26,031
No more mistakes!

2510
01:52:26,166 --> 01:52:27,999
Stay calm!

2511
01:52:28,000 --> 01:52:29,535
Another point handed to Shujitsu.

2512
01:52:29,536 --> 01:52:31,370
(Second set, Shujitsu High 18
: Wonder Dogs 10)

2513
01:52:32,439 --> 01:52:33,272
Mine!

2514
01:52:34,541 --> 01:52:36,242
It's a service ace.

2515
01:52:36,243 --> 01:52:38,611
That's way too many errors.

2516
01:52:38,612 --> 01:52:40,612
Come on! Just hit it!

2517
01:52:42,803 --> 01:52:44,978
That was an open ball, but they messed up.

2518
01:52:46,073 --> 01:52:48,207
Nice!

2519
01:52:49,763 --> 01:52:52,698
The gap was small,
but they still look rattled.

2520
01:52:52,699 --> 01:52:53,532
Right.

2521
01:52:53,533 --> 01:52:56,369
(Shujitsu High 19 : Wonder Dogs 10)

2522
01:52:56,737 --> 01:52:59,305
(Second set, Shujitsu High 20
: Wonder Dogs 10)

2523
01:52:59,306 --> 01:53:00,406
It was a real crisis.

2524
01:53:02,509 --> 01:53:04,643
Looking at their eyes...

2525
01:53:05,478 --> 01:53:08,280
and the way they were moving,

2526
01:53:08,582 --> 01:53:12,118
I realized that they were in a state
where nothing I said would get through.

2527
01:53:12,854 --> 01:53:15,488
Seung Ju's absence felt
especially significant...

2528
01:53:16,057 --> 01:53:19,592
when it came to keeping
the players together...

2529
01:53:19,794 --> 01:53:24,497
and communicating on the court.

2530
01:53:25,132 --> 01:53:26,999
Once this moment passes,
you won't get another chance.

2531
01:53:28,869 --> 01:53:30,169
What should we do now?

2532
01:53:30,837 --> 01:53:32,404
Don't panic. You're okay.

2533
01:53:32,405 --> 01:53:35,795
(The on-court anchor
who held the team together)

2534
01:53:37,511 --> 01:53:38,511
You need...

2535
01:53:40,047 --> 01:53:41,948
a player like that...

2536
01:53:42,883 --> 01:53:43,783
on the court.

2537
01:53:45,786 --> 01:53:47,253
- Yeon Joo!
- Yeon Joo!

2538
01:53:48,889 --> 01:53:50,890
The Wonder Dogs make a substitution.

2539
01:53:50,891 --> 01:53:53,593
(Yoon Young In out, Hwang Yeon Joo in)

2540
01:53:53,760 --> 01:53:56,995
Yeon Joo has a lot of experience,

2541
01:53:58,432 --> 01:54:01,868
so I thought she could bring
a little more stability in that regard.

2542
01:54:06,907 --> 01:54:10,142
Honestly, I believed that if our players
could just regain their composure...

2543
01:54:10,711 --> 01:54:13,446
and start playing their own game,

2544
01:54:13,447 --> 01:54:17,483
we could definitely win.

2545
01:54:18,518 --> 01:54:20,119
We were down by quite a few points,
but I still felt...

2546
01:54:20,455 --> 01:54:23,489
that if we just executed what we could,
we could come back and win.

2547
01:54:24,291 --> 01:54:26,359
And because their block was shifting...

2548
01:54:26,661 --> 01:54:30,329
heavily toward our left side,

2549
01:54:31,198 --> 01:54:35,468
I brought Yeon Joo in
to make better use...

2550
01:54:35,535 --> 01:54:39,438
of our opposite attack on the right.

2551
01:54:39,439 --> 01:54:40,672
(The Wonder Coach's bold move)

2552
01:54:41,576 --> 01:54:42,541
I was really worried.

2553
01:54:43,744 --> 01:54:45,310
I wasn't
in good physical condition at all,

2554
01:54:45,311 --> 01:54:48,781
and I did feel a lot of pressure.

2555
01:54:49,616 --> 01:54:51,483
(Even during training)

2556
01:54:51,484 --> 01:54:52,418
Sorry.

2557
01:54:53,053 --> 01:54:54,020
Sorry.

2558
01:54:54,021 --> 01:54:54,987
(Yeon Joo had been worried...)

2559
01:54:54,988 --> 01:54:56,922
I can't do anything. This is killing me.

2560
01:54:56,923 --> 01:54:58,391
(about her condition
after a long time off.)

2561
01:54:59,860 --> 01:55:01,627
But more than any of that,

2562
01:55:02,195 --> 01:55:03,629
we were down by so many points...

2563
01:55:04,931 --> 01:55:07,733
that I figured the coach must have been
expecting something from me.

2564
01:55:09,804 --> 01:55:13,606
So I went in thinking, "Even if my leg
tears apart, we have to win."

2565
01:55:14,075 --> 01:55:16,809
Guys, it's okay. Just stay focused.

2566
01:55:18,378 --> 01:55:21,046
- Let's slow things down, okay?
- Okay!

2567
01:55:21,047 --> 01:55:22,247
Settle down a bit.

2568
01:55:22,248 --> 01:55:23,549
Hyo Rim!

2569
01:55:23,951 --> 01:55:26,218
To the right!

2570
01:55:26,753 --> 01:55:27,753
Got it.

2571
01:55:28,321 --> 01:55:29,588
You can set it just like you did
for Young In.

2572
01:55:29,589 --> 01:55:30,789
Okay.

2573
01:55:30,790 --> 01:55:31,924
Take your time!

2574
01:55:35,562 --> 01:55:37,596
(Min Kyeong's serve)

2575
01:55:40,100 --> 01:55:41,901
(She calls for a targeted serve.)

2576
01:55:41,902 --> 01:55:44,570
(The designated serve target zone)

2577
01:55:49,810 --> 01:55:51,010
The reception is shaky.

2578
01:55:51,278 --> 01:55:53,279
It's a free ball!

2579
01:55:54,981 --> 01:55:56,148
They have to send it over.

2580
01:55:56,149 --> 01:55:57,149
Free ball!

2581
01:55:57,551 --> 01:55:59,619
- To the middle!
- Go!

2582
01:56:01,387 --> 01:56:02,688
Where is Hyo Rim setting it?

2583
01:56:02,823 --> 01:56:03,689
Hit it!

2584
01:56:07,327 --> 01:56:09,628
(This time, the set goes to the right!)

2585
01:56:13,300 --> 01:56:14,200
Hit it!

2586
01:56:14,401 --> 01:56:15,334
Yeon Joo!

2587
01:56:15,735 --> 01:56:16,935
That's it!

2588
01:56:17,804 --> 01:56:18,937
Bravo!

2589
01:56:21,208 --> 01:56:24,043
(Finally, they break through!)

2590
01:56:24,044 --> 01:56:26,045
(Yeon Joo's family)

2591
01:56:26,347 --> 01:56:28,080
Welcome to the Wonder Dogs!

2592
01:56:28,748 --> 01:56:31,616
The legend takes the point.

2593
01:56:31,617 --> 01:56:33,151
(Her first point since returning)

2594
01:56:33,453 --> 01:56:34,520
Mine!

2595
01:56:34,621 --> 01:56:36,355
- To the middle!
- Go!

2596
01:56:37,057 --> 01:56:38,591
Follow her!

2597
01:56:38,925 --> 01:56:39,858
Hit it!

2598
01:56:40,760 --> 01:56:43,095
(The opposing blockers completely take
the bait.)

2599
01:56:46,099 --> 01:56:48,967
She's using her veteran savvy
to put the ball away.

2600
01:56:50,804 --> 01:56:53,975
They haven't been able to score
from the right side at all until now.

2601
01:56:53,976 --> 01:56:55,274
- They finish it perfectly.
- Right.

2602
01:56:55,275 --> 01:56:56,208
(A clean kill from Yeon Joo)

2603
01:57:01,207 --> 01:57:04,016
(In fact, Shujitsu...)

2604
01:57:05,285 --> 01:57:07,353
Against the opposite, you only need
to put up a single block.

2605
01:57:07,354 --> 01:57:08,487
Their opposite side hasn't...

2606
01:57:08,488 --> 01:57:10,756
really been hurting us.

2607
01:57:10,757 --> 01:57:13,926
There's no need for the block to commit
all the way over on the opposite.

2608
01:57:14,694 --> 01:57:17,896
(Coach Nishihata weakens the block
against the opposite side.)

2609
01:57:17,897 --> 01:57:21,200
(Coach Kim strengthens
the opposite attack.)

2610
01:57:22,335 --> 01:57:23,669
- Good.
- Was it too long?

2611
01:57:23,670 --> 01:57:25,504
No. Just keep setting it
the way you have been.

2612
01:57:25,839 --> 01:57:27,807
Don't aim over there. Just cut it.

2613
01:57:28,542 --> 01:57:30,409
- You can set it just a little higher.
- Okay.

2614
01:57:32,479 --> 01:57:35,214
- Let's win!
- Let's go! Take it slow!

2615
01:57:35,849 --> 01:57:38,584
Yeon Joo has a lot of experience,

2616
01:57:38,952 --> 01:57:42,454
so she's good at handling difficult balls.

2617
01:57:42,756 --> 01:57:44,790
I think that was a huge help.

2618
01:57:45,725 --> 01:57:47,457
Focus!

2619
01:57:47,458 --> 01:57:49,127
Keep it going!

2620
01:57:49,296 --> 01:57:52,798
It's okay! Just do it! Let's go for it.

2621
01:57:55,802 --> 01:57:57,102
To the right side.

2622
01:57:58,405 --> 01:57:59,271
Mine!

2623
01:57:59,339 --> 01:58:00,306
She receives it well.

2624
01:58:00,840 --> 01:58:01,840
To the right again.

2625
01:58:02,676 --> 01:58:03,843
They're going right again!

2626
01:58:03,844 --> 01:58:05,344
That's it!

2627
01:58:06,079 --> 01:58:07,880
(We won't be fooled this time!)

2628
01:58:08,748 --> 01:58:09,815
Here she comes!

2629
01:58:13,053 --> 01:58:13,953
Yeon Joo!

2630
01:58:14,521 --> 01:58:15,588
They keep it alive with the defense.

2631
01:58:15,589 --> 01:58:16,455
(An iron defense)

2632
01:58:17,023 --> 01:58:19,658
(Shujitsu immediately counterattacks.)

2633
01:58:20,293 --> 01:58:21,326
One-on-one!

2634
01:58:30,604 --> 01:58:34,307
Yeon Joo blocks!

2635
01:58:35,809 --> 01:58:36,876
Good.

2636
01:58:37,278 --> 01:58:38,644
- Nice!
- Well done!

2637
01:58:43,149 --> 01:58:46,283
- Hwang Yeon Joo!
- Hwang Yeon Joo!

2638
01:58:46,284 --> 01:58:49,154
Bringing in Yeon Joo is changing
the momentum of the match.

2639
01:58:50,991 --> 01:58:51,991
Block the opening.

2640
01:58:54,094 --> 01:58:56,395
- Chae Rim, defend the cross-court shot.
- Yes.

2641
01:58:58,164 --> 01:59:00,132
Girls, keep fighting until the very end!

2642
01:59:00,534 --> 01:59:03,436
- Keep it going!
- Let's go!

2643
01:59:04,237 --> 01:59:08,473
I started thinking,
"The players are going to rely on me."

2644
01:59:10,010 --> 01:59:11,009
And I wanted...

2645
01:59:11,578 --> 01:59:12,578
to win so badly.

2646
01:59:14,914 --> 01:59:15,780
"We got it."

2647
01:59:16,683 --> 01:59:18,317
I think that's when I really found
my confidence.

2648
01:59:19,285 --> 01:59:20,952
Their right-side hitter...

2649
01:59:22,088 --> 01:59:25,791
We started making mistakes...

2650
01:59:25,792 --> 01:59:28,193
and getting rattled.

2651
01:59:28,194 --> 01:59:31,063
(The Wonder Coach 2)

2652
01:59:31,998 --> 01:59:33,632
Spike!

2653
01:59:33,699 --> 01:59:34,761
Yeon Joo!

2654
01:59:34,834 --> 01:59:36,949
(Veteran Yeon Joo)

2655
01:59:38,405 --> 01:59:41,941
(She returns to the court!)

2656
01:59:42,209 --> 01:59:44,811
(Now it's time to fight back!)

2657
01:59:45,579 --> 01:59:46,712
Hit it!

2658
01:59:46,713 --> 01:59:48,181
Enkhsoyol!

2659
01:59:48,916 --> 01:59:51,351
(Their A-game is back.)

2660
01:59:51,685 --> 01:59:53,306
She chases and saves it!

2661
01:59:53,307 --> 01:59:55,655
(Even Japan's top team is reeling...)

2662
01:59:55,936 --> 01:59:58,024
(from the stronger strategy.)

2663
01:59:58,282 --> 02:00:02,081
(Dizzy)

2664
02:00:04,465 --> 02:00:07,833
(It's time to wake up from the nightmare!)

2665
02:00:09,537 --> 02:00:11,471
(Their revenge starts now.)

2666
02:00:11,472 --> 02:00:14,541
(Let's go!)

2667
02:00:15,009 --> 02:00:16,409
Wonder Dogs!

2668
02:00:16,510 --> 02:00:18,144
They've taken the lead!

2669
02:00:18,145 --> 02:00:20,380
That's it! Bravo!

2670
02:00:21,241 --> 02:00:22,500
(The Wonder Coach 2)

2671
